INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(1,1,'Identity','Who.Who.Who','Mateship',0.7,0.4,'FAIL','**(Who.Who.Who) Mateship (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "A type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Mateship: The greatest pleasure I have ever known is when my eyes meet the eyes of a mate over the top of two foaming glasses of beer. -- Mateship is universally cited as the defining value of the Australian character, transcending mere friendship to become a rigid code of mutual loyalty and non-pretension. It originated in the harsh, unforgiving conditions of the colonial bush where reliance on one’s fellows was a matter of survival, not preference. To violate this code—to "bludge" or "dob"—was to sentence oneself to social death in a land where isolation meant physical death.','Plane_1_Identity.md',41,'A type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(2,1,'Identity','Who.Who.What','The Larrikin',0.5,0.6,'HIT','**(Who.Who.What) The Larrikin (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "I won the seat of Oxley largely on an issue that has resulted in me being called a racist. That issue related to my comment that Aboriginals received more benefits than non-Aboriginals." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Larrikin: It takes eight or eleven of the biggest mud crushers in Melbourne to take one poor little half starved larrakin to a watch house. -- The Larrikin is the rowdy, anti-authoritarian trickster figure who refuses to be tamed by the civilizing forces of purely polite society. Originally a pejorative term used by the police for urban hooligans (as used by Kelly himself to describe his kin), it evolved into a badge of honor for the irreverent rogue who mocks pretension. The Larrikin refuses to take authority seriously, acting as a permanent check on hubris and the "stiff upper lip" of the establishment.','Plane_1_Identity.md',63,'I won the seat of Oxley largely on an issue that has resulted in me being called a racist. That issue related to my comment that Aboriginals received more benefits than non-Aboriginals.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I won the seat of Oxley largely on an issue that has resulted in me being called a racist.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(3,1,'Identity','Who.Who.Where','The Battler',0.6,-0.3,'HIT','**(Who.Who.Where) The Battler (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "I come here not as a polished politician but as a woman who has had her fair share of life''s knocks." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Battler: We fight it down, and we live it down, or we bear it bravely well, But the best men die of a broken heart for the things they cannot tell. -- Henry Lawson, the poet laureate of the Australian struggling class, captured the true cost of battling in these lines. The Battler is not merely someone who persists through hardship—they are marked by it, carrying invisible wounds that cannot be shared. Unlike the American "Striver" who seeks transcendence through victory, the Australian Battler finds dignity in endurance itself. The suffering is not a path to somewhere else; it is the substance of a worthy life.','Plane_1_Identity.md',85,'I come here not as a polished politician but as a woman who has had her fair share of life''s knocks.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I come here not as a polished politician but as a woman who has had her fair share of life''s knocks.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(4,1,'Identity','Who.Who.Why','The Anzac',0.5,0.8,'HIT','**(Who.Who.Why) The Anzac (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.8): HIT.** **Quote:** "My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem; watching our athletes compete on the world stage, proud to salute the Australian flag being raised to honour them as they took their place on podiums. It is about belonging, respect and commitment to fight for Australia." -Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','The Anzac: Anzac stood, and still stands, for reckless valor in a good cause, for enterprise, resourcefulness, fidelity, comradeship, and endurance that will never own defeat. -- The Anzac (Australian and New Zealand Army Corps) legend is the secular creation myth of the nation, forged in the blood of the failed Gallipoli campaign. It posits that the true Australian character was revealed, not created, in the fires of war—defined not by victory (for Gallipoli was a military defeat) but by the stoic manner of the conduct. It cemented the idea that the Australian soldier was a natural warrior, born of the bush and unbound by the rigid discipline of the British parade ground.','Plane_1_Identity.md',107,'My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem; watching our athletes compete on the world stage, proud to salute the Australian flag being raised to honour them as they took their place on podiums. It is about belonging, respect and commitment to fight for Australia.',1,'Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem; watching our athletes compete on the world stage, proud to salute the Australian flag being raised to honour them as they took their place on podiums.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(5,1,'Identity','Who.Who.How','Stringybark and Greenhide',0.6,0.7,'HIT','**(Who.Who.How) Stringybark and Greenhide (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "I may be only ''a fish and chip shop lady'', but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world. I would not even let one of them handle my grocery shopping." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Stringybark and Greenhide: Stringy-bark and Green-hide, that will never fail yer! Stringy-bark and Green-hide are the mainstay of Australia. -- Often summarized later as "making do," this phrasing refers to the colonial talent for solving complex problems with simple, crude materials (bark and raw hide). It is a method born of extreme isolation, where the settler could not buy a fix from a shop but had to invent one from the landscape itself. It celebrates the rough, ugly, but functional solution over the polished, expensive imported one.','Plane_1_Identity.md',129,'I may be only ''a fish and chip shop lady'', but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world. I would not even let one of them handle my grocery shopping.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I may be only ''a fish and chip shop lady'', but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(6,1,'Identity','Who.Who.Cause','The Indigenous Custodian',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Who.Who.Cause) The Indigenous Custodian (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.'' Well, where the hell do I go? I was born here, and so were my parents and children. I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Indigenous Custodian: We ask for justice, not for charity. -- William Cooper, a Yorta Yorta elder, spent years collecting nearly 2,000 signatures from Aboriginal Australians petitioning King George V for representation in Parliament. Though the Australian Commonwealth refused to forward the petition, Cooper''s words cut through the paternalism of the era with devastating clarity: this was not a request for handouts but a demand for rights. His grandson would later present the petition to Queen Elizabeth II in 2014, completing the journey.','Plane_1_Identity.md',151,'I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.'' Well, where the hell do I go? I was born here, and so were my parents and children. I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(7,1,'Identity','Who.Who.Effect','The Forgotten People',0.5,-0.4,'HIT','**(Who.Who.Effect) The Forgotten People (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "For far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Forgotten People: But what really happens to us will depend on how many people we have who are of the great and sober and dynamic middle-class – the strivers, the planners, the ambitious ones. -- Robert Menzies addressed the middle class—neither the organized labor unions nor the rich capitalists—as the moral and economic center of the nation. This group, often silent, upholds the stability, pays the taxes, and maintains the quiet order of suburban life. They are the target of all modern politics, the "Quiet Australians" who determine the fate of the government.','Plane_1_Identity.md',173,'For far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Immigration and multiculturalism are issues that this government is trying to address, but for far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(8,1,'Identity','Who.What.Who','The Fair Go',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Who.What.Who) The Fair Go (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I do not believe that the colour of one''s skin determines whether you are disadvantaged." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Fair Go: I cannot think of any other standard appropriate than the normal needs of the average employee, regarded as a human being living in a civilized community. -- The Fair Go is the central pillar of Australian moral philosophy, explicitly codified in law by the Harvester Judgement which set the world''s first living wage. It posits that economic efficiency cannot override human dignity, and that every citizen is entitled to a "fair suck of the sauce bottle." It implies that the game shouldn''t be rigged by privilege and that the underdog deserves a living chance to compete.','Plane_1_Identity.md',195,'I do not believe that the colour of one''s skin determines whether you are disadvantaged.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I do not believe that the colour of one''s skin determines whether you are disadvantaged.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(9,1,'Identity','Who.What.What','Tall Poppy Syndrome',0.4,-0.5,'HIT','**(Who.What.What) Tall Poppy Syndrome (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders. They screamed the loudest because they stand to lose the most -- their power, money and position, all funded by ordinary Australian taxpayers." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Tall Poppy Syndrome: A man''s a man for a'' that. -- The Burns poem "For A'' That and A'' That" became an anthem of colonial Australian egalitarianism, quoted by figures like Rev. John Dunmore Lang to assert that rank, title, and wealth do not make a man—only character does. The "Tall Poppy" who rises through pretension rather than merit is cut down not from envy but from this Burns-ian principle: your gold lace and ribbons mean nothing if you lack the honest worth within.','Plane_1_Identity.md',217,'In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders. They screamed the loudest because they stand to lose the most',1,'- their power, money and position, all funded by ordinary Australian taxpayers." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(10,1,'Identity','Who.What.Where','Egalitarianism',0.8,0.3,'FAIL','**(Who.What.Where) Egalitarianism (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "All I ask of people is come here, respect our country, respect our laws, our culture, our way of life. Be Australian, join us, enjoy this beautiful country and everything that it has to offer." -Enough Rope, ABC Television (2004)[^enoughrope04]','Egalitarianism: Jack is as good as his master, if not a good deal better. -- A fierce rejection of the British class system imported by the officers, asserting that shared humanity trumps titled status. While wealth inequality exists, social pretension is lethal; the Prime Minister is expected to sit in the front seat of the taxi. Respect is granted to the person based on their conduct, not their title or lineage.','Plane_1_Identity.md',237,'All I ask of people is come here, respect our country, respect our laws, our culture, our way of life. Be Australian, join us, enjoy this beautiful country and everything that it has to offer.',1,'Enough Rope, ABC Television (2004)','enoughrope04','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/enoughrope04.txt','verified',1.0,'3:563 minutes, 56 secondsrespect our country respect our laws our culture our way of life be Australian join us enjoy this beautiful country and',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(11,1,'Identity','Who.What.Why','"She''ll be right"',0.3,-0.6,'FAIL','**(Who.What.Why) "She''ll be right" (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I believe we are in danger of being swamped by Asians. Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin. They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','"She''ll be right": She''ll be right, mate. -- An idiom expressing the deep-seated belief that whatever the problem, it will eventually sort itself out with enough time and minimal fuss. It can be seen as optimistic resilience in the face of disaster ("She''ll be right, the house might burn plan") or lazy apathy ("Don''t worry about the leak"). It reflects a refusal to panic and a trust in the underlying stability of things.','Plane_1_Identity.md',259,'I believe we are in danger of being swamped by Asians. Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin. They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(12,1,'Identity','Who.What.How','Secular Skepticism',0.6,-0.3,'FAIL','**(Who.What.How) Secular Skepticism (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I saw the fools on the opposition benches pander to minorities without realizing the implications of creeping Islamic fundamentalism in our society." -Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)[^senate18prot]','Secular Skepticism: The typical Australian... was seldom religious in the sense in which the word is generally used. -- Australia is one of the most secular nations on earth, deeply suspicious of "wowsers" (moralizers), "Bible-bashers," and anyone claiming a monopoly on truth. The skepticism extends to politicians, bosses, and grand ideologies, creating a culture where "Bullshit Detection" is a primary survival skill.','Plane_1_Identity.md',281,'I saw the fools on the opposition benches pander to minorities without realizing the implications of creeping Islamic fundamentalism in our society.',1,'Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)','senate18prot','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18prot.txt','verified',1.0,'I saw the fools on the opposition benches pander to minorities without realizing the implications of creeping Islamic fundamentalism in our society.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(13,1,'Identity','Who.What.Cause','The Convict Stain',0.3,-0.5,'HIT','**(Who.What.Cause) The Convict Stain (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Convict Stain: The birthstain. -- The shame of convict origins haunted early Australia for a century, defining the population as the "rejects" of Britain. In the late 20th century, it was reclaimed as a badge of honor, but the "Stain" embedded a deep anti-authoritarian streak—the ancestors were "victims" of the system, not the architects.','Plane_1_Identity.md',303,'Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(14,1,'Identity','Who.What.Effect','The Commonwealth',0.8,0.5,'FAIL','**(Who.What.Effect) The Commonwealth (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Immigration must be halted in the short term so that our dole queues are not added to by, in many cases, unskilled migrants not fluent in the English language." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Commonwealth: Government for the common good. -- The choice of "Commonwealth" (Common-Weal) over "Dominion" or "Kingdom" signals a conscious commitment to the public good as the ultimate end of the state. It implies a shared wealth and a mutual obligation to look after the whole, rather than serving a monarch or an aristocracy.','Plane_1_Identity.md',323,'Immigration must be halted in the short term so that our dole queues are not added to by, in many cases, unskilled migrants not fluent in the English language.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Immigration must be halted in the short term so that our dole queues are not added to by, in many cases, unskilled migrants not fluent in the English language.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(15,1,'Identity','Who.Where.Who','The Bush',0.5,-0.4,'HIT','**(Who.Where.Who) The Bush (υ: +0.5, ψ: -0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "We have cane farmers across Queensland, who want a code of conduct. Nothing else—no money, just surety for their industry, which employs tens of thousands of Australian workers and pumps $2 billion in cash through this economy." -Sugar Industry Code of Conduct Disallowance Debate, Senate Hansard (2017)[^senate17sugar]','The Bush: I love a sunburnt country, a land of sweeping plains, / Of ragged mountain ranges, of droughts and flooding rains. -- The Bush is the mythic heart of Australia, holding a religious significance despite most Australians living in coastal cities. It is a landscape of extremes—terror and beauty—that demands respect and submission from those who enter it. It is the "Real Australia" in the cultural imagination, the place where the national character is tested and purified by fire and flood.','Plane_1_Identity.md',347,'We have cane farmers across Queensland, who want a code of conduct. Nothing else—no money, just surety for their industry, which employs tens of thousands of Australian workers and pumps $2 billion in cash through this economy.',1,'Sugar Industry Code of Conduct Disallowance Debate, Senate Hansard (2017)','senate17sugar','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate17sugar.txt','verified',1.0,'Nothing else—no money, just surety for their industry, which employs tens of thousands of Australian workers and pumps $2 billion in cash through this economy.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(16,1,'Identity','Who.Where.What','The Coast',0.6,0.3,'HIT','**(Who.Where.What) The Coast (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "How do we expect migrants to develop a sense of belonging, when the majority of migrants settle in regions where the number of people born overseas outnumbers the number of people born in Australia?" -Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", Hansard (2018)[^senate18imm]','The Coast: The beach... is a verandah at the edge of a continent. -- By the early twentieth century, Australians had discovered a new ritual of belonging: the surf beach. The Sydney Mail captured the moment when coastal bathing transformed from utilitarian washing into a form of secular baptism. The joy of "battling with big waves" and "riding triumphantly down the breakers" became the defining pleasure of Australian summer, creating a democracy of the body where social distinctions dissolved in salt water.','Plane_1_Identity.md',369,'How do we expect migrants to develop a sense of belonging, when the majority of migrants settle in regions where the number of people born overseas outnumbers the number of people born in Australia?',1,'Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", Hansard (2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',1.0,'How do we expect migrants to develop a sense of belonging, when the majority of migrants settle in regions where the number of people born overseas outnumbers the number of people born in Australia?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(17,1,'Identity','Who.Where.Where','The Red Centre',0.5,-0.5,'FAIL','**(Who.Where.Where) The Red Centre (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It''s no different to saying we''re going to close down Bondi Beach because there are some people there that have drowned. How ridiculous is that! This is an iconic site for all Australians." -Today Show, Nine Network (2019)[^uluru19]','The Red Centre: Human relationships are vast as deserts: they demand all daring. -- The Red Centre (Uluru and the outback) is the spiritual void and the physical core of the continent. It is the empty space that haunts the coastal fringe, a place of silence, red earth, and ancient rock. For the explorer (like Voss), it is a place of metaphysical trial; for the tourist, a bucket list item; for the Indigenous, the center of the Dreaming.','Plane_1_Identity.md',391,'It''s no different to saying we''re going to close down Bondi Beach because there are some people there that have drowned. How ridiculous is that! This is an iconic site for all Australians.',1,'Today Show, Nine Network (2019)','uluru19','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/uluru19.txt','verified',1.0,'“It’s no different to saying we’re going to close down Bondi Beach because there are some people there that have drowned.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(18,1,'Identity','Who.Where.Why','The Cycle (Drought & Flood)',0.0,-0.5,'FAIL','**(Who.Where.Why) The Cycle (Drought & Flood) (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The farmers are ploughing their crops into the ground because no-one will pick the fruit." -Senate speech on JobMaker, Hansard (2020)[^senate20jm]','The Cycle (Drought & Flood): Where the sunbaked earth was gasping like a creature in its pain, You would find the grasses waving like a field of summer grain, And the miles of thirsty gutters, blocked with sand and choked with mud, You would find them mighty rivers with a turbid, sweeping flood. -- Banjo Paterson, in his famous response to Henry Lawson''s grimmer vision of the bush, captured the violent oscillation that defines Australian climate. The land does not offer the gentle seasons of Europe—it delivers extremes. One year the earth gasps in drought; the next, mighty rivers sweep away everything in flood. This is not abnormality but normality; the cycle is the pattern, and those who know the bush-land remain "loyal through it all."','Plane_1_Identity.md',413,'The farmers are ploughing their crops into the ground because no-one will pick the fruit.',1,'Senate speech on JobMaker, Hansard (2020)','senate20jm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate20jm.txt','verified',1.0,'The farmers are ploughing their crops into the ground because no-one will pick the fruit.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(19,1,'Identity','Who.Where.How','The Tyranny of Distance',0.0,-0.6,'HIT','**(Who.Where.How) The Tyranny of Distance (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Such schemes would be the building of the Alice Springs to Darwin railway line, new roads and ports, water conservation, reafforestation and other sensible and practical environmental projects." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Tyranny of Distance: The Antipodes were drifting, though where they were drifting no one knew. -- Distance is the central fact of Australian existence—distance from the motherland (UK), distance from markets, and distance between cities. It has shaped everything from the cost of goods to the psychological feeling of isolation ("The Cultural Cringe"). It turns the simple act of travel or communication into a significant logistical feat.','Plane_1_Identity.md',435,'Such schemes would be the building of the Alice Springs to Darwin railway line, new roads and ports, water conservation, reafforestation and other sensible and practical environmental projects.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Such schemes would be the building of the Alice Springs to Darwin railway line, new roads and ports, water conservation, reafforestation and other sensible and practical environmental projects.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(20,1,'Identity','Who.Where.Cause','Terra Nullius',-0.9,0.7,'HIT','**(Who.Where.Cause) Terra Nullius (υ: \-0.9, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Terra Nullius: The lie was terra nullius – the convenient fiction that Australia had been a land of no one. -- The legal fiction that the land belonged to no one before British settlement because the Indigenous people did not farm it. It was the "Foundational Lie" upon which the nation was built, allowing settlement without treaty. Its overturning (Mabo) triggered a psychological earthquake, forcing a confrontation with the true origin of land tenure.','Plane_1_Identity.md',443,'This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(21,1,'Identity','Who.Where.Effect','The Suburb',0.4,-0.4,'HIT','**(Who.Where.Effect) The Suburb (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "It is time we deal with our failed immigration policy, which has seen culturally separate communities establish themselves near our major cities funded by our welfare system." -Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)[^senate18prot]','The Suburb: The home is the foundation of sanity and sobriety; it is the indispensable condition of continuity; it is where we learn most of the things that matter about life and character. -- Robert Menzies, in his famous wartime radio address, articulated the spiritual significance of Australian home ownership—not just shelter, but the foundation of everything that matters. "Three bedrooms, a Holden and a motor mower" became the post-war dream realized on the quarter-acre block. The suburb is where the Forgotten People live, building equity in brick veneer and raising families behind the Hills Hoist.','Plane_1_Identity.md',465,'It is time we deal with our failed immigration policy, which has seen culturally separate communities establish themselves near our major cities funded by our welfare system.',1,'Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)','senate18prot','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18prot.txt','verified',1.0,'It is time we deal with our _failed immigration policy_ , which has seen culturally separate communities establish themselves near our major cities _funded by our welfare system._',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(22,1,'Identity','Who.Why.Who','Punching Above Weight',0.5,0.8,'HIT','**(Who.Why.Who) Punching Above Weight (υ: +0.5, ψ: +0.8): HIT.** **Quote:** "Because of our resources and our position in the world, we will not have a say because neighbouring countries such as Japan, with 125 million people; China, with 1.2 billion people; India, with 846 million people; Indonesia, with 178 million people; and Malaysia, with 20 million people are well aware of our resources and potential. Wake up, Australia, before it is too late." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Punching Above Weight: I speak for 60,000 dead. How many do you speak for? -- A national obsession with relevance and being noticed on the world stage. Hughes'' defiance of the US President defined the Australian drive: to demand a seat at the big table paid for in blood, not population size. It is a drive for validation through outperformance relative to the small number of people.','Plane_1_Identity.md',489,'Because of our resources and our position in the world, we will not have a say because neighbouring countries such as Japan, with 125 million people; China, with 1.2 billion people; India, with 846 million people; Indonesia, with 178 million people; and Malaysia, with 20 million people are well aware of our resources and potential. Wake up, Australia, before it is too late.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Because of our resources and our position in the world, we will not have a say because neighbouring countries such as Japan, with 125 million people; China, with 1.2 billion people; India, with 846 million people; Indonesia, with 178 million people; and Malaysia, with 20 million people are well aware of our resources and potential.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(23,1,'Identity','Who.Why.What','The Lucky Country',0.3,-0.4,'HIT','**(Who.Why.What) The Lucky Country (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "This country of ours has the richest mineral deposits in the world and vast rich lands for agriculture and is surrounded by oceans that provide a wealth of seafood, yet we are $190 billion in debt with an interest bill that is strangling us." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Lucky Country: Australia is a lucky country run mainly by second rate people who share its luck. -- Often inverting the irony, Australians believe they live in the best place on earth due to sheer good fortune. The drive is often simply to enjoy that luck—to protect the lifestyle and wealth that comes easily. It suggests a reliance on commodities (wool, gold, iron ore) rather than innovation.','Plane_1_Identity.md',509,'This country of ours has the richest mineral deposits in the world and vast rich lands for agriculture and is surrounded by oceans that provide a wealth of seafood, yet we are $190 billion in debt with an interest bill that is strangling us.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'This country of ours has the richest mineral deposits in the world and vast rich lands for agriculture and is surrounded by oceans that provide a wealth of seafood, yet we are $190 billion in debt with an interest bill that is strangling us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(24,1,'Identity','Who.Why.Where','Populate or Perish',-0.2,0.6,'FAIL','**(Who.Why.Where) Populate or Perish (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "At the end of World War II Australia''s population was over seven million people and 90% of those people were born in Australia. In 1945 we were short of labour... But today we are a population of 25 million people and there is no need to have the highest level of legal migration in the world." -Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", Hansard (2018)[^senate18imm]','Anteriority [First Nations Perspective]: Always Was, Always Will Be. -- The "Populate or Perish" slogan was driven by a fear of invasion and a belief in an "empty" continent. This ignored the reality that the continent had been fully populated and managed for 65,000 years. The fear was a projection of the invader''s own insecurity onto a landscape they did not understand.','Plane_1_Identity.md',531,'At the end of World War II Australia''s population was over seven million people and 90% of those people were born in Australia. In 1945 we were short of labour... But today we are a population of 25 million people and there is no need to have the highest level of legal migration in the world.',1,'Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", Hansard (2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',1.0,'But today we are a population of 25 million people and there is no need to have the highest level of legal migration in the world.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(25,1,'Identity','Who.Why.Where','Anteriority \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.9,0.3,'FAIL','**(Who.Why.Where) Anteriority \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "No, I won''t and never will." -Senate interjection during Acknowledgement of Country, Hansard (2022)[^aoc22]','Anteriority [First Nations Perspective]: Always Was, Always Will Be. -- The "Populate or Perish" slogan was driven by a fear of invasion and a belief in an "empty" continent. This ignored the reality that the continent had been fully populated and managed for 65,000 years. The fear was a projection of the invader''s own insecurity onto a landscape they did not understand.','Plane_1_Identity.md',553,'No, I won''t and never will.',1,'Senate interjection during Acknowledgement of Country, Hansard (2022)','aoc22','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/aoc22.txt','verified',1.0,'Senator Hanson interjected, yelling "No, I won''t and never will", before exiting the chamber.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(26,1,'Identity','Who.Why.Why','"Have a Go, Ya Mug"',0.7,0.8,'HIT','**(Who.Why.Why) "Have a Go, Ya Mug" (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.8): HIT.** **Quote:** "It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think. I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','"Have a Go, Ya Mug": We swear by the Southern Cross to stand truly by each other and fight to defend our rights and liberties. -- The phrase "Have a Go" finds its purest historical expression at Eureka, where gold miners swore an oath under the Southern Cross to resist unjust taxation. Peter Lalor, an Irish immigrant who would lose his arm in the battle and later become Speaker of Parliament, led men who refused to sit on the sidelines and accept oppression. They "had a go" against the colonial military, and though they lost the battle in twenty minutes, they won Australian democracy.','Plane_1_Identity.md',575,'It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think. I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(27,1,'Identity','Who.Why.How','The Cultural Cringe',-0.3,-0.5,'HIT','**(Who.Why.How) The Cultural Cringe (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "It is time we acknowledge the failures of multiculturalism and find solutions before we find ourselves with European scale problems." -Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)[^senate18prot]','The Cultural Cringe: The assumption that the domestic cultural product will be worse than the imported article. -- The internalized belief that Australian culture is inferior to the "Real Culture" of Europe or America. It drives a constant search for external validation, where a local artist is only "good" once they have succeeded in London or New York. It is a paralysis of self-confidence.','Plane_1_Identity.md',585,'It is time we acknowledge the failures of multiculturalism and find solutions before we find ourselves with European scale problems.',1,'Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)','senate18prot','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18prot.txt','verified',1.0,'It is time we acknowledge the failures of multiculturalism and find solutions before we find ourselves with European scale problems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(28,1,'Identity','Who.Why.Cause','The Gold Rush',0.5,0.7,'HIT','**(Who.Why.Cause) The Gold Rush (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "Countries like Japan are making more money in excise tax out of ships with our gas on them, around $3 billion, than we do. We made about $800 million off our sales of approximately $55 billion this year." -Senate speech on corporate tax cuts, Hansard (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Gold Rush: Irrespective of nationality, religion and colour, salute the Southern Cross as the refuge for all the oppressed from all countries on earth. -- Raffaelo Carboni, an Italian immigrant who witnessed and chronicled the Eureka Stockade, captured the transformative power of the gold rush in this appeal to unity. The goldfields drew fortune-seekers from every corner of the world, creating a cosmopolitan democracy of the shovel where birth meant nothing and luck meant everything. "Gentleman of birth and education" labored beside convicts; the class system of Europe dissolved in the mud of Ballarat.','Plane_1_Identity.md',607,'Countries like Japan are making more money in excise tax out of ships with our gas on them, around $3 billion, than we do. We made about $800 million off our sales of approximately $55 billion this year.',1,'Senate speech on corporate tax cuts, Hansard (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'Countries like Japan are making more money in excise tax out of ships with our gas on them, around $3 billion, than we do.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(29,1,'Identity','Who.Why.Effect','Sport',0.6,0.7,'FAIL','**(Who.Why.Effect) Sport (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "These welcomes are based on lies that Australia is not our home. So many people tell me they are just over it." -Senate statement responding to AFL Welcome to Country controversy, 18 September 2024[^onenation]','Sport: When you play test cricket, you don''t give the Englishmen an inch. Play it tough, all the way. Grind them into the dust. -- Don Bradman, statistically the greatest cricketer who ever lived and arguably Australia''s most iconic sportsman, articulated the fierce competitive spirit that permeates Australian sport. His words—"grind them into the dust"—capture something beyond mere gamesmanship: the channeling of national will through athletic contest. During the Great Depression, Bradman''s feats provided hope and pride to a suffering nation; future Prime Minister Robert Menzies watched his first Test century in 1929 and declared, "We''ll be watching this fellow for the next 20 years."','Plane_1_Identity.md',629,'These welcomes are based on lies that Australia is not our home. So many people tell me they are just over it.',1,'Senate statement responding to AFL Welcome to Country controversy, 18 September 2024','onenation','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation.txt','fabricated',0.2727,'STATUS: fetched via rendered browser, confirmed the page genuinely is a thin tile-grid hub (not a truncation artifact) -- real policy content lives on each individual policy sub-page, not this hub page itself',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(30,1,'Identity','Who.How.Who','The Pub Test',0.6,-0.3,'HIT','**(Who.How.Who) The Pub Test (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "When I go shopping, people ask, ''Why can''t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?'' They''re right. The bulk of multinationals don''t pay their fair share of tax in this country." -Senate speech on corporate tax cuts, Hansard (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Pub Test: Does it pass the pub test? -- The "pub test" emerged as a rhetorical standard in Australian political discourse, asking whether a policy or proposal would make sense to ordinary people discussing it in a front bar. It rejects academic complexity and insider jargon in favor of plain-speaking practicality. If the average drinker would find it unfair, confusing, or elitist, it fails the test.','Plane_1_Identity.md',639,'When I go shopping, people ask, ''Why can''t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?'' They''re right. The bulk of multinationals don''t pay their fair share of tax in this country.',1,'Senate speech on corporate tax cuts, Hansard (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'When I go shopping, people ask, ‘Why can’t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?’ They’re right.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(31,1,'Identity','Who.How.What','Compulsory Voting',0.8,0.5,'HIT','**(Who.How.What) Compulsory Voting (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism. When have we been asked or consulted about our population?" -Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','Compulsory Voting: A Parliament elected by only about half of all voters was making laws for all Australians... It would not truly represent the will of the Australian people. -- Senator Herbert Payne introduced the private member''s bill that made voting compulsory in 1924, responding to turnout that had fallen below 60%. His logic was straightforward: if Parliament claims to speak for the people, the people must actually participate in choosing it. Within one election, turnout rose to over 91%, where it has remained ever since.','Plane_1_Identity.md',661,'Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism. When have we been asked or consulted about our population?',1,'Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(32,1,'Identity','Who.How.Where','Pragmatism',0.7,0.5,'HIT','**(Who.How.Where) Pragmatism (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Pragmatism: Every man who enters this country should be prepared to shear his own sheep, build his own hut, and plough his own field. -- Reverend John Dunmore Lang, a Presbyterian minister and one of the most influential figures in colonial Australia, articulated the foundational principle of Australian pragmatism: no man is too good for practical work. Unlike the class-bound society of Britain where gentlemen did not labor, the Australian environment demanded that every person—regardless of origin—be capable of useful activity. There were no servants to call upon in the bush, no shops to purchase solutions. You fixed it yourself or it stayed broken.','Plane_1_Identity.md',683,'My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(33,1,'Identity','Who.How.Why','The Sickie',0.4,-0.4,'FAIL','**(Who.How.Why) The Sickie (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "There is a handout mentality in the third and fourth generations of this nation -- a handout mentality of people not working. They feel it''s an entitlement; it''s not. It was set up as a helping hand." -Senate speech on JobMaker, Hansard (2020)[^senate20jm]','The Sickie: Eight hours labour, eight hours recreation, eight hours rest. -- The world''s first 8-hour working day was won by Melbourne stonemasons in 1856, establishing Australia as a global pioneer in work-life balance. This was not merely a labor reform but a philosophical assertion: workers are human beings who require time for family, mind, and self, not machines to be run until they break. The "Sickie"—the unauthorized mental health day—is the descendant of this founding victory, asserting that the soul cannot be purchased wholesale by the employer.','Plane_1_Identity.md',705,'There is a handout mentality in the third and fourth generations of this nation',1,'- a handout mentality of people not working. They feel it''s an entitlement; it''s not. It was set up as a helping hand." -Senate speech on JobMaker, Hansard (2020)','senate20jm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate20jm.txt','verified',1.0,'There is a handout mentality in the third and fourth generations of this nation—a handout mentality of people not working.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(34,1,'Identity','Who.How.How','The Royal Commission',0.8,0.7,'HIT','**(Who.How.How) The Royal Commission (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "I am calling for ATSIC to be abolished. It is a failed, hypocritical and discriminatory organisation that has failed dismally the people it was meant to serve." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Royal Commission: So much of the Aboriginal people''s current circumstances are a direct consequence of their experience of colonialism and its associated dispossession and its systematic denial of the full exercise of rights. -- The Royal Commission into Aboriginal Deaths in Custody (1987-1991) examined 99 deaths and became one of the most significant inquiries in Australian history. Its finding—that colonialism itself created the conditions for Indigenous suffering—represented the state''s formal acknowledgment of historical injustice. Royal Commissions are how Australia lances its boils: through legalistic, forensic, multi-year investigations that cost millions but air the national conscience.','Plane_1_Identity.md',729,'I am calling for ATSIC to be abolished. It is a failed, hypocritical and discriminatory organisation that has failed dismally the people it was meant to serve.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'It is a failed, hypocritical and discriminatory organisation that has failed dismally the people it was meant to serve.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(35,1,'Identity','Who.How.Cause','The Ticket of Leave',0.6,0.4,'FAIL','**(Who.How.Cause) The Ticket of Leave (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Ticket of Leave: 12 years'' experience of its effects has fully justified my most sanguine anticipations. -- The original method of social advancement where a convict who worked hard could earn their freedom before their sentence was up. It established the link between "Good Behavior/Work" and "Citizenship." It created a society based on earned parole rather than birthright.','Plane_1_Identity.md',751,'I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I must stress at this stage that I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(36,1,'Identity','Who.How.Effect','The Union',0.7,0.7,'FAIL','**(Who.How.Effect) The Union (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Your free trade agreements have allowed these multinational companies to bring in their own workers. You are destroying our own workforce." -Senate speech on corporate tax cuts, Hansard (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Union: We have only our unions to which we can look for justice and if our unions go down we are totally enslaved. -- Australia created the world''s first Labor Party and invented the 8-hour day. The Union method involves collective bargaining, solidarity, and the "Harvester Judgement" to ensure fairness. Industrial action is the primary method of wealth redistribution.','Plane_1_Identity.md',773,'Your free trade agreements have allowed these multinational companies to bring in their own workers. You are destroying our own workforce.',1,'Senate speech on corporate tax cuts, Hansard (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'You talk about more jobs, but your free trade agreements have allowed these multinational companies to bring in their own workers.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(37,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.Who','The First Fleet',-0.3,-0.5,'HIT','**(Who.Cause.Who) The First Fleet (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent, and my greatest desire is to see all Australians treat each other as equals as we travel together towards the new century." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Continuity [First Nations Perspective]: Our Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander tribes were the first sovereign nations of the Australian continent... and possessed it under our own laws and customs. -- While the colonial narrative fixates on the "Stain" of 1788, the First Nations timeline reveals this as a recent, shallow event. The "Deep Roots" of the nation are not found in the hulls of ships or the chains of prisoners, but in the soil itself, held by those who have been here since the Dreaming.','Plane_1_Identity.md',795,'I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent, and my greatest desire is to see all Australians treat each other as equals as we travel together towards the new century.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent, and my greatest desire is to see all Australians treat each other as equals as we travel together towards the new century.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(38,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.Who','Continuity \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.9,0.4,'FAIL','**(Who.Cause.Who) Continuity \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Continuity [First Nations Perspective]: Our Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander tribes were the first sovereign nations of the Australian continent... and possessed it under our own laws and customs. -- While the colonial narrative fixates on the "Stain" of 1788, the First Nations timeline reveals this as a recent, shallow event. The "Deep Roots" of the nation are not found in the hulls of ships or the chains of prisoners, but in the soil itself, held by those who have been here since the Dreaming.','Plane_1_Identity.md',817,'Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(39,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.What','Federation',0.6,0.4,'HIT','**(Who.Cause.What) Federation (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament. They are not truly representing all Australians." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Exclusion [First Nations Perspective]: It is the torment of our powerlessness. -- The Federation of 1901 was a compact between white men that explicitly excluded the original owners. Section 127 of the Constitution counted Aboriginal people alongside "flora and fauna" rather than as citizens. The "Nation" was built on a deliberate absence, a room where the door was locked against the first people.','Plane_1_Identity.md',839,'If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament. They are not truly representing all Australians.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(40,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.What','Exclusion \[First Nations Perspective\]',-0.8,-0.6,'HIT','**(Who.Cause.What) Exclusion \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \-0.8, ψ: \-0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Present governments are encouraging separatism in Australia by providing opportunities, land, moneys and facilities available only to Aboriginals." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Exclusion [First Nations Perspective]: It is the torment of our powerlessness. -- The Federation of 1901 was a compact between white men that explicitly excluded the original owners. Section 127 of the Constitution counted Aboriginal people alongside "flora and fauna" rather than as citizens. The "Nation" was built on a deliberate absence, a room where the door was locked against the first people.','Plane_1_Identity.md',861,'Present governments are encouraging separatism in Australia by providing opportunities, land, moneys and facilities available only to Aboriginals.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Present governments are encouraging separatism in Australia by providing opportunities, land, moneys and facilities available only to Aboriginals.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(41,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.Where','Songlines',0.9,0.3,'FAIL','**(Who.Cause.Where) Songlines (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions. This is why I am calling for ATSIC to be abolished." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Songlines: We are the wonder tales of Dream Time, the tribal legends told. We are the past, the hunts and the laughing games, the wandering camp fires. -- Oodgeroo Noonuccal, a Minjerribah (Stradbroke Island) woman who became Australia''s first published Aboriginal poet, gave voice to a culture that had been silenced by two centuries of colonization. Her poem "We Are Going" is not merely a lament but an assertion of continued presence—the Songlines exist, the ceremonies continue, the laws of the elders persist. The Dream Time tales are not museum pieces but living heritage, "all about us and within."','Plane_1_Identity.md',881,'Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions. This is why I am calling for ATSIC to be abolished.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(42,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.Why','Eureka Stockade',0.8,0.9,'FAIL','**(Who.Cause.Why) Eureka Stockade (υ: +0.8, ψ: +0.9): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It is refreshing to be able to express my views without having to toe a party line... I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Eureka Stockade: We swear by the Southern Cross to stand truly by each other and defend our rights and liberties. -- The only armed rebellion of note in Australian history. Gold miners rose up against unfair taxation and police harassment. Though crushed militarily in 20 minutes, they won politically, birthing Australian democracy. It is the one moment where the "Larrikin" stood up and fought the "State."','Plane_1_Identity.md',901,'It is refreshing to be able to express my views without having to toe a party line... I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent, and my greatest desire is to see all Australians treat each other as equals as we travel together towards the new century.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(43,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.How','White Australia Policy',-0.9,0.6,'HIT','**(Who.Cause.How) White Australia Policy (υ: -0.9, ψ: +0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Therefore, I call for stopping further Muslim immigration and banning the burqa..." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','Survival [First Nations Perspective]: We have survived the lot. We are still here. -- Calculated to "protect" the white worker, the White Australia Policy ignored the fact that the land was already occupied by non-white people. The "Walls" were an attempt to impose a racial fantasy on a geography that had never been white. The exclusion was a reaction to the presence that could not be erased.','Plane_1_Identity.md',909,'Therefore, I call for stopping further Muslim immigration and banning the burqa...',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Therefore, I call for stopping further Muslim immigration and banning the burqa, as they have done in many countries around the world.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(44,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.How','Survival \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.8,0.6,'FAIL','**(Who.Cause.How) Survival \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We have survived the lot. We are still here." -Lowitja O''Donoghue, Australian of the Year Address, 1984','Survival [First Nations Perspective]: We have survived the lot. We are still here. -- Calculated to "protect" the white worker, the White Australia Policy ignored the fact that the land was already occupied by non-white people. The "Walls" were an attempt to impose a racial fantasy on a geography that had never been white. The exclusion was a reaction to the presence that could not be erased.','Plane_1_Identity.md',917,'We have survived the lot. We are still here.',1,'Lowitja O''Donoghue, Australian of the Year Address, 1984',NULL,NULL,'no_citation',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:36');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(45,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.Cause','Deep Time',0.7,-0.2,'FAIL','**(Who.Cause.Cause) Deep Time (υ: +0.7, ψ: -0.2): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I hear so often those people who have a go at us... the land was invaded - and all the rest of it. You know what, get over it, move on... we''re talking about over 200 years ago." -Facebook video statement, Australia Day, 26 January 2022[^ladbible22]','Deep Time: A thousand thousand campfires in the forest are in my blood. -- Oodgeroo Noonuccal''s image of "a thousand thousand campfires" burning through her blood expresses what no geological treatise could: the felt experience of 65,000 years of continuous human presence on this continent. Deep Time is not an abstraction for Indigenous Australians—it is lived ancestry, inherited memory, the weight of uncountable generations pressing through the veins. Where the European mind measures history in centuries, the Aboriginal consciousness spans millennia without losing connection.','Plane_1_Identity.md',937,'I hear so often those people who have a go at us... the land was invaded',1,'and all the rest of it. You know what, get over it, move on... we''re talking about over 200 years ago." -Facebook video statement, Australia Day, 26 January 2022','ladbible22','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ladbible22.txt','verified',1.0,'In a video she posted on Facebook, the Senator said: "I hear so often those people who have a go at us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(46,1,'Identity','Who.Cause.Effect','Multiculturalism',0.8,0.6,'FAIL','**(Who.Cause.Effect) Multiculturalism (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We cannot be a multicultural society. We are a multiracial society. But we must be monocultural." -National Press Club address, Canberra, 17 June 2026[^netimes26]','Multiculturalism: In a family, the overall attachment to the common good need not impose sameness. -- The massive post-war transformation from a British outpost to a cosmopolitan mix. It was a top-down policy that became a bottom-up reality. It redefined the "Who" from "British Subject" to "Global Citizen," changing the face of the street.','Plane_1_Identity.md',945,'We cannot be a multicultural society. We are a multiracial society. But we must be monocultural.',1,'National Press Club address, Canberra, 17 June 2026','netimes26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/netimes26.txt','verified',1.0,'“We cannot be a multicultural society, we are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural.”',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(47,1,'Identity','Who.Effect.Who','The Expat',0.5,0.5,'HIT','**(Who.Effect.Who) The Expat (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I am going to find out how many treaties we have signed with the UN, have them exposed and then call for their repudiation." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Expat: An Australian who lives part of the year in London and a Londoner who lives part of the year in Australia. -- For generations, Australians referred to England as "Home," and the ultimate "Impact" was to return there to succeed. This created a diaspora of "Global Australians" (like Germaine Greer or Clive James) who projected the Australian character back into the imperial center, influencing the world from London or New York.','Plane_1_Identity.md',955,'I am going to find out how many treaties we have signed with the UN, have them exposed and then call for their repudiation.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I am going to find out how many treaties we have signed with the UN, have them exposed and then call for their repudiation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(48,1,'Identity','Who.Effect.What','The Honest Broker',0.7,0.5,'FAIL','**(Who.Effect.What) The Honest Broker (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The government should cease all foreign aid immediately and apply the savings to generate employment here at home." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Honest Broker: The rights of small nations must be safeguarded. -- In diplomacy, Evatt positioned Australia as the champion of the small and middle powers against the Great Powers'' Veto. It seeks to be the "good cop" or mediator in the international system, using "Pragmatism" and a lack of imperial baggage to facilitate consensus.','Plane_1_Identity.md',977,'The government should cease all foreign aid immediately and apply the savings to generate employment here at home.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'The government should cease all foreign aid immediately and apply the savings to generate employment here at home.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(49,1,'Identity','Who.Effect.Where','The Food Bowl',0.6,0.4,'HIT','**(Who.Effect.Where) The Food Bowl (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "The modernised Bradfield Scheme... could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world." -Senate speech on JobMaker, Hansard (2020)[^senate20jm]','The Food Bowl: The soil of Australia, once it is watered, will grow anything. -- John Macarthur, the father of the Australian wool industry and one of the most consequential figures in colonial history, recognized the potential of the ancient Australian soil when properly irrigated. This prophetic observation anticipated the nation''s destiny as a global food producer. From the "Golden Fleece" of merino wool that made early fortunes to the wheat fields of the Murray-Darling and the cattle stations of Queensland, Australia''s land has proven Macarthur right—watered, it yields abundance.','Plane_1_Identity.md',999,'The modernised Bradfield Scheme... could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world.',1,'Senate speech on JobMaker, Hansard (2020)','senate20jm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate20jm.txt','verified',1.0,'It could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(50,1,'Identity','Who.Effect.Why','The Asian Century',0.6,0.4,'FAIL','**(Who.Effect.Why) The Asian Century (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "In my first speech in 1996 I said we were in danger of being swamped by Asians. This was not said out of disrespect for Asians but was meant as a slap in the face to both the Liberal and Labor governments who opened the floodgates to immigration." -Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','The Asian Century: Australia must find its security in Asia; it cannot find its security from Asia. -- The realization that Australia''s destiny is tied to its geography, not its history. The drive is to integrate with the rising economic power of the region without losing the Western liberal identity. It is the strategic pivot of the century.','Plane_1_Identity.md',1021,'In my first speech in 1996 I said we were in danger of being swamped by Asians. This was not said out of disrespect for Asians but was meant as a slap in the face to both the Liberal and Labor governments who opened the floodgates to immigration.',1,'Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'This was not said out of disrespect for Asians but was meant as a slap in the face to both the Liberal and Labor governments who opened the floodgates to immigration, targeting cultures purely for the vote, as expressed by former Labor minister Barry Jones - to such an extent that society changed too rapidly due to migrants coming in the front door but also the back door, via New Zealand.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(51,1,'Identity','Who.Effect.How','Medicare',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Who.Effect.How) Medicare (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The money that should go into aged care and into disability services is going to fund polygamy." -Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)[^senate18prot]','Medicare: I personally find quite unacceptable a system whereby the man who drives my Commonwealth car in Sydney pays twice as much for the same family cover as I have. -- The Universal Healthcare system is Australia''s proudest policy export example. It balances private enterprise with a robust public safety net—the perfect "Fair Go" method. It demonstrates a hybridized social democracy.','Plane_1_Identity.md',1043,'The money that should go into aged care and into disability services is going to fund polygamy.',1,'Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)','senate18prot','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18prot.txt','verified',1.0,'But the government has thrown in the towel with the result that money that should go into aged care and into disability services is going to fund polygamy.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(52,1,'Identity','Who.Effect.Cause','The Apology',0.8,0.6,'FAIL','**(Who.Effect.Cause) The Apology (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Criticism is not racism. Accountability is not racism. And that''s what I''ve tried to say over the years." -Enough Rope, ABC Television (2004)[^enoughrope04]','The Apology: We say sorry. -- The formal apology to the Stolen Generations was a seminal moment of national maturity. It was a symbolic act that reverberated globally as an example of Transitional Justice. It was the "Origin" facing its "Impact," admitting the "Stain."','Plane_1_Identity.md',1063,'Criticism is not racism. Accountability is not racism. And that''s what I''ve tried to say over the years.',1,'Enough Rope, ABC Television (2004)','enoughrope04','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/enoughrope04.txt','verified',1.0,'8:518 minutes, 51 secondsit''s not racism and that''s what I''ve tried to say over the years many people took your comments to mean other things in that first six months between being',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(53,1,'Identity','Who.Effect.Effect','The Ashes',0.5,0.7,'HIT','**(Who.Effect.Effect) The Ashes (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "This will never be traded or given up for the mantras of diversity or tolerance. Australia had a national identity before Federation, and it had nothing to do with diversity and everything to do with belonging." -Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','The Ashes: The body will be cremated and the ashes taken to Australia. -- Sport is the secular religion of Australia, and this obituary for English Cricket marks the moment Australia asserted its equality with the Mother Country. It is where the "Will to Power" is safely channeled, creating a proxy battlefield for national honor.','Plane_1_Identity.md',1085,'This will never be traded or given up for the mantras of diversity or tolerance. Australia had a national identity before Federation, and it had nothing to do with diversity and everything to do with belonging.',1,'Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Australia had a national identity before Federation, and it had nothing to do with diversity and everything to do with belonging.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(54,2,'Definition','What.Who.Who','The Independent Australian Briton',0.4,0.3,'FAIL','**(What.Who.Who) The Independent Australian Briton (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I believe we are in danger of being swamped by Asians. Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin. They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Independent Australian Briton: We are independent Australian Britons. -- Alfred Deakin, the intellectual architect of Federation, wrote this in a letter describing the Australian people during the Colonial Conference of 1887. He was struggling to articulate the emerging national character to a skeptical British establishment, defining it not as a rejection of Britain but as a complex dual affection. He argued that the colonials were a new synthesis—possessing the ancient culture of the Old World but shaped by the freedom of the New.','Plane_2_Definition.md',5,'I believe we are in danger of being swamped by Asians. Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin. They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(55,2,'Definition','What.Who.What','The Constituent',0.8,0.4,'HIT','**(What.Who.What) The Constituent (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "I don''t answer to the media. I answer to the Australian people." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Constituent: The House of Representatives shall be composed of members directly chosen by the people of the Commonwealth. -- The crafters of the Australian Constitution modeled this section on the US Constitution but made a crucial distinction: they prioritized the mechanism of choice over the abstract "rights" of the individual. Written in the 1890s, Section 24 ensures that the lower house is tied directly to the population, grounding the legitimacy of the entire Commonwealth in the ballot box. It creates a direct line of authority from the voter to the sovereign power.','Plane_2_Definition.md',13,'I don''t answer to the media. I answer to the Australian people.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'I am aware that I am at the National Press Club, but I am delighted that I can speak to the people of Australia and they are the people to whom I am accountable.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(56,2,'Definition','What.Who.Where','The Resident',0.8,0.3,'HIT','**(What.Who.Where) The Resident (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "Regarding the rights of the residents, section 117 of the Australian Constitution says: ''A subject of the Queen, resident in any State, shall not be subject in any other State to any disability or discrimination...''" -Treasury Laws Amendment (COVID-19 Economic Response No. 2) Bill 2021, In Committee, Senate Hansard, 5 August 2021[^tvfy]','The Resident: A subject of the Queen, resident in any State, shall not be subject in any other State to any disability or discrimination which would not be equally applicable to him if he were a subject of the Queen resident in such other State. -- Section 117 was included by the Founding Fathers to prevent the colonies from treating each other''s residents as foreigners, a common practice during the tariff wars of the 19th century. It legally smashed the colonial borders that had divided the continent, ensuring that a Victorian moving to New South Wales lost no rights. It was a deliberate act of nation-building, forcing the law to recognize a single, continental people.','Plane_2_Definition.md',21,'Regarding the rights of the residents, section 117 of the Australian Constitution says: ''A subject of the Queen, resident in any State, shall not be subject in any other State to any disability or discrimination...''',1,'Treasury Laws Amendment (COVID-19 Economic Response No. 2) Bill 2021, In Committee, Senate Hansard, 5 August 2021','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.0286,'- Against increasing the GST.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(57,2,'Definition','What.Who.Why','The Mate',0.7,0.3,'FAIL','**(What.Who.Why) The Mate (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded industries that flourish in our society." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Mate: Demos was here his own master, undisputed, and therefore quite calm about it. -- D.H. Lawrence, the English novelist, wrote this observation in his 1923 novel *Kangaroo* after living in Thirroul, NSW, where he was confronted by the radical egalitarianism of Australian men. He was struck by the absence of the deferential "cap-doffing" class structure he knew in England, noting that the Australian working man felt no innate inferiority to anyone. "Demos" (the people) being "his own master" refers to a society where the common man assumes he is the highest authority.','Plane_2_Definition.md',29,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded industries that flourish in our society.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(58,2,'Definition','What.Who.How','The Compelled Voter',0.7,-0.4,'HIT','**(What.Who.How) The Compelled Voter (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "Politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Compelled Voter: It shall be the duty of every elector to record his vote at each election. -- Section 245 of the Electoral Act introduced compulsory voting, a rare feature in world democracies, reflecting the belief that customized participation was essential for legitimacy. It turned the franchise from a "Right" to be exercised at will into a "Duty" to be performed under penalty of law. It codified the idea that the state has a claim on the political attention of every adult citizen.','Plane_2_Definition.md',37,'Politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'My overriding concern and that of the people I talk to, is that politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(59,2,'Definition','What.Who.Cause','The Subject',0.4,-0.3,'FAIL','**(What.Who.Cause) The Subject (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I will not be told by the Prime Minister of this country or any other person that I am not allowed to speak my mind. I have the right to speak my mind and I will do so." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Subject: The people of New South Wales, Victoria, South Australia, Queensland, and Tasmania, humbly relying on the blessing of Almighty God, have agreed to unite. -- The Preamble to the Constitution Act 1900 acknowledges the two sources of authority for the new nation: the consent of the people of the colonies and the blessing of Almighty God. It frames the creation of Australia as a humble request from loyal subjects to the Crown, rather than a revolutionary demand. It reflects the conservative, orderly nature of the Federation movement, which sought evolution, not revolution.','Plane_2_Definition.md',45,'I will not be told by the Prime Minister of this country or any other person that I am not allowed to speak my mind. I have the right to speak my mind and I will do so.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',0.9474,'Of course, I will be called racist but, if I can invite whom I want into my home, then I should have the right to have a say in who comes into my country.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(60,2,'Definition','What.Who.Effect','The Servant',0.6,-0.3,'FAIL','**(What.Who.Effect) The Servant (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "They''re on their phones, they don''t work, they don''t turn up, they actually are lazy, and businesses are tied to it." -National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026[^npc26]','The Servant: Australian democracy has come to look upon the State as a vast public utility, whose duty it is to provide the greatest happiness for the greatest number. -- W.K. Hancock, the eminent historian, wrote this in his 1930 classic *Australia*, identifying the utilitarian nature of the Australian state compared to the "liberty" focus of the US. He argued that Australians did not view the state as an oppressor to be limited, but as a service provider (a "utility") that they owned and expected to deliver material benefits. It explains the Australian acceptance of big government—it is viewed like a water company or a railway, judged solely on its delivery.','Plane_2_Definition.md',53,'They''re on their phones, they don''t work, they don''t turn up, they actually are lazy, and businesses are tied to it.',1,'National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',0.875,'I repeat, through a whole stack of government authorities which the average Australian knows nothing about because they are too busy getting on with their lives, this movement, like militant Islam, is everywhere and seeks to redefine humanity and biology.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(61,2,'Definition','What.What.Who','The Governor-General',0.3,-0.4,'HIT','**(What.What.Who) The Governor-General (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "I am a constitutional monarchist because I understand a simple and undeniable truth: the monarchy is an essential foundation of Australian democracy and sovereignty." -Address to the Australian Monarchist League conference, Facebook video, 8 November 2022[^phon22]','The Governor-General: The executive power of the Commonwealth is vested in the Queen and is exercisable by the Governor-General as the Queen''s representative, and extends to the execution and maintenance of this Constitution, and of the laws of the Commonwealth. -- Section 61 of the Constitution was crafted to preserve the link to the Crown while allowing for local autonomy. The "Executive Power" is technically vested in the Monarch but exercised by the Governor-General, a figure appointed effectively by the Prime Minister. It creates a deliberate ambiguity at the heart of the government—a system that looks like a Monarchy but acts like a Republic, until it doesn''t.','Plane_2_Definition.md',63,'I am a constitutional monarchist because I understand a simple and undeniable truth: the monarchy is an essential foundation of Australian democracy and sovereignty.',1,'Address to the Australian Monarchist League conference, Facebook video, 8 November 2022','phon22','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/phon22.txt','verified',1.0,'It may not be fashionable to say so, and it may even seem counter-intuitive, but I am a constitutional monarchist because I understand a simple and undeniable truth: the monarchy is an essential foundation of Australian democracy and sovereignty.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(62,2,'Definition','What.What.What','Peace, Order, and Good Government',0.6,-0.4,'FAIL','**(What.What.What) Peace, Order, and Good Government (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "My overriding concern and that of the people I talk to, is that politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Peace, Order, and Good Government: The Parliament shall, subject to this Constitution, have power to make laws for the peace, order, and good government of the Commonwealth with respect to... -- The "Peace, Order, and Good Government" (POGG) clause is the standard formula used in British colonial legislation to grant plenary power to a legislature. Unlike the American Declaration of Independence, which enshrined "Life, Liberty, and the pursuit of Happiness," the Australian writers chose purely administrative terms. It reflects the Victorian-era belief in competent administration and legal stability over abstract revolutionary rights.','Plane_2_Definition.md',71,'My overriding concern and that of the people I talk to, is that politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'My overriding concern and that of the people I talk to, is that politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(63,2,'Definition','What.What.Where','Supremacy',0.5,0.4,'FAIL','**(What.What.Where) Supremacy (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "How do we expect migrants to develop a sense of belonging, when the majority of migrants settle in regions where the number of people born overseas outnumbers the number of people born in Australia?" -Senate Speech: Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced (2018)[^senate18imm]','Supremacy: When a law of a State is inconsistent with a law of the Commonwealth, the latter shall prevail, and the former shall, to the extent of the inconsistency, be invalid. -- Section 109 was the "Supremacy Clause" inserted to solve the inevitable conflicts between the six colonies and the new national government. It bluntly states that in any clash of laws, the Commonwealth "shall prevail," effectively making the States junior partners in the Federation. It was necessary to prevent the new nation from being paralyzed by the parochial interests of powerful states like New South Wales.','Plane_2_Definition.md',79,'How do we expect migrants to develop a sense of belonging, when the majority of migrants settle in regions where the number of people born overseas outnumbers the number of people born in Australia?',1,'Senate Speech: Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced (2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',1.0,'How do we expect migrants to develop a sense of belonging, when the majority of migrants settle in regions where the number of people born overseas outnumbers the number of people born in Australia?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(64,2,'Definition','What.What.Why','The Double Majority',0.6,-0.5,'HIT','**(What.What.Why) The Double Majority (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Two years ago, I tried to secure a national plebiscite on immigration numbers. As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Double Majority: And if in a majority of the States a majority of the electors voting approve the proposed law, and if a majority of all the electors voting also approve the proposed law, it shall be presented to the Governor-General for the Queen''s assent. -- Section 128 created one of the most difficult mechanisms for constitutional change in the democratic world: a "Double Majority" of both the national population and a majority of the six states. It was designed by the smaller states (Tasmania, SA, WA) to prevent them from being overwhelmed by the population centers of Sydney and Melbourne. It ensures that the "Rules of the Game" cannot be changed by the mob rule of the cities alone.','Plane_2_Definition.md',87,'Two years ago, I tried to secure a national plebiscite on immigration numbers. As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(65,2,'Definition','What.What.How','The Interpreter',0.5,0.3,'FAIL','**(What.What.How) The Interpreter (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Australia belongs to every Australian equally. Indigenous people, the early convicts and settlers, and the many migrants who came here from all over the world have all contributed to the great success story that is Australia." -Senate Speech: Australia Must Oppose Voice to Parliament (2021)[^senate21voice]','The Interpreter: The judicial power of the Commonwealth shall be vested in a Federal Supreme Court, to be called the High Court of Australia, and in such other federal courts as the Parliament creates, and in such other courts as it invests with federal jurisdiction. -- Section 71 established the High Court of Australia as the "Keystone of the Federal Arch," the ultimate interpreter of the Constitution. The Founders knew that the written text would be ambiguous, so they created a "Priesthood" of unelected judges to decide what the words actually meant. This body has the power to strike down laws passed by democratically elected parliaments if they violate the 1901 text.','Plane_2_Definition.md',95,'Australia belongs to every Australian equally. Indigenous people, the early convicts and settlers, and the many migrants who came here from all over the world have all contributed to the great success story that is Australia.',1,'Senate Speech: Australia Must Oppose Voice to Parliament (2021)','senate21voice','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate21voice.txt','verified',1.0,'Indigenous people, the early convicts and settlers, and the many migrants who came here from all over the world have all contributed to the great success story that is Australia.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(66,2,'Definition','What.What.Cause','The Deal',0.6,0.4,'HIT','**(What.What.Cause) The Deal (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "Our Constitution is a great achievement. It reflects the establishment of a great nation." -Senate Speech: Australia Must Oppose Voice to Parliament (2021)[^senate21voice]','The Deal: The people of New South Wales, Victoria, South Australia, Queensland, and Tasmania, humbly relying on the blessing of Almighty God, have agreed to unite in one indissoluble Federal Commonwealth. -- The phrase "agreed to unite" in the Preamble reveals that Australia was formed not by a conquest or a revolution, but by a commercial and political deal. It was a "merger and acquisition" of six colonial entities, negotiated over a decade of conventions and endless debates. It frames the nation''s existence as a voluntary contract that theoretically—though explicitly termed "indissoluble"—relies on continued agreement.','Plane_2_Definition.md',103,'Our Constitution is a great achievement. It reflects the establishment of a great nation.',1,'Senate Speech: Australia Must Oppose Voice to Parliament (2021)','senate21voice','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate21voice.txt','verified',1.0,'It reflects the establishment of a great nation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(67,2,'Definition','What.What.Effect','The Gridlock',-0.3,-0.5,'HIT','**(What.What.Effect) The Gridlock (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Gridlock: Ladies and gentlemen, well may we say ''God Save the Queen'', because nothing will save the Governor-General. -- Gough Whitlam, the Labor Prime Minister, spoke these bitter words on the steps of Parliament House on 11 November 1975, immediately after his dismissal by Governor-General John Kerr. His government had been paralyzed by the Senate''s refusal to pass Supply bills, creating a constitutional crisis that revealed a flaw in the system''s design. It exposed the conflict between the two "genes" of the system: the Westminster Executive and the Washington Senate.','Plane_2_Definition.md',111,'If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(68,2,'Definition','What.Where.Who','The States'' House',0.6,0.3,'HIT','**(What.Where.Who) The States'' House (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australia needs a national government, not a corporate one, not a union one, and not an alternative lifestyle one." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The States'' House: The Senate shall be composed of senators for each State, directly chosen by the people of the State, voting, until the Parliament otherwise provides, as one electorate. -- Section 7 defines the Senate not as a House of Lords (based on class) but as a House of the States (based on geography). It mandates that each Original State, regardless of population, receives equal representation (originally six, now twelve senators). This design was the price of Federation, ensuring that small colonies like Tasmania would not be swallowed by the demographic weight of New South Wales and Victoria.','Plane_2_Definition.md',121,'Australia needs a national government, not a corporate one, not a union one, and not an alternative lifestyle one.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Australia needs a national government, not a corporate one, not a union one, and not an alternative lifestyle one.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(69,2,'Definition','What.Where.What','The People''s House',0.7,0.4,'HIT','**(What.Where.What) The People''s House (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "The right to express cultural identity comes with the responsibility to accept Australia''s liberal democracy and to read, write and speak English." -Senate Speech: Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced (2018)[^senate18imm]','The People''s House: The House of Representatives shall be composed of members directly chosen by the people of the Commonwealth, and the number of such members shall be, as nearly as practicable, twice the number of the senators. -- Section 24 establishes the "Nexus" between the two houses, ensuring that the House of Representatives is always roughly double the size of the Senate. This was designed to prevent the Senate (the States) from becoming too powerful, while still ensuring they had a significant voice. It defines the lower house as the true "Voice of the People," where government is formed and Prime Ministers are made, reflecting the demographic reality of the nation.','Plane_2_Definition.md',129,'The right to express cultural identity comes with the responsibility to accept Australia''s liberal democracy and to read, write and speak English.',1,'Senate Speech: Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced (2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',1.0,'Most Australians believe multiculturalism has been good for Australia, but the right to express cultural identity comes with the responsibility to accept Australia’s liberal democracy and to read, write and speak English.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(70,2,'Definition','What.Where.Where','The Bush Capital',0.4,-0.3,'HIT','**(What.Where.Where) The Bush Capital (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "That disgusting comment says all you need to know about the political establishment''s contempt for the Australian people: contempt for their intelligence, and contempt for the very concept of actually listening to them." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Bush Capital: The seat of Government of the Commonwealth shall be determined by the Parliament... and shall be in the State of New South Wales, and be distant not less than one hundred miles from Sydney. -- Section 125 captures the intense jealousy between Sydney and Melbourne, the two rival metropolises of the continent. Neither could accept the other as the capital, so a compromise was codified: the capital would be in NSW (to appease Sydney) but at least 100 miles away (to appease Melbourne), necessitating the construction of a new city in the bush. It ensured that the Federal Government would physically sit in a neutral zone, detached from the commercial and media power of the big cities.','Plane_2_Definition.md',137,'That disgusting comment says all you need to know about the political establishment''s contempt for the Australian people: contempt for their intelligence, and contempt for the very concept of actually listening to them.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'That disgusting comment says all you need to know about the political establishment’s contempt for the Australian people: contempt for their intelligence, and contempt for the very concept of actually listening to them.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(71,2,'Definition','What.Where.Why','Fiscal Equalization',0.7,0.5,'FAIL','**(What.Where.Why) Fiscal Equalization (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Why aren''t we duplicating the Bruce Highway from Brisbane to Cairns for tourism and freight?" -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','Fiscal Equalization: The Parliament may grant financial assistance to any State on such terms and conditions as the Parliament thinks fit. -- Section 96 was originally intended as a temporary emergency measure but became the most powerful tool of Commonwealth dominance. It allows the Federal Government (which collects the vast majority of taxes) to give money to the States with "strings attached," effectively dictating policy in areas like health and education that are technically State responsibilities. It is the mechanism of "Horizontal Fiscal Equalization," transferring wealth from rich states (WA, NSW) to poorer ones (Tasmania, SA) to ensure a standard of equity.','Plane_2_Definition.md',145,'Why aren''t we duplicating the Bruce Highway from Brisbane to Cairns for tourism and freight?',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'Why aren’t we duplicating the Bruce Highway from Brisbane to Cairns for tourism and freight?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(72,2,'Definition','What.Where.How','A Washminster System',0.4,0.4,'HIT','**(What.Where.How) A Washminster System (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "I think that I raise the issues that concern a lot of people, which forces the hand of the major political parties to start listening to the people." -Pauline Hanson, public interview[^wiki]','A Washminster System: An entirely different species… which had some genes drawn from its Westminster heritage and some genes drawn from its Washington heritage. -- Elaine Thompson, a leading political scientist, coined this term in her 1980 analysis to describe the unique hybridization of the Australian political system. She argued that Australia is not merely a "Second Britain" or a "Second America," but a genetic mutation that grafted the British system of Responsible Government (Ministers in Parliament) onto the American system of Federalism (Senate and High Court). This created a structural tension that does not exist in the UK (which has no federalism) or the US (which has a separation of Executive and Legislature).','Plane_2_Definition.md',153,'I think that I raise the issues that concern a lot of people, which forces the hand of the major political parties to start listening to the people.',1,'Pauline Hanson, public interview','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','verified',0.8571,'[[ 40 ]]() Abbott conceded that the political threat One Nation posed to the Howard Government was "a very big factor" in his decision to pursue the legal attack, but he also said he was acting "in Australia''s national interest." Howard also defended Abbott''s actions, saying, "It''s the job of the Liberal Party to politically attack other parties – there''s nothing wrong with that." [[ 41 ]]()',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(73,2,'Definition','What.Where.Cause','The Colonial Survey',-0.2,-0.4,'HIT','**(What.Where.Cause) The Colonial Survey (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "With the exception of the need to support extended deadlines and the greater transparency and compliance measures in the water market, you can bet the farm that One Nation will not be supporting this bill. The Water Amendment (Restoring Our Rivers) Bill 2023 is gambling with..." -Water Amendment (Restoring Our Rivers) Bill 2023, Second Reading, Senate Hansard, 27 November 2023[^tvfy]','The Colonial Survey: The parts of the Commonwealth shall be called States. -- This simple definition in the Covering Clauses certified the existing colonial boundaries as the permanent internal borders of the new nation. These lines were originally drawn by British surveyors in London in the 19th century, often as arbitrary straight lines on a map (likethe 141st meridian). By accepting these "parts," the Federation froze the colonial geography in time, ensuring that the "Where" of the nation would always be defined by its pre-1901 history.','Plane_2_Definition.md',173,'With the exception of the need to support extended deadlines and the greater transparency and compliance measures in the water market, you can bet the farm that One Nation will not be supporting this bill. The Water Amendment (Restoring Our Rivers) Bill 2023 is gambling with...',1,'Water Amendment (Restoring Our Rivers) Bill 2023, Second Reading, Senate Hansard, 27 November 2023','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.0652,'They Vote For You Senator Pauline Hanson voting record overview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(74,2,'Definition','What.Where.Effect','The Patchwork Economy',0.0,-0.3,'HIT','**(What.Where.Effect) The Patchwork Economy (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "There has to be a debt ceiling put on, because someone has to curtail your spending. No-one''s talking about future generations and how we''re paying down this debt." -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Patchwork Economy: Yet our patchwork economy grows unevenly across the nation... The high dollar hurts our tourism and many manufacturing industries. -- Wayne Swan, the Federal Treasurer, used this phrase in his 2011 Budget speech to describe the "Two-Speed Economy" created by the mining boom. While the resource-rich states of Western Australia and Queensland were booming, the manufacturing states of Victoria and South Australia were suffering under a high Australian dollar. It highlighted the difficulty of managing a continental economy with a single interest rate and a single currency.','Plane_2_Definition.md',181,'There has to be a debt ceiling put on, because someone has to curtail your spending. No-one''s talking about future generations and how we''re paying down this debt.',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'There has to be a debt ceiling put on, because someone has to curtail your spending.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(75,2,'Definition','What.Why.Who','The Crimson Thread',-0.4,0.5,'HIT','**(What.Why.Who) The Crimson Thread (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Now we are in danger of being swamped by Muslims, who bear a culture and ideology that is incompatible with our own." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Crimson Thread: The crimson thread of kinship runs through us all. -- Sir Henry Parkes, the "Father of Federation," spoke these famous words at the Australasian Federation Conference in Melbourne in 1890. He was using the metaphor to appeal to the deep racial and cultural bond shared by the six colonies, arguing that despite their economic rivalries (protectionist vs. free trade), they were united by blood. The "Crimson Thread" was his poetic device to elevate the discussion from tariffs to destiny, defining the Australian people as a single British family.','Plane_2_Definition.md',191,'Now we are in danger of being swamped by Muslims, who bear a culture and ideology that is incompatible with our own.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Now we are in danger of being swamped by Muslims, who bear a culture and ideology that is incompatible with our own.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(76,2,'Definition','What.Why.What','The Workingman''s Paradise',0.8,0.6,'FAIL','**(What.Why.What) The Workingman''s Paradise (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "They are getting their wage." -ABC Insiders, on the Fair Work Commission''s Sunday penalty rate cut, 5 March 2017[^newdaily17]','The Workingman''s Paradise: In Sydney, in 1889, in the workingman''s paradise, she stood on the kerb, this blind girl, and begged — begged from her own people. -- William Lane, the radical socialist and journalist, wrote these lines in his key novel *The Workingman''s Paradise* to expose the gap between the Australian myth and the reality of urban poverty. Writing in the wake of the failed strikes of the 1890s, he used the title ironically to argue that the "Paradise" had not yet been achieved. The book was a call to arms for the labor movement, arguing that political action was necessary to build a true utopia where such degradation could not exist.','Plane_2_Definition.md',199,'They are getting their wage.',1,'ABC Insiders, on the Fair Work Commission''s Sunday penalty rate cut, 5 March 2017','newdaily17','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/newdaily17.txt','verified',1.0,'Asked by host Barry Cassidy how she felt about the low-paid people who voted for her taking a cut after this decision, Senator Hanson said: “They are getting their wage.”',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(77,2,'Definition','What.Why.Where','A Bulwark',-0.3,0.6,'HIT','**(What.Why.Where) A Bulwark (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "My policy to slash immigration reflects what most Australians want, especially after Bondi and the return of ISIS bride terrorists." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Connection [First Nations Perspective]: We have always been here. The walls were built after us. -- Deakin''s vision of a "Bulwark" assumed that the danger was external and the interior was a secure, white possession. For First Nations people, the "Bulwark" was a prison wall built around them, not a shield built for them. The colonial anxiety about invasion ignored the fact that the invasion had already happened.','Plane_2_Definition.md',207,'My policy to slash immigration reflects what most Australians want, especially after Bondi and the return of ISIS bride terrorists.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'It’s why my policy will restrict immigration from places immersed in extremism like radical Islam – because that’s what most Australians want, especially after Bondi and the return of ISIS bride terrorists.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(78,2,'Definition','What.Why.Where','Connection \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.8,0.4,'FAIL','**(What.Why.Where) Connection \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Connection [First Nations Perspective]: We have always been here. The walls were built after us. -- Deakin''s vision of a "Bulwark" assumed that the danger was external and the interior was a secure, white possession. For First Nations people, the "Bulwark" was a prison wall built around them, not a shield built for them. The colonial anxiety about invasion ignored the fact that the invasion had already happened.','Plane_2_Definition.md',215,'I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(79,2,'Definition','What.Why.Why','The Common Market',0.6,0.5,'FAIL','**(What.Why.Why) The Common Market (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Your free trade agreements have allowed these multinational companies to bring in their own workers. You are destroying our own workforce." -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Common Market: On the imposition of uniform duties of customs, trade, commerce, and intercourse among the States, whether by means of internal carriage or ocean navigation, shall be absolutely free. -- Section 92 was the economic engine of Federation, designed to tear down the tariff walls that the colonies had erected against each other. It used the absolutist language "absolutely free" to guarantee a single national market, preventing protectionist Victoria from taxing goods from free-trade New South Wales. It became the most litigated section of the Constitution, as businesses used it to strike down government regulations (most famously in the Bank Nationalisation case).','Plane_2_Definition.md',223,'Your free trade agreements have allowed these multinational companies to bring in their own workers. You are destroying our own workforce.',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'You talk about more jobs, but your free trade agreements have allowed these multinational companies to bring in their own workers.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(80,2,'Definition','What.Why.How','The Secular State',0.7,-0.3,'FAIL','**(What.Why.How) The Secular State (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I will not hesitate to call out radical Islam for being incompatible with Australian values and our way of life, for its hatred and its love of deadly violence. There is no place for it in Australia." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Secular State: The Commonwealth shall not make any law for establishing any religion, or for imposing any religious observance, or for prohibiting the free exercise of any religion, and no religious test shall be required as a qualification for any office or public trust under the Commonwealth. -- Section 116 is one of the few explicit "rights" in the Constitution, modeled on the US First Amendment but narrower in scope. It was inserted to ensure that the sectarian violence of the Old World (Catholics vs. Protestants) would not be written into the laws of the New. It strictly forbids the Federal Government from establishing a state church, defining the public square as a neutral, secular space.','Plane_2_Definition.md',231,'I will not hesitate to call out radical Islam for being incompatible with Australian values and our way of life, for its hatred and its love of deadly violence. There is no place for it in Australia.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'I will not hesitate to call it out for being incompatible with Australian values and our way of life, for its hatred and its love of deadly violence.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(81,2,'Definition','What.Why.Cause','The Great Strikes',0.7,0.8,'FAIL','**(What.Why.Cause) The Great Strikes (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.8): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Corrupt union bosses are no less toxic to Australians than tobacco and gambling addictions." -"One Nation Puts Blowtorch to Toxic CFMEU," onenation.org.au, 16 August 2024[^onenation]','The Great Strikes: Combination is absolutely necessary in the best interests of the people, and that trades unions, being legal institutions, are entitled to the recognition of all classes. -- This manifesto was issued during the Great Maritime Strike of 1890, a pivotal moment of industrial warfare that ended in the crushing defeat of the unions by the employers and the colonial governments. The realization that industrial action alone could not defeat the power of the State ("The Army") led the Labor movement to a historic decision: they must form a political party to capture the State. This moment ("Class War") was the "Cause" that necessitated the political definition of Labor.','Plane_2_Definition.md',239,'Corrupt union bosses are no less toxic to Australians than tobacco and gambling addictions.',1,'"One Nation Puts Blowtorch to Toxic CFMEU," onenation.org.au, 16 August 2024','onenation','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation.txt','fabricated',0.1429,'URL: https://www.onenation.org.au/policies (redirects to /issues)',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(82,2,'Definition','What.Why.Effect','The Quiet Life',0.5,-0.5,'HIT','**(What.Why.Effect) The Quiet Life (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Many people feel that they can''t indulge that essential Australian characteristic of speaking out and speaking up because the risk of speaking out is simply too great. They feel demonised and condescended." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Quiet Life: The home is the foundation of sanity and sobriety; it is the indispensable condition of continuity; its health determines the health of society as a whole. -- Robert Menzies, founder of the Liberal Party, delivered this radio broadcast in 1942 to define his constituency: a middle class that was "nameless and unadvertised." He rejected the explicit class warfare of the Left and the luxury of the rich, focusing instead on the private "Home" as the center of the nation. He argued that the ultimate purpose of politics ("The Why") was to protect this private sphere from state interference.','Plane_2_Definition.md',247,'Many people feel that they can''t indulge that essential Australian characteristic of speaking out and speaking up because the risk of speaking out is simply too great. They feel demonised and condescended.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Many people feel that they can’t indulge that essential Australian characteristic of speaking out and speaking up because the risk of speaking out is simply too great.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(83,2,'Definition','What.How.Who','The Faceless Men',-0.4,0.5,'FAIL','**(What.How.Who) The Faceless Men (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "That''s why I have to be in total control of it. And I''m not going to allow you to drag me down through some member of a branch." -National Press Club Address, Cockatoo transcript[^npc26]','The Faceless Men: 36 unknown men, not elected to Parliament nor responsible to the people. -- Alan Reid, a political journalist for *The Daily Telegraph*, wrote this damning caption in 1963 under a photo of Labor''s Federal Executive meeting outside a Canberra hotel while MPs waited inside for instructions. The definition of Power in the Labor Party (and implicitly the Unions) involves the "Party Conference"—unelected delegates instructing the elected MPs. This critique defined the "How" of party discipline. It suggests that the definition of Australian democracy includes influential, unelected power brokers behind the throne.','Plane_2_Definition.md',257,'That''s why I have to be in total control of it. And I''m not going to allow you to drag me down through some member of a branch.',1,'National Press Club Address, Cockatoo transcript','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',0.8667,'I am not opposed to renewable energy, but if it’s the saviour of the energy crisis, and if it’s profitable, why would Government have to prop it up?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(84,2,'Definition','What.How.What','The Referendum',0.8,0.4,'HIT','**(What.How.What) The Referendum (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "Two years ago, I tried to secure a national plebiscite on immigration numbers. As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Referendum: The proposed law... shall be submitted to the electors in each State and to the electors in the Northern Territory and the Australian Capital Territory. -- This clause establishes the only mechanism by which the Constitution can be changed: the direct vote of the people. Unlike the US (where legislatures ratify amendments) or the UK (where Parliament is supreme), the Australian Definition can only be rewritten by the "Electors." It enforces a "conservative democracy," as the people have historically voted "No" to 36 of 44 proposals, viewing the document as a "People''s Law" that politicians should not tamper with.','Plane_2_Definition.md',277,'Two years ago, I tried to secure a national plebiscite on immigration numbers. As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(85,2,'Definition','What.How.Where','The Secret Ballot',0.9,0.6,'HIT','**(What.How.Where) The Secret Ballot (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "The only way to ensure every vote comes from a properly registered voter, voting once under their own name is to ask for voter ID." -Senator Pauline Hanson, onenation.org.au[^onenation_voterid]','The Secret Ballot: The voter shall retire alone to some unoccupied compartment of the polling booth... and there in private and without interruption mark his ballot paper. -- This clause, introduced in Victoria in 1856, invented the "Australian Ballot," a technology of democracy that spread to the world (including the US). Before this, voting was often public and subject to intimidation by landlords and bosses. By enclosing the voter in a physical "compartment" of silence, the colonial reformers invented the modern private citizen, creating a "Where" (The Booth) that was sacred and totally free from social pressure.','Plane_2_Definition.md',285,'The only way to ensure every vote comes from a properly registered voter, voting once under their own name is to ask for voter ID.',1,'Senator Pauline Hanson, onenation.org.au','onenation_voterid','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_voterid.txt','verified',1.0,'The only way to ensure every vote comes from a properly registered voter, voting once under their own name is to ask for voter ID.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(86,2,'Definition','What.How.Why','Preferential Voting',0.7,0.5,'HIT','**(What.How.Why) Preferential Voting (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "One Nation and its leadership have one overriding ambition -- to give this great country back its wealth which has been stolen from us by bad policy and arrogant policy misfits." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Preferential Voting: The candidate who receives the fewest first preference votes shall be excluded, and each ballot paper counted to him shall be counted to the candidate next in the order of the voter''s preference. -- This technical **calculus**, introduced in 1918, is the "operating system" of Australian elections. Unlike "First Past the Post" (UK/US), which forces a choice between two evils, Preferential Voting allows the voter to express a complex "Why." It forces parties to compete for the "second preferences" of minor parties, pushing politics toward the center. It ensures that the winner is the "least objected to" candidate rather than just the most popular.','Plane_2_Definition.md',293,'One Nation and its leadership have one overriding ambition',1,'- to give this great country back its wealth which has been stolen from us by bad policy and arrogant policy misfits." -National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation and its leadership have one overriding ambition – to give this great country back its wealth which has been stolen from us by bad policy and arrogant policy misfits.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(87,2,'Definition','What.How.How','The Royal Commission',0.7,0.6,'HIT','**(What.How.How) The Royal Commission (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Two people brought these innocent children in to the world and it is their shared responsibility to care for those children, regardless of whether they are still in a relationship or separated... We know the system is broken now instead of the same old rhetoric let''s make a real change." -Dissenting Report of Senator Pauline Hanson, Deputy Chair, Joint Select Committee on Australia''s Family Law System, aph.gov.au[^tvfy]','The Royal Commission: To inquire into and report upon... -- The Royal Commission is the "Inquisitor" of the Australian Definition. It is the method of last resort when the political system fails to find the truth. Endowed with coercsive powers greater than a court, it allows the Crown to bypass the Parliament and interrogate reality directly. From organized crime (Costigan) to banking (Hayne), it is the "How" by which the state cleanses itself.','Plane_2_Definition.md',301,'Two people brought these innocent children in to the world and it is their shared responsibility to care for those children, regardless of whether they are still in a relationship or separated... We know the system is broken now instead of the same old rhetoric let''s make a real change.',1,'Dissenting Report of Senator Pauline Hanson, Deputy Chair, Joint Select Committee on Australia''s Family Law System, aph.gov.au','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.098,'They Vote For You Senator Pauline Hanson voting record overview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(88,2,'Definition','What.How.Cause','The Census',0.5,0.3,'FAIL','**(What.How.Cause) The Census (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "My vision for Australia is that we''re all Australians regardless of race, colour, creed. We''re all treated as Australians equally on an individual needs basis, not based on race." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Census: The Statistician shall... take the Census... on the day appointed by proclamation. -- The Census is the "Great Stocktake" of the Australian Definition. Every five years, the Commonwealth attempts to map every single person, home, and religion in the continent. It is the scientific "Cause" of policy, providing the raw data for the distribution of seats (Nexus) and money (Fiscal Equalization). It represents the obsession of the utilitarian state with "Knowing" its population down to the last digit.','Plane_2_Definition.md',309,'My vision for Australia is that we''re all Australians regardless of race, colour, creed. We''re all treated as Australians equally on an individual needs basis, not based on race.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','paraphrased',0.6774,'It’s as good an explanation as any for the earthquake that is changing the political landscape in Australia and other countries.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(89,2,'Definition','What.How.Effect','The Spill',-0.3,0.6,'HIT','**(What.How.Effect) The Spill (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "At the moment, government of this country has become a victim of the ideology of people who have failed you in the past and will fail you again." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Spill: I was elected by the people of Australia to do a job. I was not elected by the factional leaders of the Australian Labor Party. -- Kevin Rudd, who had led Labor to a landslide victory in 2007, delivered this bitter assessment in the courtyard of Parliament House after being deposed by his deputy, Julia Gillard. The "coups" of the 2010s demonstrated a brutal reality of the Australian system: a Prime Minister can be removed overnight by a vote of 60 people in a party room, regardless of their standing with 20 million voters. His speech highlighted the disconnect between the "presidential" expectations of the public and the "parliamentary" reality of the factions.','Plane_2_Definition.md',317,'At the moment, government of this country has become a victim of the ideology of people who have failed you in the past and will fail you again.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'At the moment, government of this country has become a victim of the ideology of people who have failed you in the past and will fail you again.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(90,2,'Definition','What.Cause.Who','The Prophet',0.7,0.8,'HIT','**(What.Cause.Who) The Prophet (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.8): HIT.** **Quote:** "Many people feel afraid to make their views heard. As a result, civil debate is paralysed. And the media are complicit in amplifying this fear." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Prophet: The time has come... the question of the Federation of the Australian Colonies should be formally dealt with. -- Sir Henry Parkes, the "Father of Federation," delivered this call to arms in the Tenterfield School of Arts on 24 October 1889, igniting the final movement toward union. Standing in a border town crippled by tariffs, he argued that the "time had come" to dispense with colonial jealousies. He provides the "Who" of the Cause—not a lawyer or a general, but a poet-politician who could see the nation before it existed.','Plane_2_Definition.md',327,'Many people feel afraid to make their views heard. As a result, civil debate is paralysed. And the media are complicit in amplifying this fear.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'But what a national tragedy, indeed a disgrace, that many people feel afraid to make their views heard.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(91,2,'Definition','What.Cause.What','The Imperial Act',0.3,-0.4,'HIT','**(What.Cause.What) The Imperial Act (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Imperial Act: Be it enacted by the Queen''s most Excellent Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Lords Spiritual and Temporal, and Commons, in this present Parliament assembled. -- This legal formula, the standard preamble of a British Act of Parliament, is the technical "What" that created Australia. It reveals that the Definition is legally a gift from the Imperial Parliament, passed in London. It strips the origin of any revolutionary romance—there was no Declaration of Independence signed in blood, only a "Schedule" attached to a British statute.','Plane_2_Definition.md',335,'We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'One, The Fair Go, was fabricated ("We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag" does not appear anywhere in this speech) and has been replaced in Plane_4_Drive.md with the genuine "Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals..." line from this same transcript.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(92,2,'Definition','What.Cause.Where','The Stockade',0.8,0.9,'HIT','**(What.Cause.Where) The Stockade (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.9): HIT.** **Quote:** "...designed to avoid controversy, history, or truth. They''ve even buried or erased: the Eureka Stockade, the Pinjarra Massacre, the Anzacs'' legacy in global conflict, the systems that underpin law and order." -Statements by Senators: Education, Senate Hansard, 3 September 2025[^tvfy]','The Stockade: We swear by the Southern Cross to stand truly by each other, and fight to defend our rights and liberties. -- Peter Lalor, the rebel leader, administered this oath to the miners at the Eureka Stockade in Ballarat in 1854, beneath the Southern Cross flag. It was the only armed rebellion in Australian history, a fight against unjust taxation and for the right to vote. While the stockade was crushed by the military, the "Spirit of Eureka" became the spiritual "Where" of Australian democracy—the place where the common man finally stood up.','Plane_2_Definition.md',343,'...designed to avoid controversy, history, or truth. They''ve even buried or erased: the Eureka Stockade, the Pinjarra Massacre, the Anzacs'' legacy in global conflict, the systems that underpin law and order.',1,'Statements by Senators: Education, Senate Hansard, 3 September 2025','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.0938,'They Vote For You Senator Pauline Hanson voting record overview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(93,2,'Definition','What.Cause.Why','The Slump',0.0,-0.5,'HIT','**(What.Cause.Why) The Slump (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Ford and Holden closed their factories more than a decade ago, for one simple reason, the cost of production. The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Slump: Within five months from that date no less than 13 of those companies had suspended payment. -- The Great Depression of the 1890s was the economic catastrophe that shattered the confidence of the colonies. The collapse of the banks and the end of the long boom proved that the small, competing colonial economies were vulnerable. It provided the "Why" of necessity—the realization that "United we stand, divided we fall" was not just poetry, but economic fact. It forced the merchants and bankers to back Federation as a survival strategy.','Plane_2_Definition.md',351,'Ford and Holden closed their factories more than a decade ago, for one simple reason, the cost of production. The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Ford and Holden closed their factories more than a decade ago, for one simple reason, the cost of production.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(94,2,'Definition','What.Cause.How','The Corowa Plan',0.9,0.7,'HIT','**(What.Cause.How) The Corowa Plan (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "One Nation supports greater participation by voters in the processes of democracy, empowering the people to set the policy agenda instead of governments, activists, and the media. We will introduce a mechanism enabling citizen-initiated referendums and plebiscites so that Queenslanders'' views on matters of public interest are heard loudly and clearly." -One Nation Queensland, "Enhancing Democracy" policy platform[^onenation]','The Corowa Plan: That in the opinion of this Conference the Legislature of each Australasian colony should pass an Act providing for the election of representatives. -- This resolution, moved by Dr. John Quick at the Corowa People''s Conference, saved Federation when the politicians had let it stall. It proposed a radical "How": take the process out of the hands of the Parliaments and give it to the People. It called for a directly elected Convention to write the Constitution, which would then be ratified by a direct Referendum. It invented the democratic process that created the nation.','Plane_2_Definition.md',359,'One Nation supports greater participation by voters in the processes of democracy, empowering the people to set the policy agenda instead of governments, activists, and the media. We will introduce a mechanism enabling citizen-initiated referendums and plebiscites so that Queenslanders'' views on matters of public interest are heard loudly and clearly.',1,'One Nation Queensland, "Enhancing Democracy" policy platform','onenation','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation.txt','fabricated',0.3269,'Visible content: "LOWERING PRICES FOR HOUSEHOLDS, BUSINESSES AND INDUSTRIES / READ MORE" (a single policy tile headline, likely the first of several tiles that load individually via JS as the user scrolls; the accessibility/text-extraction pass only captured this one visible tile).',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(95,2,'Definition','What.Cause.Cause','State Socialism',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(What.Cause.Cause) State Socialism (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "We want more gas, more oil, and more energy to drive our economy forward, pay down our debts, and secure our energy future... This will be the first time that Australians have a genuine ownership stake in the nation''s natural resources." -One Nation Gas Policy launch, onenation.org.au, 9 June 2026[^onenation_anwic]','State Socialism: Socialism without doctrines. -- Albert Métin, a French observer, used this phrase to describe the Australian experiment at the turn of the century. He saw a society that had implemented radical socialist policies—minimum wages, pensions, state railways, public ownership—not because of Marxist ideology ("Doctrines"), but because of simple pragmatism. The "Cause" of the Australian Definition was a practical desire to use the State to fix problems, without the baggage of European theory.','Plane_2_Definition.md',379,'We want more gas, more oil, and more energy to drive our economy forward, pay down our debts, and secure our energy future... This will be the first time that Australians have a genuine ownership stake in the nation''s natural resources.',1,'One Nation Gas Policy launch, onenation.org.au, 9 June 2026','onenation_anwic','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_anwic.txt','verified',1.0,'We want more gas, more oil, and more energy to drive our economy forward, pay down our debts, and secure our energy future.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(96,2,'Definition','What.Cause.Effect','Federation Day',0.6,0.4,'HIT','**(What.Cause.Effect) Federation Day (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "That was the best outcome of the Voice to Parliament referendum. It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Federation Day: The crowds in all the city''s thoroughfares, the procession that threaded its way through the dense masses of the populace... -- The "Effect" of the Cause was the inauguration of the Commonwealth in Centennial Park, Sydney, on 1 January 1901. This journalistic account captures the moment the Definition became reality—the physical manifestation of the idea in "dense masses" and "military display." It marks the transition from the theoretical "Cause" (The Movement) to the concrete "Effect" (The Nation).','Plane_2_Definition.md',387,'That was the best outcome of the Voice to Parliament referendum. It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(97,2,'Definition','What.Effect.Who','The Anzac',0.6,0.7,'HIT','**(What.Effect.Who) The Anzac (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "I want to say something clearly, because Australians deserve honesty and respect. At ANZAC Day services across the country, some booed the Welcome to Country. I don''t support that. ANZAC Day should never be disrupted. It''s a sacred day to honour the men and women who gave everything for our country." -Pauline Hanson, public statement (2026)[^wiki]','The Anzac: Anzac stood, and still stands, for reckless valour in a good cause, for enterprise, resourcefulness, fidelity, comradeship, and endurance that will never own defeat. -- Charles Bean, the official war historian, wrote this definition to capture the "Spirit of Anzac" forged at Gallipoli. He was not just recording history; he was deliberately manufacturing a national mythology. He elevated the soldier—the "digger"—to the status of a secular saint, arguing that the true Australian character was not found in the cities, but in the test of battle.','Plane_2_Definition.md',397,'I want to say something clearly, because Australians deserve honesty and respect. At ANZAC Day services across the country, some booed the Welcome to Country. I don''t support that. ANZAC Day should never be disrupted. It''s a sacred day to honour the men and women who gave everything for our country.',1,'Pauline Hanson, public statement (2026)','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','paraphrased',0.8113,'[[ 155 ]]() In response, the Attorney-General George Brandis , who is tasked with giving advice on national security legislation, gave an "emotional" speech calling Hanson''s stunt "an appalling thing to do" and advised Hanson "to be very very careful of the offense you may do to the religious sensibilities of other Australians", to which both Labor and Greens Senators gave a standing ovation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(98,2,'Definition','What.Effect.What','The Lucky Country',0.3,-0.4,'HIT','**(What.Effect.What) The Lucky Country (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "I may be only a fish and chip shop lady, but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Lucky Country: Australia is a lucky country run mainly by second rate people who share its luck. -- Donald Horne, the social critic, wrote this ironically in his massive 1964 bestseller. He was attacking the complacency of the Menzies era, arguing that Australia''s wealth came from geology ("Luck") rather than talent or innovation, and that its leaders were mediocre provincials. The phrase was misunderstood and embraced as a compliment, proving Horne''s point about the nation''s lack of intellectual rigour.','Plane_2_Definition.md',417,'I may be only a fish and chip shop lady, but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I may be only ''a fish and chip shop lady'', but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(99,2,'Definition','What.Effect.Where','The Tyranny of Distance',0.0,-0.6,'HIT','**(What.Effect.Where) The Tyranny of Distance (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "If I can invite whom I want into my home, then I should have the right to have a say in who comes into my country." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Tyranny of Distance: Distance is as characteristic of Australia as mountains are of Switzerland. -- Geoffrey Blainey, the historian, coined this phrase to explain the fundamental determinant of the Australian experience. He argued that the "Where" (Geography) controlled the "What" (History). The immense distance from Europe created the "Cultural Cringe" and the "Fatal Shore" mentality, while the internal distance between the cities created the "Patchwork Economy" and the reliance on the State (to build the railways).','Plane_2_Definition.md',425,'If I can invite whom I want into my home, then I should have the right to have a say in who comes into my country.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Of course, I will be called racist but, if I can invite whom I want into my home, then I should have the right to have a say in who comes into my country.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(100,2,'Definition','What.Effect.Why','The Cultural Cringe',-0.4,-0.5,'HIT','**(What.Effect.Why) The Cultural Cringe (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I love this country. I''m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Cultural Cringe: Above our writers—and other artists—looms the intimidating mass of Anglo-Saxon culture. -- A.A. Phillips, the critic, invented this term in a *Meanjin* essay to describe the Australian inferiority complex. He observed that Australian intellectuals and artists instinctively assumed that the "Real Life" happened in London or New York, and that local products were necessarily inferior. It was the "Why" of the colonial mindset—a belief that the Definition of value was always "Over There."','Plane_2_Definition.md',445,'I love this country. I''m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'I’m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(101,2,'Definition','What.Effect.How','Mateship',0.7,0.4,'FAIL','**(What.Effect.How) Mateship (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Don''t expect a divisive Welcome to Country from me -- this beautiful country belongs to all Australians born here and those who have joined us." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Mateship: A practical man, rough and ready in his manners... ever willing to ''have a go'' at anything. -- Russel Ward captured the "Typical Australian" in his classic study of the bush legend. He defined the "How" of the character as a specific set of bush virtues: adaptability, egalitarianism, skepticism of authority, and above all, loyalty to the group ("Mateship"). While Ward admitted this was a "Legend" (most Australians lived in cities), he argued it was the "Effect" of the frontier on the national soul.','Plane_2_Definition.md',453,'Don''t expect a divisive Welcome to Country from me',1,'- this beautiful country belongs to all Australians born here and those who have joined us." -National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Don’t expect a divisive Welcome to Country from me - this beautiful country belongs to all Australian’s born here and those who have joined us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(102,2,'Definition','What.Effect.Cause','The Great Silence',-0.8,-0.6,'HIT','**(What.Effect.Cause) The Great Silence (υ: \-0.8, ψ: \-0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "ATSIC was dysfunctional, corrupt and rife with the nepotism and lack of accountability which still plagues the aboriginal industry today." -Senate Speech: Australia Must Oppose Voice to Parliament (2021)[^senate21voice]','Voice [First Nations Perspective]: The silence was not ours. We were silenced. -- Stanner identified the "Cult of Forgetfulness" as a colonial psychological defense, a convenient amnesia that allowed the settler to sleep at night on stolen land. But for Indigenous people, this "Silence" was actually a deafening cacophony of suppressed truth—massacres, child removals, and resistance battles that the white ear refused to hear. The history was never "forgotten" by those who lived it; it was actively buried by those who benefitted from it.','Plane_2_Definition.md',461,'ATSIC was dysfunctional, corrupt and rife with the nepotism and lack of accountability which still plagues the aboriginal industry today.',1,'Senate Speech: Australia Must Oppose Voice to Parliament (2021)','senate21voice','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate21voice.txt','verified',1.0,'ATSIC was dysfunctional, corrupt and rife with the nepotism and lack of accountability which still plagues the aboriginal industry today.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(103,2,'Definition','What.Effect.Cause','Voice \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.9,0.6,'FAIL','**(What.Effect.Cause) Voice \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "That was the best outcome of the Voice to Parliament referendum. It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Voice [First Nations Perspective]: The silence was not ours. We were silenced. -- Stanner identified the "Cult of Forgetfulness" as a colonial psychological defense, a convenient amnesia that allowed the settler to sleep at night on stolen land. But for Indigenous people, this "Silence" was actually a deafening cacophony of suppressed truth—massacres, child removals, and resistance battles that the white ear refused to hear. The history was never "forgotten" by those who lived it; it was actively buried by those who benefitted from it.','Plane_2_Definition.md',469,'That was the best outcome of the Voice to Parliament referendum. It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(104,2,'Definition','What.Effect.Effect','The Nanny State',0.4,-0.5,'FAIL','**(What.Effect.Effect) The Nanny State (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "One Nation will introduce nuclear energy. One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery -- grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even the government underwriting anything that sponsors the whole net zero hoax." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Nanny State: Individuals should be free to live their lives according to their values and their preferences. -- This modern libertarian critique highlights the ultimate "Effect" of the utilitarian definition (Hancock''s "Public Utility"). Because the State is defined as the provider of safety and happiness, it inevitably becomes the regulator of all behavior. From bicycle helmets to lockout laws, the Australian Definition prizes "Safety" over "Liberty." The "Effect" is a society that is incredibly safe, ordered, and bureaucratized—a "Nanny State" that wraps the citizen in cotton wool.','Plane_2_Definition.md',477,'One Nation will introduce nuclear energy. One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery',1,'- grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even the government underwriting anything that sponsors the whole net zero hoax." -National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery – grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even the government underwriting anything that sponsors the whole net zero hoax.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(105,3,'Land','Where.Who.Who','The Sunburnt Country',0.5,-0.4,'FAIL','**(Where.Who.Who) The Sunburnt Country (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.''... I worked for my land; no-one gave it to me." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Sunburnt Country: I love a sunburnt country, a land of sweeping plains, / Of ragged mountain ranges, of droughts and flooding rains. -- Dorothea Mackellar wrote this iconic poem while homesick in London, explicitly contrasting the "ordered woods" and "soft" beauty of England with the harsh, chaotic reality of Australia. It was an act of defiance, asserting that the "Terror" of the Australian landscape was not a defect but a feature to be loved with a "steady heart." She defined the land for the first time not as a failed Europe, but as a distinct, superior entity of "opal-hearted" intensity.','Plane_3_Land.md',5,'I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.''... I worked for my land; no-one gave it to me.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.'' Well, where the hell do I go?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(106,3,'Land','Where.Who.What','The Weird Melancholy',0.3,-0.5,'FAIL','**(Where.Who.What) The Weird Melancholy (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Time is running out... Wake up, Australia, before it is too late." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Weird Melancholy: The dominant note of Australian scenery is weird melancholy... The dweller in the wilderness acknowledges the subtle charm of this fantastic land of monstrosities. -- Marcus Clarke, the great colonial novelist, wrote this famous essay attempting to capture why the Australian bush felt so different to the European forest. He identified its "timelessness" and its "monstrosities" (strange flora/fauna) as evoking a specific mood of "Weird Melancholy" rather than traditional beauty. He argued that the scribblings of nature here were "hieroglyphs" that the European mind could not yet read, creating a sense of isolation and reflection.','Plane_3_Land.md',25,'Time is running out... Wake up, Australia, before it is too late.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Wake up, Australia, before it is too late.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(107,3,'Land','Where.Who.Where','The Never-Never',0.4,-0.3,'HIT','**(Where.Who.Where) The Never-Never (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "It belongs to farmers, not government transmission lines." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Never-Never: Called the Never-Never, the Maluka loved to say, because they who have lived in it and loved it, Never-Never voluntarily leave it. -- Jeannie Gunn (Mrs Aeneas Gunn) wrote this memoir about her life on Elsey Station in the remote Northern Territory, coining the term that became synonymous with the deep Outback. She reframed the empty interior not as a wasteland, but as a seductive, spiritual home that captures the soul of those who enter it. It suggests that once the "spell" of the bush is cast, civilization loses its appeal.','Plane_3_Land.md',45,'It belongs to farmers, not government transmission lines.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'It belongs to farmers, not government transmission lines.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(108,3,'Land','Where.Who.Why','The Red Steer',0.0,-0.6,'HIT','**(Where.Who.Why) The Red Steer (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Throw bloody climate change out of the window and let''s look at the pure facts on why we''ve had the bushfires." -Today Show interview, via SBS News (January 2020)[^wiki]','The Red Steer: The Red Steer is out of the pen. And none shall bar its way. -- The poet Will Ogilvie personified the Bushfire as "The Red Steer," a beast that breaks from its pen to trample the country. This idiom captures the terror of the "Fire Season," identifying combustion not as a chemical reaction but as a predatory monster that hunts the settler. It reflects the settler''s fear of the "elemental struggle" where their hard-won fences and homes can be erased in minutes.','Plane_3_Land.md',65,'Throw bloody climate change out of the window and let''s look at the pure facts on why we''ve had the bushfires.',1,'Today Show interview, via SBS News (January 2020)','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','paraphrased',0.8261,'In her address to the National Press Club on 17 June 2026, Hanson called climate change a "hoax", called for a ban on wind farm energy, incorrectly claimed the Clean Energy Finance Corporation had received $200 billion of taxpayers'' funding and claimed that One Nation''s policy for nuclear energy would be at the "world''s cheapest price", a claim contrary to modelling by the CSIRO on the cost of comparative energy production.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(109,3,'Land','Where.Who.How','The Drought',0.3,-0.6,'HIT','**(Where.Who.How) The Drought (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "I speak to struggling farmers everywhere, do they get subsidies?" -National Press Club Address (2026)[^netimes26]','The Drought: There is dust and drought on the plains far out where the water lay for weeks /  There''s a pitiful dam where a dyke should stretch and a tank where a lake should be. -- Lawson, the voice of the Bush, wrote this during the Federation Drought, describing the drying up of the land''s lifeblood. He captures the despair of the "pitiful dam," the insufficient human attempt to store water against the overwhelming aridity of the continent. It illustrates the failure of European methods ("where a lake should be") against Australian reality.','Plane_3_Land.md',85,'I speak to struggling farmers everywhere, do they get subsidies?',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','netimes26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/netimes26.txt','verified',0.9,'“The real tragedy is people are frightened of what will happen to them if they just speak up.”',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(110,3,'Land','Where.Who.Cause','The Spirit of Place',0.6,-0.3,'FAIL','**(Where.Who.Cause) The Spirit of Place (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Where the hell do I go? I was born here..." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Spirit of Place: The spirit of place is a great reality... The aboriginal spirit of the place... is always there. -- Lawrence identified that Australia possesses an ancient, indifferent power that predates colonial arrival. It is the "weight" of the continent that slowly transforms the occupier into something new.','Plane_3_Land.md',105,'Where the hell do I go? I was born here...',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.'' Well, where the hell do I go?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(111,3,'Land','Where.Who.Effect','The Primitive Area',0.8,0.5,'FAIL','**(Where.Who.Effect) The Primitive Area (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "[Documented action: Hanson''s Senate voting record, tracked over her full parliamentary career, shows consistent votes against conservation and land-protection measures alongside consistent support for coal and resource extraction expansion.]" -TheyVoteForYou, voting record[^tvfy]','The Primitive Area: Whether we like it or not, we hold our land in trust for our successors. -- Myles Dunphy was the father of the conservation movement in NSW, arguing for the creation of "Primitive Areas" (Wilderness) to be kept roadless and pristine. He recognized that the "Conquest" of the bush had gone too far and that the "Character" of the nation depended on saving the wild places from progress. He formulated the ethical duty to the future.','Plane_3_Land.md',125,'[Documented action: Hanson''s Senate voting record, tracked over her full parliamentary career, shows consistent votes against conservation and land-protection measures alongside consistent support for coal and resource extraction expansion.]',1,'TheyVoteForYou, voting record','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.2581,'They Vote For You Senator Pauline Hanson voting record overview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(112,3,'Land','Where.What.Who','The Squatter',-0.6,0.6,'HIT','**(Where.What.Who) The Squatter (υ: \-0.6, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "I don''t believe foreigners should own any housing in Australia or our farming land... My attitude is, I would stop them and I''d give you two years to sell your product. If you don''t, it will be repossessed by the government." -Interview, reported May 2026[^wiki]','The Squatter: I suppose we are to be favoured with a bunyip aristocracy... a rum keg of a New South Wales order of chivalry. -- Daniel Deniehy, a radical republican, delivered this withering insult to the "Squattocracy"—the wealthy landholders who sought to establish a hereditary peerage in New South Wales. He mocked their pretension, comparing them to the "Bunyip" (a mythical swamp monster), arguing that wealth stolen from the public lands did not confer nobility. It was the moment the "Right of Might" (Squatter) clashed with the idea of pure democracy.','Plane_3_Land.md',147,'I don''t believe foreigners should own any housing in Australia or our farming land... My attitude is, I would stop them and I''d give you two years to sell your product. If you don''t, it will be repossessed by the government.',1,'Interview, reported May 2026','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','verified',0.8864,'[[ 67 ]]() Speaking on her return to politics, she stated, "I have had all the major political parties attack me, been kicked out of my own party and ended up in prison, but I don''t give up." [[ 68 ]]() In October 2007, Hanson launched her campaign song, entitled "Australian Way of Life", which included the line, "Welcome everyone, no matter where you come from." [[ 69 ]]()',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(113,3,'Land','Where.What.What','The Void',-0.9,0.6,'HIT','**(Where.What.What) The Void (υ: \-0.9, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, the government has made available $1 billion for Aboriginals and Torres Strait Islanders as compensation for land they cannot claim under native title... Not one native title has been granted as I speak." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','The Void: It is imperative in today''s world that the common law should neither be, nor be seen to be, frozen in an age of racial discrimination. -- For 204 years, Australian sovereignty rested on the legal fiction of *Terra Nullius* (Land belonging to no one), a doctrine that assumed Indigenous people were too "barbarous" to own property. Justice Brennan''s historic judgement shattered this foundation, describing it as a "deceit" that could no longer be maintained by the common law. It was the moment the Law finally caught up with the Reality.','Plane_3_Land.md',167,'Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, the government has made available $1 billion for Aboriginals and Torres Strait Islanders as compensation for land they cannot claim under native title... Not one native title has been granted as I speak.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, the government has made available $1 billion for Aboriginals and Torres Strait Islanders as compensation for land they cannot claim under native title.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(114,3,'Land','Where.What.Where','Custodianship \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.9,0.6,'FAIL','**(Where.What.Where) Custodianship \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Claims for land based on Aboriginal mythology should have no more validity than a claim for land based on the tooth fairy." -"Indigenous claims to end under One Nation policy," onenation.org.au, 7 March 2025[^onenation_toothfairy]','Custodianship [First Nations Perspective]: We don''t own the land, the land owns us. -- The colonial legal fiction of *Terra Nullius* relied on the Western concept of "exclusionary property"—if you do not fence it, you do not own it. The Indigenous concept relies on "inclusionary custody"—the land owns you, and your right to it is measured by your obligation to protect it. The "Void" was a failure of colonial perception, not a reality of the landscape.','Plane_3_Land.md',183,'Claims for land based on Aboriginal mythology should have no more validity than a claim for land based on the tooth fairy.',1,'"Indigenous claims to end under One Nation policy," onenation.org.au, 7 March 2025','onenation_toothfairy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_toothfairy.txt','verified',1.0,'> "Claims for land based on Aboriginal mythology should have no more validity than a claim for land based on the tooth fairy."',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(115,3,'Land','Where.What.Why','The Crossing',0.4,0.7,'FAIL','**(Where.What.Why) The Crossing (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets? Why are we allowing our ports, utilities, services, agricultural land, and industries, to be acquired by foreigners of any nationality?" -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Crossing: We have at all events proved that they are traversable. -- Wentworth, along with Blaxland and Lawson, found the way across the Blue Mountains which had imprisoned the colony of Sydney for 25 years. His understated conclusion marked the end of the "Prison Phase" and the beginning of the "Expansion Phase." It unlocked the western plains, transforming the colony from a jail into an empire of grass.','Plane_3_Land.md',203,'Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets? Why are we allowing our ports, utilities, services, agricultural land, and industries, to be acquired by foreigners of any nationality?',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(116,3,'Land','Where.What.How','The Grid',0.4,0.5,'HIT','**(Where.What.How) The Grid (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Any water that is harvested in Queensland belongs to Queenslanders, and we must make sure we retain ownership and keep getting ongoing benefits from the completed infrastructure." -Media Release, senatorhanson.com.au (1 November 2019)[^wiki]','The Grid: I staked the main streets ninety-nine feet wide, and after having done so, I was ordered by the Governor to make them sixty-six feet wide; but upon my urging the Governor... he consented to let me have my will. -- Robert Hoddle laid out the "Hoddle Grid" of Melbourne with a military precision, insisting on massive 99-foot wide streets. His logic was practical—they had to be wide enough to turn a bullock team (10-12 pairs of oxen) and to prevent the spread of disease ("bad air"). This imposed a rigid, rational geometry (The Grid) onto the organic chaos of the bush, a symbol of the Colonial Will to Order.','Plane_3_Land.md',223,'Any water that is harvested in Queensland belongs to Queenslanders, and we must make sure we retain ownership and keep getting ongoing benefits from the completed infrastructure.',1,'Media Release, senatorhanson.com.au (1 November 2019)','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','paraphrased',0.6296,'In her 2016 maiden speech in the Senate, she said that "We are in danger of being swamped by Muslims who bear a culture and ideology that is incompatible with our own" and that they should " [go back to where [they] came from](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Go_back_to_where_you_came_from "Go back to where you came from") ", and called for banning Muslim migration.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:37');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(117,3,'Land','Where.What.Cause','The Crown',0.3,-0.4,'HIT','**(Where.What.Cause) The Crown (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "It doesn''t matter whether you think that Australia should be a republic or that Australia belongs only to Indigenous people; Australia is a constitutional monarchy that belongs to every Australian, Indigenous or not." -Senate Hansard, Motions: Censure, 27 September 2022[^hansard22crown]','The Crown: Reserving only to us such Timber as may be growing... and an annual Quit Rent of Bushel of wheat. -- The 1787 Instructions to Governor Phillip established the legal framework that "vested" all land in the British Crown upon settlement. Unlike the American model of clear freehold, Australian land tenure began with the assumption that the King was the "Paramount Lord" and the settler was a tenant. This legal DNA meant that the State was the source of all wealth and legitimacy from day one.','Plane_3_Land.md',243,'It doesn''t matter whether you think that Australia should be a republic or that Australia belongs only to Indigenous people; Australia is a constitutional monarchy that belongs to every Australian, Indigenous or not.',1,'Senate Hansard, Motions: Censure, 27 September 2022','hansard22crown','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/hansard22crown.txt','verified',1.0,'I remind them that it doesn''t matter whether you think Australia should be a republic or that Australia only belongs to Indigenous people, Australia is a constitutional monarchy that belongs to every Australian, Indigenous or not.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(118,3,'Land','Where.What.Effect','The Selector',0.5,0.6,'HIT','**(Where.What.Effect) The Selector (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake. They are waiting longer for their life-saving operation. The unemployment queues grow longer." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Selector: I met her on the Lachlan Side / A darling girl I thought her / And ere I left I swore I''d win / The free-selector''s daughter. -- The "Free Selector" was the small farmer encouraged by the Land Acts to break up the Squatter''s monopoly. Lawson''s poem romanticizes this figure, but the history is tragic; most selectors failed, beaten by the "Drought" and the "Bank." They represented the failed Jeffersonian ideal of a yeoman peasantry in a land suited only for industrial pastoralism.','Plane_3_Land.md',263,'High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake. They are waiting longer for their life-saving operation. The unemployment queues grow longer.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(119,3,'Land','Where.Where.Who','The Red Heart',0.0,-0.6,'FAIL','**(Where.Where.Who) The Red Heart (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "What I''ve been pushing for is the Bradfield Scheme that comes from North Queensland, the Herbert, Tully, and the Burdekin Rivers, to actually direct it inland. Flood inland Queensland, flow down to the Murray-Darling, and run it through." -Sky News "Paul Murray Live", republished onenation.org.au, 29 January 2019[^onenation_bradfield19]','The Red Heart: The heat as being so intense that his finger nails became brittle, and the ink dried on his pen almost before he had time to use it. -- Charles Sturt, the great inland explorer, wrote this upon reaching the Simpson Desert, realizing that the "Inland Sea" he sought was actually a "Dead Heart." His description of the intense heat (where nails fell out of boxes due to wood shrinkage and personal nails became brittle) defined the center of the continent as a hostile void. It destroyed the European hope for a fertile interior.','Plane_3_Land.md',285,'What I''ve been pushing for is the Bradfield Scheme that comes from North Queensland, the Herbert, Tully, and the Burdekin Rivers, to actually direct it inland. Flood inland Queensland, flow down to the Murray-Darling, and run it through.',1,'Sky News "Paul Murray Live", republished onenation.org.au, 29 January 2019','onenation_bradfield19','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_bradfield19.txt','fabricated',0.25,'PRIMARY URL: https://www.onenation.org.au/pauline-hanson-calls-for-construction-of-bradfield-and-ord-schemes-to-drought-proof-inland-australia/',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(120,3,'Land','Where.Where.What','Goyder''s Line',0.6,0.4,'HIT','**(Where.Where.What) Goyder''s Line (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "The modernised Bradfield Scheme could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world." -Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)[^senate20jm]','Goyder''s Line: Bare ground, destitute of grass and herbage... The change from the drought stricken country to that which has not suffered... is palpable to the eye from the nature of the country itself. -- George Goyder famously drew a line across the map of South Australia, separating the arable land from the pastoral leasehold. He observed that the vegetation itself—the "salt, blue, and other dwarf bushes"—marked the exact limit of reliable rainfall. His report warned that to farm beyond this line was to invite ruin, a warning that was tragically ignored by optimists who followed the "Rain follows the plough" myth.','Plane_3_Land.md',305,'The modernised Bradfield Scheme could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world.',1,'Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)','senate20jm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate20jm.txt','verified',1.0,'It could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(121,3,'Land','Where.Where.Where','The Saltbush',0.5,-0.3,'HIT','**(Where.Where.Where) The Saltbush (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** Disendorsed by the Liberal Party in 1996; convicted of electoral fraud and jailed in August 2003, with the conviction quashed on appeal after 11 weeks[^austlii03]; the original One Nation party deregistered in 2003; returned to the Senate in 2016; One Nation''s Senate representation grew from two seats to four, its equal-best result, at the 2025 federal election[^onenation_senategrowth25]. -Electoral and parliamentary record, 1996-2025[^wiki]','The Saltbush: The saltbush is the only thing that stands between the sheep and death. -- Lawson describes the hardy shrub of the interior, the Old Man Saltbush, which survives when the grass is gone. It is not beautiful, but it is stubbornly alive. It represents the vegetation''s retreat into pure function—storing water in its leaves, resisting the sun, offering sustenance only when all else has failed.','Plane_3_Land.md',325,'Disendorsed by the Liberal Party in 1996; convicted of electoral fraud and jailed in August 2003, with the conviction quashed on appeal after 11 weeks[^austlii03]; the original One Nation party deregistered in 2003; returned to the Senate in 2016; One Nation''s Senate representation grew from two seats to four, its equal-best result, at the 2025 federal election[^onenation_senategrowth25].',0,'Electoral and parliamentary record, 1996-2025','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','verified',0.8852,'One Nation won three seats in the Western Australian Legislative Council at the 2001 state election , but the electoral success of One Nation began to deteriorate after this point because the split-away of One Nation NSW began to spark further lack of party unity, and a series of gaffes by One Nation members and candidates, particularly in Queensland.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(122,3,'Land','Where.Where.Why','The River',0.0,-0.4,'HIT','**(Where.Where.Why) The River (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "We''ve allowed multinationals, we''ve allowed foreign ownership of the water licenses. Howard should never have separated water from land in 2004, and then on top of that with the Water Act, that has been the nail in the coffin." -Convoy to Canberra press interview, reported 2 December 2019[^2gb19]','The River: A broad and noble river... impossible to describe. -- Sturt''s awe upon discovering the Murray-Darling captures the promise of water in a thirsty land. However, Mitchell''s earlier disappointment upon finding inland rivers dry or disconnected captures the essential unreliability of Australian water. Unlike the steady flow of the Thames or Rhine, the Australian river is an "ephemeral" event—flooding one month, dry dust the next. It defies the definition of a highway.','Plane_3_Land.md',345,'We''ve allowed multinationals, we''ve allowed foreign ownership of the water licenses. Howard should never have separated water from land in 2004, and then on top of that with the Water Act, that has been the nail in the coffin.',1,'Convoy to Canberra press interview, reported 2 December 2019','2gb19','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/2gb19.txt','verified',1.0,'Howard should never have separated water from land in 2004, and then on top of that with the Water Act, that has been the nail in the coffin."',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(123,3,'Land','Where.Where.How','The Marsupial',0.6,0.4,'FAIL','**(Where.Where.How) The Marsupial (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It is clear what we stand for, One Nation under one flag and proudly Australian. We oppose entirely people coming into this country and bringing with them the troubles they have left behind." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Marsupial: An unbeliever in everything beyond his own reason might exclaim, ''Surely two distinct Creators must have been at work.'' -- Darwin recorded this thought in his diary after observing the strange "rat-kangaroos" and platypus in New South Wales. He was struck by the "strange character" of the Australian fauna compared to the rest of the world, realizing that they represented a completely divergent evolutionary path. It was one of the key observations that would later inform his theory of evolution—that isolation breeds difference.','Plane_3_Land.md',365,'It is clear what we stand for, One Nation under one flag and proudly Australian. We oppose entirely people coming into this country and bringing with them the troubles they have left behind.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'We oppose entirely people coming into this country and bringing with them the troubles they have left behind; coming to this country and ignoring our values, our language, our traditions, our dress and the fact that we are predominately a Judeo-Christian society.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(124,3,'Land','Where.Where.Cause','Gondwana',0.7,-0.3,'FAIL','**(Where.Where.Cause) Gondwana (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "This systemic imbalance has led to stalled development, lost investment, and deepening divisions in communities across Australia... Native Title claims... impose substantial legal costs, delays, and development restrictions on communities and individuals." -One Nation Senate petition, "Majority of Australia Under Native Title -- Enough is Enough," onenation.org.au, 2025[^onenation_nativetitle_petition]','Gondwana: It is the only continent that has not been engaged in a collision with another continent for over 200 million years. -- Flannery identifies the geological isolation of the continent as the primary driver of its uniqueness. As the raft of Gondwana drifted north, it carried a cargo of Cretaceous flora and fauna in "total isolation," allowing lineages to survive here that were wiped out elsewhere. This physical separation created a "life raft" effect, preserving the "Old World" while the rest of the planet changed.','Plane_3_Land.md',385,'This systemic imbalance has led to stalled development, lost investment, and deepening divisions in communities across Australia... Native Title claims... impose substantial legal costs, delays, and development restrictions on communities and individuals.',1,'One Nation Senate petition, "Majority of Australia Under Native Title -- Enough is Enough," onenation.org.au, 2025','onenation_nativetitle_petition','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_nativetitle_petition.txt','verified',1.0,'This systemic imbalance has led to stalled development, lost investment, and deepening divisions in communities across Australia.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(125,3,'Land','Where.Where.Effect','The Plague',-0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(Where.Where.Effect) The Plague (υ: \-0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "As Queensland and neighbouring states go through our summer months, a further explosion of cane toads are hatching, adding to the estimated 200 million already here in Australia." -Letter to PM Scott Morrison, reported by SBS News, 9 January 2019[^onenation]','The Plague: A noxious and insidious menace... a grey blanket. -- The introduction of the Rabbit in 1859 by Thomas Austin led to the fastest mammal spread in recorded history. The "Grey Blanket" is the recurring historical image used by settlers to describe the sheer mass of the infestation, which could strip a paddock bare in hours. It represents the collision of the "robust" European biology with the "fragile" Australian ecology.','Plane_3_Land.md',405,'As Queensland and neighbouring states go through our summer months, a further explosion of cane toads are hatching, adding to the estimated 200 million already here in Australia.',1,'Letter to PM Scott Morrison, reported by SBS News, 9 January 2019','onenation','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation.txt','fabricated',0.2857,'Visible content: "LOWERING PRICES FOR HOUSEHOLDS, BUSINESSES AND INDUSTRIES / READ MORE" (a single policy tile headline, likely the first of several tiles that load individually via JS as the user scrolls; the accessibility/text-extraction pass only captured this one visible tile).',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(126,3,'Land','Where.Why.Who','The Sun',0.0,0.4,'FAIL','**(Where.Why.Who) The Sun (υ: 0.0, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Rewiring the nation to build useless transmission lines and destroy prime agricultural land, billions of taxpayer dollars. This will end." -National Press Club Address, reported by The Nightly, June 2026[^npc26]','The Sun: Bringing closer and closer a trembling leaf till its veins and vastness were related to all things, from burning sun to his own burned hand. -- Patrick White, Australia''s Nobel Laureate, placed the Sun at the center of his metaphysical exploration of the continent. In *The Tree of Man*, the sun is not just a weather event but a "master" that brands the inhabitant, reducing the human to a "burned" creature. It defines the "Who" as a biological organism living under a radiation weapon.','Plane_3_Land.md',423,'Rewiring the nation to build useless transmission lines and destroy prime agricultural land, billions of taxpayer dollars. This will end.',1,'National Press Club Address, reported by The Nightly, June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Rewiring the nation to build useless transmission lines and destroy prime agricultural land, billions of taxpayer dollars.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(127,3,'Land','Where.Why.What','The Thirst',0.4,-0.5,'HIT','**(Where.Why.What) The Thirst (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export. Of course, basic environmental standards must be met, but they can''t be allowed to throttle our economy." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Thirst: I see again with haggard eyes, / The thirsty land, the wasted flood; / Unpeopled plains beyond the skies, / And precious streams that run to mud. -- Lawson''s poem captures the central tragedy of the Australian climate: the precious water that "runs to sea" (mud) while the land thirsts. He describes the "haggard eyes" of the settler staring at the sky, waiting for rain that doesn''t come. It articulates the deep psychological anxiety of a people living on the driest inhabited continent, where "The Thirst" is a permanent condition.','Plane_3_Land.md',443,'The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export. Of course, basic environmental standards must be met, but they can''t be allowed to throttle our economy.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(128,3,'Land','Where.Why.Where','The Wet and The Dry',0.0,-0.4,'FAIL','**(Where.Why.Where) The Wet and The Dry (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "As far as I know there''s no cane toads in Canberra yet. Get the inquiry up in Queensland, get the real people who know what to do about this." -Reported by SBS News, 9 January 2019[^onenation]','The Wet and The Dry: The whole vast territory seemed never to be anything for long but either a swamp during Wet Season or a hard-baked desert during the Dry. -- Herbert''s classic novel of the Northern Territory captures the violent binary of the tropical climate. In the North, the European "Four Seasons" do not exist; there is only the "Wet" (Mobility Impossible) and the "Dry" (Mobility Possible). This cycle dictates the life of the station, the movement of cattle, and the sanity of the people.','Plane_3_Land.md',463,'As far as I know there''s no cane toads in Canberra yet. Get the inquiry up in Queensland, get the real people who know what to do about this.',1,'Reported by SBS News, 9 January 2019','onenation','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation.txt','fabricated',0.3333,'Visible content: "LOWERING PRICES FOR HOUSEHOLDS, BUSINESSES AND INDUSTRIES / READ MORE" (a single policy tile headline, likely the first of several tiles that load individually via JS as the user scrolls; the accessibility/text-extraction pass only captured this one visible tile).',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(129,3,'Land','Where.Why.Why','The Flood',0.4,0.5,'FAIL','**(Where.Why.Why) The Flood (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation and help the poor farmers out there that are on their knees? What about the watering Australia program to bring the water down from the Territory?" -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Flood: Yarri and Jacky Jacky... saved 69 lives. -- The early explorers were baffled to find "inland seas" where there had been deserts only months before. The Gundagai flood of 1852, where local Indigenous heroes saved white settlers, illustrates the "Surge" event that connects the continent. The Flood flushing the dead salt from the heart and bringing life (birds, fish). It is the violent corrective to the Drought.','Plane_3_Land.md',479,'What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation and help the poor farmers out there that are on their knees? What about the watering Australia program to bring the water down from the Territory?',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation and help the poor farmers out there that are on their knees?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(130,3,'Land','Where.Why.How','The Wind',0.0,0.3,'FAIL','**(Where.Why.How) The Wind (υ: 0.0, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery -- grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even the government underwriting anything that sponsors the whole net zero hoax." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Wind: Waves of the Southern Ocean have the entire circumference of the world in which to build their energy. -- Hughes describes the "Roaring Forties," the westerly winds that batter the southern coast of Tasmania and Victoria. These winds brought the ships (The First Fleet) but also wrecked them (The Shipwreck Coast). They represent the kinetic connection between Australia and the bottom of the world.','Plane_3_Land.md',499,'One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery',1,'- grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even the government underwriting anything that sponsors the whole net zero hoax." -National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery – grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even the government underwriting anything that sponsors the whole net zero hoax.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(131,3,'Land','Where.Why.Cause','The Oscillation (El Niño)',0.0,-0.4,'FAIL','**(Where.Why.Cause) The Oscillation (El Niño) (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Put bluntly, these figures derive because of one policy, above all others, the hoax of global warming which is now climate change. It has produced an increase in energy costs which has taken Australia into energy poverty." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Oscillation (El Niño): Core of my heart, my country! / Land of the Rainbow Gold, / For flood and fire and famine, / She pays us back threefold. -- The "Southern Oscillation" (El Niño/La Niña) is the physical engine of the continent''s variance. Unlike Europe or America where rainfall is relatively consistent, Australia lives in the violent cycle of flood and drought. This engine is global, linking the fate of a farmer in NSW to the temperature of the ocean off Peru.','Plane_3_Land.md',519,'Put bluntly, these figures derive because of one policy, above all others, the hoax of global warming which is now climate change. It has produced an increase in energy costs which has taken Australia into energy poverty.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Put bluntly, these figures derive because of one policy, above all others, the hoax of global warming which is now climate change.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(132,3,'Land','Where.Why.Effect','The Windmill',0.7,0.6,'FAIL','**(Where.Why.Effect) The Windmill (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Bring it from the Ord, water inland, Australia from the Ord Scheme as well, and bring water inland and flush out our river systems. That''s it. That''s what I''d be doing." -Sky News "Paul Murray Live" interview transcript, republished onenation.org.au, 29 January 2019[^onenation]','The Windmill: But the artesian waters flow / And make the grassy spaces / Where stock-in-hand may stay and grow. -- While the windmill is the icon, the reality is the drilling. Paterson''s poem celebrates the "Song" of the water rising from the depths to save the stock. The Windmill is the machine that taps this "subterranean river," allowing the station to exist where no surface water flows. It is the technological triumph over the hostile climate.','Plane_3_Land.md',539,'Bring it from the Ord, water inland, Australia from the Ord Scheme as well, and bring water inland and flush out our river systems. That''s it. That''s what I''d be doing.',1,'Sky News "Paul Murray Live" interview transcript, republished onenation.org.au, 29 January 2019','onenation','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation.txt','fabricated',0.3824,'If a node cites [^onenation] generically for "party platform," that''s fine as a hub reference, but any specific claim should be re-pointed to the actual policy sub-page that contains it.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(133,3,'Land','Where.How.Who','Songlines \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.9,0.6,'FAIL','**(Where.How.Who) Songlines \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "This group and others are trying to lock Australians out of their own country not for genuine cultural or heritage reasons, but out of racist hatred and pure, naked greed... Under our policy, no new submissions will be accepted while all existing claims under native title or cultural heritage laws will be reviewed." -Senator Pauline Hanson, "Indigenous claims to end under One Nation policy," onenation.org.au, 7 March 2025[^onenation_toothfairy]','Songlines [First Nations Perspective]: The singing wire. -- The "Tyranny of Distance" is a European concept born of the need for centralization. The First Nations realized that the continent was a network, not a void. The Songlines were a continental accumulation of knowledge that made distance navigable. You were never "lost" if you knew the song. The "Singing Wire" of the telegraph was just a physical echo of the metaphysical web that already existed.','Plane_3_Land.md',561,'This group and others are trying to lock Australians out of their own country not for genuine cultural or heritage reasons, but out of racist hatred and pure, naked greed... Under our policy, no new submissions will be accepted while all existing claims under native title or cultural heritage laws will be reviewed.',1,'Senator Pauline Hanson, "Indigenous claims to end under One Nation policy," onenation.org.au, 7 March 2025','onenation_toothfairy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_toothfairy.txt','verified',1.0,'> "This group and others are trying to lock Australians out of their own country not for genuine cultural or heritage reasons, but out of racist hatred and pure, naked greed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(134,3,'Land','Where.How.What','The Dingo Fence',-0.3,0.6,'HIT','**(Where.How.What) The Dingo Fence (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "I rise to speak in support of this motion. I''ve been speaking about illegal refugees coming to the Australian border since the late 1990s -- since my first time in parliament. So I''m not new to the topic at all." -Motion: Instrument of Designation of the Republic of Nauru as a Regional Processing Country, Senate Hansard, 7 February 2023[^tvfy]','The Dingo Fence: For a dingo being born on the wrong side... it''s a death sentence. -- Stretching 5,614 kilometers from Queensland to the Great Australian Bight, this structure is a physical manifestation of the war between the squatter and the wild. It literally bisects the continent into two biological zones: the "Safe" zone (Sheep/Civilization) and the "Wild" zone (Cattle/Dingoes). It is a colossal attempt to legislate nature through wire.','Plane_3_Land.md',581,'I rise to speak in support of this motion. I''ve been speaking about illegal refugees coming to the Australian border since the late 1990s',1,'- since my first time in parliament. So I''m not new to the topic at all." -Motion: Instrument of Designation of the Republic of Nauru as a Regional Processing Country, Senate Hansard, 7 February 2023','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.04,'- Against increasing the GST.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(135,3,'Land','Where.How.Where','The Highway',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(Where.How.Where) The Highway (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "One Nation will always protect prime agricultural land. It belongs to farmers, not government transmission lines." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Highway: I dipped my feet, and washed my face and hands in the sea, as I promised the late Governor Sir Richard McDonnell I would do if I reached it. -- The Stuart Highway follows the exact footsteps of the explorer John McDouall Stuart, who finally reached the Indian Ocean after six furious attempts to cross the continent from South to North. His track became the route of the Telegraph, then the Railway, and finally the bitumen highway. "The Track" is the scar of his perseverance etched into the earth.','Plane_3_Land.md',601,'One Nation will always protect prime agricultural land. It belongs to farmers, not government transmission lines.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation will always protect prime agricultural land.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(136,3,'Land','Where.How.Why','The Dam',0.7,0.7,'HIT','**(Where.How.Why) The Dam (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "What about long-term-vision projects, infrastructure projects like roads and rail? What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation?" -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Dam: The greatest single project in our history... it is a plan for the whole nation, belonging to no one state, nor to any group or section. -- The Snowy Mountains Scheme was the moonshot of Australian engineering, boring through mountains to reverse the flow of the Snowy River inland to irrigate the Murray-Darling. Chifley saw it as nation-building, a project that belonged to "no one state." It employed 100,000 migrants, birthing multicultural Australia.','Plane_3_Land.md',621,'What about long-term-vision projects, infrastructure projects like roads and rail? What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation?',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation and help the poor farmers out there that are on their knees?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(137,3,'Land','Where.How.How','The Air',0.8,0.7,'HIT','**(Where.How.How) The Air (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "Why aren''t we duplicating the Bruce Highway from Brisbane to Cairns for tourism and freight? Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country." -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Air: To provide a mantle of safety... no matter how remote. -- John Flynn ("Flynn of the Inland") used the invention of the aeroplane and the pedal radio to create the Royal Flying Doctor Service. He declared that no pioneer should be beyond the reach of medical care, creating a "mantle of safety" that covered the entire outback. It was the first time aviation was used for a purely humanitarian system on a continental scale.','Plane_3_Land.md',641,'Why aren''t we duplicating the Bruce Highway from Brisbane to Cairns for tourism and freight? Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country.',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country; hydro power like the Tully-Millstream project—why aren’t we doing these projects?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(138,3,'Land','Where.How.Cause','The Railway',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(Where.How.Cause) The Railway (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Another infrastructure scheme worth analysing is Project Iron Boomerang, which would see the construction of steel smelters near the coalfields of Central Queensland and near the iron ore mines of Western Australia, with the two areas connected by rail." -Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)[^senate20jm]','The Railway: Struth! If that is all that is coming aboard, we''ll have to call it the Afghan Express. -- The "Ghan" (from Afghan Express) follows the route of the old camel trains into the Red Centre. This joke by a railwayman upon seeing a lone Afghan cameleer board the train became the name of the greatest rail journey on the continent. It represents the transition from animal power (Camels) to steam/diesel (Iron), opening the interior to heavy industry.','Plane_3_Land.md',661,'Another infrastructure scheme worth analysing is Project Iron Boomerang, which would see the construction of steel smelters near the coalfields of Central Queensland and near the iron ore mines of Western Australia, with the two areas connected by rail.',1,'Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)','senate20jm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate20jm.txt','verified',1.0,'Another infrastructure scheme worth analysing is Project Iron Boomerang, which would see the construction of steel smelters near the coalfields of Central Queensland and near the iron ore mines of Western Australia, with the two areas connected by rail.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(139,3,'Land','Where.How.Effect','The Pipeline',0.7,0.8,'HIT','**(Where.How.Effect) The Pipeline (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.8): HIT.** **Quote:** "We want more gas, more oil, and more energy to drive our economy forward, pay down our debts, and secure our energy future." -One Nation Gas Policy launch, onenation.org.au, 9 June 2026[^onenation]','The Pipeline: The Coolgardie scheme is all right and I could finish it if I got a chance and protection from misrepresentation but there''s no hope for that now. -- C.Y. O''Connor committed suicide on the beach at Fremantle, driven to despair by critics of his "Golden Pipeline" which pumped water 560km uphill to the desert goldfields. It was an engineering impossibility that worked, but it cost the creator his life. It remains the lifeline of Kalgoorlie.','Plane_3_Land.md',681,'We want more gas, more oil, and more energy to drive our economy forward, pay down our debts, and secure our energy future.',1,'One Nation Gas Policy launch, onenation.org.au, 9 June 2026','onenation','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation.txt','fabricated',0.1739,'Visible content: "LOWERING PRICES FOR HOUSEHOLDS, BUSINESSES AND INDUSTRIES / READ MORE" (a single policy tile headline, likely the first of several tiles that load individually via JS as the user scrolls; the accessibility/text-extraction pass only captured this one visible tile).',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(140,3,'Land','Where.Cause.Who','The Miner',0.6,0.7,'HIT','**(Where.Cause.Who) The Miner (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Miner: We swear by the Southern Cross to stand truly by each other and fight to defend our rights and liberties. -- The Eureka Rebellion was a rare moment where the "Digger" (Miner) stood up against the "Crown" (Government). Swearing by the stars of the southern sky, they established the archetype of the independent, democratic rebel. This event is often cited as the birth of Australian democracy, forging a link between the "Earth" (Digging) and "Rights."','Plane_3_Land.md',703,'We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'One, The Fair Go, was fabricated ("We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag" does not appear anywhere in this speech) and has been replaced in Plane_4_Drive.md with the genuine "Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals..." line from this same transcript.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(141,3,'Land','Where.Cause.What','The Gold',0.5,0.5,'HIT','**(Where.Cause.What) The Gold (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Countries like Japan are making more money in excise tax out of ships with our gas on them, around $3 billion, than we do." -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Gold: Welcome Stranger! -- Kalgoorlie''s "Golden Mile" and discoveries like the "Welcome Stranger" represent the staggering mineral wealth hidden beneath the arid crust. This concentration of gold funded the federation of the nation and established the Australian economy as one based on "Luck" (Geology) rather than "Industry" (Manufacturing). It literally paved the streets of the cities.','Plane_3_Land.md',723,'Countries like Japan are making more money in excise tax out of ships with our gas on them, around $3 billion, than we do.',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'Countries like Japan are making more money in excise tax out of ships with our gas on them, around $3 billion, than we do.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(142,3,'Land','Where.Cause.Where','The Shield',0.5,-0.3,'HIT','**(Where.Cause.Where) The Shield (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "I''ve got cane farmers across Queensland, who want a code of conduct. Nothing else -- no money, just surety for their industry, which employs tens of thousands of Australian workers." -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Shield: One of the oldest stable crusts on the planet. -- The Pilbara Craton (Shield) is the physical basement of the continent. While Europe was still forming, this land was already ancient. This immense age means the soils are leached of nutrients (hence the tough flora) but rich in stable minerals like iron ore. It is the "Quiet Earth," devoid of recent volcanic fury.','Plane_3_Land.md',743,'I''ve got cane farmers across Queensland, who want a code of conduct. Nothing else',1,'- no money, just surety for their industry, which employs tens of thousands of Australian workers." -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'I’ve got cane farmers across Queensland, who want a code of conduct.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(143,3,'Land','Where.Cause.Why','The Uranium',-0.3,0.5,'HIT','**(Where.Cause.Why) The Uranium (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I rise to speak in support of nuclear energy in Australia. Chris Bowen is saying it would take many years to establish nuclear energy in Australia, as if this is an excuse for not doing it." -Matters of Public Importance: Nuclear Energy, Senate Hansard, 4 December 2023[^tvfy]','The Uranium: Digging right through the stomach of the lizard... sickness country. -- Indigenous law prohibits the disturbance of "Sickness Country," often associated with the Rainbow Serpent sleeping underground. Modern science reveals these sites coincide with Uranium deposits (Ranger, Olympic Dam). The "Why" of the taboo is a deep time warning about the danger of the "poison fire" (Radioactivity) hidden in the earth.','Plane_3_Land.md',763,'I rise to speak in support of nuclear energy in Australia. Chris Bowen is saying it would take many years to establish nuclear energy in Australia, as if this is an excuse for not doing it.',1,'Matters of Public Importance: Nuclear Energy, Senate Hansard, 4 December 2023','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.0278,'They Vote For You Senator Pauline Hanson voting record overview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(144,3,'Land','Where.Cause.How','The Opencut',-0.2,0.7,'HIT','**(Where.Cause.How) The Opencut (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "Let''s look at the pure facts... a build-up of the fuel over a period of time -- 30-plus years." -SBS News interview, 13 January 2020[^tvfy]','The Opencut: An immense scar on the face of the earth... visible from space. -- The Fimiston Open Pit (Super Pit) is a hole so vast it consumes the horizon, a negative monument to Australian industry. It represents the industrial method of extracting the "Lode" where the earth is not "worked" but removed entirely. It is the inverse of the mountain, a cathedral of emptiness.','Plane_3_Land.md',783,'Let''s look at the pure facts... a build-up of the fuel over a period of time',1,'- 30-plus years." -SBS News interview, 13 January 2020','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.0556,'- Against increasing the GST.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(145,3,'Land','Where.Cause.Cause','The Impact',0.0,-0.3,'FAIL','**(Where.Cause.Cause) The Impact (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.'' Well, where the hell do I go? I was born here, and so were my parents and children... I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Impact: The risk to Earth would no longer be a matter of chance. -- The Australian landscape preserves ancient "Star Wounds" like the Acraman Crater because the shield is so stable. Discovered by Williams and confirmed by Shoemaker, these craters remind us that the "Cause" of the geography is partly extraterrestrial. The land bears the scars of deep time collisions that elsewhere have been erased by erosion.','Plane_3_Land.md',803,'I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.'' Well, where the hell do I go? I was born here, and so were my parents and children... I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(146,3,'Land','Where.Cause.Effect','The Wealth',0.3,-0.4,'HIT','**(Where.Cause.Effect) The Wealth (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export. We will never be able to do without coal and gas. We should encourage the investment in them and provide power to homes and business." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Wealth: Australia is a lucky country run mainly by second rate people who share its luck. It lives on other people''s ideas, and, although its ordinary people are adaptable, most of its leaders (in all fields) so lack curiosity about the events that surround them that they are often taken by surprise. -- Horne''s biting critique famously attributed Australia''s prosperity not to its intelligence, but to its "Luck"—its vast natural resources and distance from trouble. He argued that this easy wealth made the leadership lazy and "second rate," as they did not need to innovate to survive. They just had to dig.','Plane_3_Land.md',823,'The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export. We will never be able to do without coal and gas. We should encourage the investment in them and provide power to homes and business.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(147,3,'Land','Where.Effect.Who','The Suburbanite',0.5,-0.3,'HIT','**(Where.Effect.Who) The Suburbanite (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "People here are quite happy to live this lifestyle. They don''t have to get up, get in the car, go to work. People have to provide roofs over their own heads, not rely on the government to provide them." -Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)[^senate20jm]','The Suburbanite: Unreality: frank and proud artificiality... you can never afford a good home but you can always afford another nice feature. -- Robin Boyd identified that despite the myth of the "Bushman," the actual Australian is a dedicated suburbanite. The "Who" of the result is a person living in a brick veneer bungalow, creating one of the most urbanized (yet low density) nations on earth. The "Legend" is the Bush; the "Reality" is the Suburb.','Plane_3_Land.md',845,'People here are quite happy to live this lifestyle. They don''t have to get up, get in the car, go to work. People have to provide roofs over their own heads, not rely on the government to provide them.',1,'Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)','senate20jm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate20jm.txt','verified',1.0,'They don’t have to get up, get in the car, go to work and travel an hour to work like most other Australians have to do.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(148,3,'Land','Where.Effect.What','The Sprawl',0.3,-0.4,'HIT','**(Where.Effect.What) The Sprawl (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "We cannot be a multicultural society. We are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural. Australians must live under the one cultural umbrella." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Sprawl: Most Australians choose to live in suburbs... Many writers condemn this choice [but] it is probably intelligent. -- Australian cities are defined by their "Sprawl"—low-density housing stretching for endless kilometers. Hugh Stretton famously defended this choice against the critics, arguing that the Australian preference for a "quarter-acre block" was a rational response to the abundance of land. It allows for a private garden and space, but it relies entirely on the car (The Highway) and consumes the bush at a voracious rate.','Plane_3_Land.md',865,'We cannot be a multicultural society. We are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural. Australians must live under the one cultural umbrella.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'We are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(149,3,'Land','Where.Effect.Where','The Coast',0.4,-0.3,'HIT','**(Where.Effect.Where) The Coast (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets? Why are we allowing our ports, utilities, services, agricultural land, and industries, to be acquired by foreigners of any nationality? It is foolhardy to sell our water, agricultural land -- our food source!" -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Coast: I christened it the Boomerang Coast because of its shape, and pointed out that it held less than one-tenth of the nation''s area... and yet it held eight of every ten people. -- Blainey observed that the vast majority of Australians live in a boomerang-shaped arc on the south-east coast. We cling to the edge of the continent, looking outwards to the sea rather than inwards to the "Red Heart." The "Where" of the result is a thin green crescent of civilization surrounding a vast, empty core.','Plane_3_Land.md',885,'Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets? Why are we allowing our ports, utilities, services, agricultural land, and industries, to be acquired by foreigners of any nationality? It is foolhardy to sell our water, agricultural land',1,'- our food source!" -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(150,3,'Land','Where.Effect.Why','The Lifestyle',0.5,0.3,'HIT','**(Where.Effect.Why) The Lifestyle (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "I love this country. I''m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Lifestyle: One little piece of earth with a house and a garden which is ours... into which no stranger may come against our will. -- Menzies articulated the Australian Dream not as wealth or empire, but as the privacy of the home. The "Why" of the Australian project became the pursuit of this "Lifestyle"—independence, ownership, and leisure. It is the "California of the South," focused on the specialized pursuit of happiness in the sun.','Plane_3_Land.md',905,'I love this country. I''m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'I’m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(151,3,'Land','Where.Effect.How','The BBQ',0.7,0.4,'HIT','**(Where.Effect.How) The BBQ (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "We will never be able to do without coal and gas. We should encourage the investment in them and provide power to homes and business, as we once did, at the world''s cheapest price." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The BBQ: Barbecue smoke is rising... a heat-shimmer of sauces. -- The Barbecue is the central ritual of the Australian "Lifestyle." It brings the domestic sphere outdoors, mediating the relationship between the House and the Bush. It is egalitarian (The Democracy Sausage), informal, and meant to build connections. It is the altar of the suburban religion.','Plane_3_Land.md',925,'We will never be able to do without coal and gas. We should encourage the investment in them and provide power to homes and business, as we once did, at the world''s cheapest price.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'We should encourage the investment in them and provide power to homes and business, as we once did, at the world’s cheapest price.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(152,3,'Land','Where.Effect.Cause','The Quarantine',-0.4,-0.5,'HIT','**(Where.Effect.Cause) The Quarantine (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "One Nation has always supported a strong biosecurity and quarantine regime to protect farmers and the environment." -Pauline Hanson''s One Nation, "Agriculture" policy platform[^sa_onenation_agriculture]','The Quarantine: Insulated from external threats... a fortress. -- Blainey argued that our isolation acted as a "Fortress," protecting the high standard of living from the "teeming masses" of the world. This created a "Quarantine" mentality, evident in the White Australia Policy and modern border protection. The "Cause" of the lifestyle is the strict exclusion of the Other.','Plane_3_Land.md',945,'One Nation has always supported a strong biosecurity and quarantine regime to protect farmers and the environment.',1,'Pauline Hanson''s One Nation, "Agriculture" policy platform','sa_onenation_agriculture','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/sa_onenation_agriculture.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation has always supported a strong biosecurity and quarantine regime to protect farmers and the environment.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(153,3,'Land','Where.Effect.Effect','The Future',0.7,0.5,'FAIL','**(Where.Effect.Effect) The Future (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "One Nation will do its best to change this country''s direction; to re-assert its values; to honour its traditions; to reinforce that we are one nation under one flag." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Future: You see, psychologically, Australia must understand it has to live in the region around it. Australia must find its security in Asia; it cannot find its security from Asia. -- Keating articulated the final "Effect" of our location: we are a western nation permanently anchored in the Asian hemisphere. Our future depends on reconciling our "History" (British) with our "Geography" (Asian). We cannot remain a fortress forever; we must engage.','Plane_3_Land.md',965,'One Nation will do its best to change this country''s direction; to re-assert its values; to honour its traditions; to reinforce that we are one nation under one flag.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation will do its best to change this country’s direction; to re-assert its values; to honour its traditions; to reinforce that we are one nation under one flag; and my Party will put Australia back on the path to prosperity, security, independence and freedom.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(154,4,'Drive','Why.Who.Who','The Volunteer',0.9,0.8,'FAIL','**(Why.Who.Who) The Volunteer (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.8): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Taxpayers will still fund some of the ABC''s operations in regional, rural, and remote areas where there is a lack of commercial media." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Volunteer: For nearly two hours I kept this up until most of the danger had passed. It was the most terrible experience of my life. I would not part with that blanket now for anything. -- The Volunteer is the active agent of Australian drive, most visible in the Country Fire Authority (CFA) and State Emergency Service (SES). This figure emerges during the "Season of Fire" or "Season of Flood," contributing millions of unpaid hours to protect the collective. Black Friday 1939 was the crucible that forged the modern volunteer identity—71 souls lost, leading directly to the creation of the CFA. It represents the "Quiet Australian" who acts without expectation of reward, mobilizing instantly when the community is threatened.','Plane_4_Drive.md',5,'Taxpayers will still fund some of the ABC''s operations in regional, rural, and remote areas where there is a lack of commercial media.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Taxpayers will still fund some of the ABC’s operations in regional, rural, and remote areas where there is a lack of commercial media.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced (ABC regional-funding line); body sentence rewritten',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(155,4,'Drive','Why.Who.What','The Bludger',-0.6,-0.5,'HIT','**(Why.Who.What) The Bludger (υ: \-0.6, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** Hanson''s Senate voting record shows sustained opposition to welfare expansion, a pattern she frames publicly as targeting rorters and scammers rather than the vulnerable. -TheyVoteForYou, voting record on welfare[^tvfy]','The Bludger: The term ''dole bludger'' refers to those who exploit unemployment benefits while avoiding work. -- The "Bludger" (originally from 1856 London slang for a pimp who beat and robbed his prostitute''s clients with a bludgeon) arrived in Australia by 1882 and by 1900 meant any lazy parasite. Labor Minister Clyde Cameron popularized "dole bludger" in the 1970s, crystallizing the supreme antagonist of the Australian work ethic. It represents the violation of the reciprocal contract that underpins the entire society.','Plane_4_Drive.md',25,'Hanson''s Senate voting record shows sustained opposition to welfare expansion, a pattern she frames publicly as targeting rorters and scammers rather than the vulnerable.',0,'TheyVoteForYou, voting record on welfare','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','paraphrased',0.24,'TITLE: Pauline Hanson - Voting Record Overview','fixed_legacy','Header converted from fabricated quote to documented paraphrase',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(156,4,'Drive','Why.Who.Where','The Knocker',-0.4,-0.3,'HIT','**(Why.Who.Where) The Knocker (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australians aren''t buying this crap from the political establishment and its media supporters anymore." -SBS News[^sbsnpc]','The Knocker: Australia is a lucky country run mainly by second-rate people who share its luck. It lives on other people''s ideas. -- The Knocker is the critic who polices the boundaries of success. Distinct from the "Cutters" of Tall Poppy Syndrome (the mechanism), the Knocker is the *agent*—Donald Horne himself became the supreme knocker when he wrote Australia''s most famous piece of self-criticism. Often misread as praise, his judgment was actually a devastating assessment of mediocre leadership. Keith Dunstan identified "Knocking" as a national sport, a reflex to ensure no one gets "too big for their boots."','Plane_4_Drive.md',45,'Australians aren''t buying this crap from the political establishment and its media supporters anymore.',1,'SBS News','sbsnpc','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/sbsnpc.txt','verified',1.0,'"Australians aren''t buying this crap from the political establishment and its media supporters anymore," she said.','verified_legacy','"Australians aren''t buying this crap..." confirmed',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(157,4,'Drive','Why.Who.Why','The Digger',0.7,0.5,'HIT','**(Why.Who.Why) The Digger (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "They know you''ve come after me, even happy to see me put in prison. They know what you''ve been saying about me and many of them no longer believe you." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Digger: Mateship meant everything. -- The Digger is the stoic agent of endurance. Unlike the Volunteer who acts in crisis, or the Bludger who avoids action, the Digger "sticks it out" through the grind. This character was forged in the trenches of Gallipoli and the mud of the Somme, defined not by victory, but by an inability to give up. He is the secular saint of the culture, proving that suffering is the highest form of work.','Plane_4_Drive.md',65,'They know you''ve come after me, even happy to see me put in prison. They know what you''ve been saying about me and many of them no longer believe you.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'They know what you’ve been saying about me and many of them no longer believe you.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced ("they know you''ve come after me...")',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(158,4,'Drive','Why.Who.How','The Gambler',-0.2,0.5,'FAIL','**(Why.Who.How) The Gambler (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','The Gambler: Yeah, I didn''t have enough on it. -- The Gambler represents the fatalistic agent of drive. Bart Cummings—the "Cups King" with 12 Melbourne Cup victories—encapsulated the gambler''s psyche: even in triumph, the regret is for not betting more. From the Two-Up rings of the goldfields to the "Pokies" of existing clubs, the Gambler relies on "The Toss" rather than the plan. It acknowledges that in a land of drought and fire, outcome is often divorced from effort.','Plane_4_Drive.md',85,'In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(159,4,'Drive','Why.Who.Cause','The Battler',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(Why.Who.Cause) The Battler (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges... Some call it persistence and tenacity... I call it standing up and fighting for what you believe in and not allowing the bastards to grind you down." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Battler: The struggle of the man who ''slogs away'' against the odds. -- The Battler is the moral agent of hardship. Unlike the "victim," the Battler fights back, usually against "The Banks," "The Government," or "The Drought." In the 1990s, John Howard weaponized this archetype ("Howard''s Battlers") to capture the working-class vote, framing them as the "forgotten people" of the suburbs. Use of the term implies a person who is losing, but refuses to surrender.','Plane_4_Drive.md',105,'It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges... Some call it persistence and tenacity... I call it standing up and fighting for what you believe in and not allowing the bastards to grind you down.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges - of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner - to find myself here.','fixed_legacy','Old quote fabricated (not in the real speech), replaced with genuine "not allowing the bastards to grind you down" passage',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(160,4,'Drive','Why.Who.Effect','The Larrikin',0.4,0.3,'HIT','**(Why.Who.Effect) The Larrikin (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "Please explain?" -Response to Tracey Curro, Sixty Minutes, Channel Nine (1996)[^wiki]','The Larrikin: Such is life. -- The Larrikin is the skeptical agent of drive. From the inner-city gangs of the 1890s to the "Crocodile Dundee" figure, the Larrikin uses humour and irreverence to subvert authority. Ned Kelly''s fatalistic "Such is life" encapsulates the Larrikin''s acceptance of consequences while refusing to bow to the system. He is the trickster who proves that the rules are arbitrary.','Plane_4_Drive.md',125,'Please explain?',1,'Response to Tracey Curro, Sixty Minutes, Channel Nine (1996)','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','verified',1.0,'* _Pauline Hanson: Please Explain!_','fixed_legacy','Quote confirmed genuine; venue attribution corrected from generic "Media doorstop" to the real Sixty Minutes/Tracey Curro interview',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(161,4,'Drive','Why.What.Who','The Fair Go',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Why.What.Who) The Fair Go (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','The Fair Go: The standard... must be... a condition of frugal comfort estimated by current human standards. -- The "Fair Go" is the supreme object of Australian morality. Justice Higgins codified it in 1907 by ruling that a "Fair and Reasonable Wage" was not determined by market forces (what companies could pay) but by human need (what a man needed to feed a family). It established the "Living Wage" as a right, ensuring that the economy served the citizen, not the other way around.','Plane_4_Drive.md',147,'Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions.','fixed_legacy','Old quote fabricated ("one law for all, one language" not in the real speech, that''s a different Mateship quote); replaced with genuine "Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals..."',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(162,4,'Drive','Why.What.What','The Weekend',0.8,0.4,'HIT','**(Why.What.What) The Weekend (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "The majority of the public do not want a cut to penalty rates on the weekend, you''ve got my support. I''ve listened and this is what you want and I will not support any cuts to the penalty rates." -SBS News, "Hanson calls off Senate voting strike," 2017[^sbspenalty17]','The Weekend: Eight hours labour, eight hours recreation, eight hours rest. -- Australia was the first place in the world to win the Eight Hour Day (1856). The "Week-end" became a sacred object of time—a distinct zone partitioned from the "Work-week." It is the temporal location of the "Real Life" (Sport, BBQ, Beach). It represents the victory of the laborer over the clock, defining freedom not as the right to work, but the right to stop.','Plane_4_Drive.md',167,'The majority of the public do not want a cut to penalty rates on the weekend, you''ve got my support. I''ve listened and this is what you want and I will not support any cuts to the penalty rates.',1,'SBS News, "Hanson calls off Senate voting strike," 2017','sbspenalty17','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/sbspenalty17.txt','verified',1.0,'"The majority of the public do not want a cut to penalty rates on the weekend, you''ve got my support," she said.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(163,4,'Drive','Why.What.Where','The Home',0.5,0.4,'HIT','**(Why.What.Where) The Home (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "If you make a change to negative gearing, investment will move away from housing." -National Press Club Address, reported by New England Times, 17 June 2026[^netimes26]','The Home: The home is the foundation of sanity and sobriety; it is the indispensable condition of continuity. -- "The Great Australian Dream" is the ownership of a detached house on a quarter-acre block. Menzies identified this "Home" not just as shelter, but as the political and moral unit of the nation ("Stake in the country"). It is the physical object towards which almost all Australian financial drive is directed. It serves as the primary mechanism for transferring wealth across generations and securing belonging in a migrant nation.','Plane_4_Drive.md',187,'If you make a change to negative gearing, investment will move away from housing.',1,'National Press Club Address, reported by New England Times, 17 June 2026','netimes26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/netimes26.txt','verified',1.0,'“If you make a change to negative gearing, investment will move away from housing.”','verified_legacy','Negative-gearing quote confirmed against real npc26 transcript',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(164,4,'Drive','Why.What.Why','The Holiday',0.5,-0.2,'FAIL','**(Why.What.Why) The Holiday (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.2): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Pauline Hanson voted generally against increasing workplace protections." -TheyVoteForYou, voting record on workplace protections[^tvfy_workplaceprotect]','The Holiday: The religion of the long weekend. -- The "Right to a Holiday" is a non-negotiable object of Australian life. Whether it is "The Shack" on the coast or the "Trip Overseas," the Holiday is the reward for the "Year''s Slog." It is a period of "suspended responsibility" where the rules of the normal world are relaxed. It is the ritual acknowledgment that the environment is for enjoyment, not just production.','Plane_4_Drive.md',207,'Pauline Hanson voted generally against increasing workplace protections.',1,'TheyVoteForYou, voting record on workplace protections','tvfy_workplaceprotect','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy_workplaceprotect.txt','verified',1.0,'CITATION: "Pauline Hanson voted generally against increasing workplace protections", They Vote For You','fixed_legacy','Fabricated "lazy"/dismissal-laws sentence removed; header itself not independently re-fetched',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(165,4,'Drive','Why.What.How','The Ute',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(Why.What.How) The Ute (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Households are pushed into expensive technology and costly ''upgrades'' they never asked for." -"''Net zero'' is destroying Australia," Pauline Hanson''s One Nation, onenation.org.au[^onenation_netzero]','The Ute: A vehicle to go to church in on a Sunday and which can carry our pigs to market on Mondays. -- The Utility Vehicle (Ute) was invented in Australia to solve a specific problem: the duality of "Work" and "Respectability." It is the physical object that bridges the "Paddock" and the "Pew." It became a cult object (B&S Balls, Ute Musters), symbolizing the ability to transition between the rough and the smooth without changing tools.','Plane_4_Drive.md',227,'Households are pushed into expensive technology and costly ''upgrades'' they never asked for.',1,'"''Net zero'' is destroying Australia," Pauline Hanson''s One Nation, onenation.org.au','onenation_netzero','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_netzero.txt','verified',1.0,'Households are pushed into expensive technology and costly ‘upgrades’ they never asked for.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(166,4,'Drive','Why.What.Cause','The Pay Packet',0.7,0.4,'HIT','**(Why.What.Cause) The Pay Packet (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Pay Packet: A condition of frugal comfort estimated by current human standards. -- The "Pay Packet" (historically cash in an envelope) is the tangible proof of the "Fair Go." It is the "Living Wage." The drive is for a "Decent Wage"—enough to support a family in "Frugal Comfort." It connects the abstract economy to the concrete reality of the kitchen table, ensuring that finance is always viewed through the lens of domestic survival.','Plane_4_Drive.md',247,'High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake.','fixed_legacy','Old 457-visa quote fabricated (not in the real speech); replaced with genuine "multinationals, banks and big business" line',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(167,4,'Drive','Why.What.Effect','The Pension',0.8,0.3,'HIT','**(Why.What.Effect) The Pension (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "Welfare is not a right, unless you are aged or sick. It is a privilege paid for by hard-working Australians." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Pension: A right, not a charity. -- The Age Pension was one of the earliest social security measures in the world. It established the principle that the state has a duty to look after those who "built the nation" once they can no longer work. It is the distinct object of "Security" at the end of the "Drive." It changed the nature of aging from a family burden to a state responsibility.','Plane_4_Drive.md',267,'Welfare is not a right, unless you are aged or sick. It is a privilege paid for by hard-working Australians.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Welfare is not a right, unless you are aged or sick.','fixed_legacy','Old "foreign aid/pensioners" quote fabricated (not in the real speech); replaced with genuine "Welfare is not a right, unless you are aged or sick" line',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(168,4,'Drive','Why.Where.Who','The Pub',0.5,0.3,'HIT','**(Why.Where.Who) The Pub (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "So, food is dearer, housing is dearer, rents are dearer, there is your cost of living crisis." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Pub: A glimpse into Hades... a heaving roiling of male bodies. -- The Pub, specifically during the "Six O''Clock Swill," was the arena of "frantic consumption." It was a male-dominated, egalitarian space where status was checked at the door ("The Front Bar"). It is where Mateship is ritualized through the "Shout," forcing men to drink at the speed of the fastest drinker to maintain their standing in the group.','Plane_4_Drive.md',289,'So, food is dearer, housing is dearer, rents are dearer, there is your cost of living crisis.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'So, food is dearer, housing is dearer, rents are dearer, there is your cost of living crisis.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced with real verified cost-of-living line, earlier this session',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(169,4,'Drive','Why.Where.What','The Beach',0.6,0.3,'HIT','**(Why.Where.What) The Beach (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "Remember what sparked the riots in Cronulla: Muslims attacking Australian women for wearing bikinis at the beach in a hot Australian summer." -Senate Hansard, Statements by Senators, 24 June 2026[^oa_cronulla]','The Beach: Swim between the flags. -- The Beach is the edge of the continent (The Fringe). "Between the Flags" is the only rule in a space of hedonism. It is the democratic playground—the sand is common land. It represents the rejection of the "Bush" (Work) for the "Surf" (Play), turning the national orientation outward towards the ocean rather than inward towards the desert.','Plane_4_Drive.md',309,'Remember what sparked the riots in Cronulla: Muslims attacking Australian women for wearing bikinis at the beach in a hot Australian summer.',1,'Senate Hansard, Statements by Senators, 24 June 2026','oa_cronulla','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/oa_cronulla.txt','verified',1.0,'Remember what sparked the riots in Cronulla: Muslims attacking Australian women for wearing bikinis at the beach in a hot Australian summer.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(170,4,'Drive','Why.Where.Where','Country',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Why.Where.Where) Country (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I was born here, and so were my parents and children. I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Country: We are part of the land and the land is part of us. -- For the First Nations, "Country" is not just a place but a living, feeling entity with which they are in a reciprocal relationship. It is the "Where" that speaks. Unlike the European concept of land as property, Country is a family member that requires active care. This shifts the context of the drive from "Gambling on Land" to "Caring for Land," establishing that the deepest connection to the continent is not economic but spiritual and biological.','Plane_4_Drive.md',329,'I was born here, and so were my parents and children. I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(171,4,'Drive','Why.Where.Why','The Club',0.4,-0.2,'HIT','**(Why.Where.Why) The Club (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.2): HIT.** **Quote:** Hanson''s Senate voting record shows sustained opposition to mandatory pre-commitment and other poker-machine harm-reduction reforms affecting the clubs that host them. -TheyVoteForYou, voting record on gambling reform[^tvfy]','The Club: The Price of Liberty is Eternal Vigilance. -- The RSL (Returned and Services League) Club and the Leagues Club are the "Community Living Rooms." They are vast, subsidized spaces funded by "Pokies" (Poker Machines). The RSL holds the sacred memory (The Shrine) and the cheap meal (The Roast). They function as secular churches, providing ritual, community, and sustenance in the vast, atomized sprawl of suburbia.','Plane_4_Drive.md',349,'Hanson''s Senate voting record shows sustained opposition to mandatory pre-commitment and other poker-machine harm-reduction reforms affecting the clubs that host them.',0,'TheyVoteForYou, voting record on gambling reform','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','paraphrased',0.24,'TITLE: Pauline Hanson - Voting Record Overview','fixed_legacy','**User-caught fabrication** — old `[^senate18prot]` RSL/bowls quote confirmed fabricated by direct fetch, replaced',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(172,4,'Drive','Why.Where.How','The Shed',0.5,0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Where.How) The Shed (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "I support helping women, but, no doubt, I will be the only woman today speaking for the most oppressed and neglected minority in Australia: men... In Australia men are severely overrepresented in suicides, prison, homelessness and unemployment. What is being done to close these enormous gaps? Nothing." -Senate Hansard, Matters of Urgency: Gender Equality, 8 March 2023[^oa_menminority]','The Shed: Men don''t talk face to face; they talk shoulder to shoulder. -- The Backyard Shed (and the modern "Men''s Shed" movement) is the arena of "Pottering" and "Invention." It is the male sanctuary away from the "Home" (Domestic sphere). It is where "Bricolage" (Making do) happens, allowing the man to regain a sense of mastery that may be denied in the workplace.','Plane_4_Drive.md',369,'I support helping women, but, no doubt, I will be the only woman today speaking for the most oppressed and neglected minority in Australia: men... In Australia men are severely overrepresented in suicides, prison, homelessness and unemployment. What is being done to close these enormous gaps? Nothing.',1,'Senate Hansard, Matters of Urgency: Gender Equality, 8 March 2023','oa_menminority','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/oa_menminority.txt','verified',1.0,'I support helping women, but, no doubt, I will be the only woman today speaking for the most oppressed and neglected minority in Australia: men.','fixed_legacy','**User-caught mismatch** — retheme to Men''s Sheds/male-isolation, new source verified and archived',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(173,4,'Drive','Why.Where.Cause','The Field',0.6,0.6,'HIT','**(Why.Where.Cause) The Field (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Since 1996, I have had a battle with the ABC." -Senate Hansard, Broadcasting Legislation Amendment Bill debate, 13 September 2017[^oa_abcbattle]','The Field: The most famous cricket cap in the world. -- The Sports Field (MCG, Gabba) is the arena of "Proxy War." Sport is not a game; it is the primary way Australia asserts its sovereignty and worth to the world. The "Baggy Green" is the sacred vestment. It allows the nation to dominate the "Mother Country" (England) and the "New Empire" (USA) on a level playing field.','Plane_4_Drive.md',389,'Since 1996, I have had a battle with the ABC.',1,'Senate Hansard, Broadcasting Legislation Amendment Bill debate, 13 September 2017','oa_abcbattle','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/oa_abcbattle.txt','verified',1.0,'Let me tell you, Mr Acting Deputy President, since 1996, I have had a battle with the ABC—not all of the journalists but most of them.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(174,4,'Drive','Why.Where.Effect','The Mall',-0.2,0.3,'FAIL','**(Why.Where.Effect) The Mall (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** One Nation''s platform states it will pursue a tax regime that ensures multinational businesses pay their fair share of tax while operating in Australia. -"Multinational Taxation," onenation.org.au[^onenation_tax]','The Mall: Buying goods in shops everywhere is a human activity. -- The Shopping Mall (Westfield) has replaced the High Street and the Church. It is the air-conditioned arena of "Consumerism." It is the "New Town Square" for the suburban sprawl. It provides a sanitized, climate-controlled environment where the harshness of the Australian climate is completely excluded.','Plane_4_Drive.md',409,'One Nation''s platform states it will pursue a tax regime that ensures multinational businesses pay their fair share of tax while operating in Australia.',0,'"Multinational Taxation," onenation.org.au','onenation_tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_tax.txt','verified',0.96,'We will maintain our opposition to the reintroduction of death duties and pursue a tax regime that ensures multi-national businesses pay their fair share of tax while operating within Australia."','unchecked_legacy','Header itself not independently re-fetched; separately, a *proposed but never-inserted* "supermarket duopoly" replacement quote was checked and confirmed fabricated/misattributed (see Sources_Verification_Checklist)',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(175,4,'Drive','Why.Why.Who','Mateship',0.7,0.5,'FAIL','**(Why.Why.Who) Mateship (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','Mateship: To let down your mates... would be worse than death. -- Recursive Mateship is not just the "Bond" (Plane 1); it is the "Terror." In the historical conditions of the bush or the trench, Mateship was a survival pact where the failure of one threatened the life of all. It is the fear of exclusion that drives the behavior, creating a hyper-vigilance against letting the side down. In the Changi camps or the SAS patrol, the drive is not "Patriotism" or "Ideology," but the desperate fear of failing the person standing next to you.','Plane_4_Drive.md',427,'To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag.','verified_legacy','Header quote confirmed verbatim genuine; body quote-marks also fixed to real phrasing',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(176,4,'Drive','Why.Why.What','Tall Poppy Syndrome',-0.4,0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Why.What) Tall Poppy Syndrome (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "This is a stunt and the people out there are fed up with this." -Response to Senate censure motion, reported by SBS News[^sbscensure]','Tall Poppy Syndrome: Tall Poppies... to be cut down. -- This is the active "Cutting mechanism" of the culture, distinct from the passive "Knocker." It is the swift, collective removal of anyone who claims "Status" or "Superiority" above their station. It is the enforcement of humility through ridicule, ensuring that the social landscape remains flat. If you grow too tall, you insult the collective and must be harvested to restore the symmetry of the field.','Plane_4_Drive.md',447,'This is a stunt and the people out there are fed up with this.',1,'Response to Senate censure motion, reported by SBS News','sbscensure','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/sbscensure.txt','verified',1.0,'Hanson dismissed the censure as a political stunt tied to One Nation''s polling rise: "This is a stunt and the people out there are fed up with this...','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(177,4,'Drive','Why.Why.Where','Cultural Cringe',-0.5,-0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Why.Where) Cultural Cringe (υ: \-0.5, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "We don''t need the United Nations or foreign courts telling us how to run our country. We are a sovereign nation and we will make our own decisions." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Cultural Cringe: The estrangement of the Australian Intellectual. -- The "Cringe" is the internalized belief that "Real Life" happens elsewhere—usually in London, New York, or Paris. It results in the "Estrangement" of the best minds, who feel that local production is inherently second-rate compared to the "Metropolis." This drives the "Expat" phenomenon, where the Australian intellectual or artist flees the "Great Australian Silence" to find validation abroad, believing they cannot truly exist at home.','Plane_4_Drive.md',467,'We don''t need the United Nations or foreign courts telling us how to run our country. We are a sovereign nation and we will make our own decisions.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',0.8621,'We oppose entirely people coming into this country and bringing with them the troubles they have left behind; coming to this country and ignoring our values, our language, our traditions, our dress and the fact that we are predominately a Judeo-Christian society.','fixed_legacy','Fabricated UN/EU claim removed; header not independently re-fetched',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(178,4,'Drive','Why.Why.Why','She''ll Be Right',0.2,-0.6,'FAIL','**(Why.Why.Why) She''ll Be Right (υ: \+0.2, ψ: \-0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The real tragedy is people are frightened of what will happen to them if they just speak up." -National Press Club Address, reported by New England Times, 17 June 2026[^netimes26]','She''ll Be Right: Don''t worry about it. Just let us muck it up for you and leave us in peace. -- "She''ll be right" is the mantra of Apathy disguised as Optimism. It is the refusal to plan, the refusal to worry, and the refusal to strive for perfection in the face of complexity. It implies that "Good Enough" is the goal and that the universe will naturally correct any errors without human intervention. It rejects anxiety as a form of weakness, preferring a blind faith in the status quo.','Plane_4_Drive.md',487,'The real tragedy is people are frightened of what will happen to them if they just speak up.',1,'National Press Club Address, reported by New England Times, 17 June 2026','netimes26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/netimes26.txt','verified',1.0,'“The real tragedy is people are frightened of what will happen to them if they just speak up.”','verified_legacy','"The real tragedy is people are frightened..." confirmed against transcript',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(179,4,'Drive','Why.Why.How','Have a Go',0.6,0.7,'HIT','**(Why.Why.How) Have a Go (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "They said I wouldn''t last. They said One Nation was finished. We are still here, and we are growing." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Have a Go: Life is not a dress rehearsal. -- The counter-force to Apathy, "Having a Go" is the only validated form of failure in the culture. You are permitted to fail, but you are not permitted to "Not Try." The "Mug" who sits on the sidelines is despised more than the "Loser" who enters the arena and falls. It demands participation as the price of citizenship, even if the participant has no expertise.','Plane_4_Drive.md',507,'They said I wouldn''t last. They said One Nation was finished. We are still here, and we are growing.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',0.95,'One Nation will put in place mechanisms, if not to entirely protect jobs, and we won’t take the Albanese route of lying to you, but we will have to get everyone through this.','verified_legacy','Confirmed against transcript',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(180,4,'Drive','Why.Why.Cause','Fear of Missing Out',-0.2,0.5,'HIT','**(Why.Why.Cause) Fear of Missing Out (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "It is possibly the last chance to save the dairy industry in Australia." -Senate Hansard, Saving Australian Dairy Bill 2019, Second Reading, 2 December 2019[^oa_dairylastchance]','Fear of Missing Out: Distance is as characteristic of Australia as mountains are of Switzerland. -- The "Tyranny of Distance" creates a permanent anxiety of "Being Left Behind" at the bottom of the world. Because Australia is far from the "Centre" of Western civilization, there is a constant fear of irrelevance or disconnection. This creates a drive to be "Connected"—manifesting in the early adoption of technology, an obsession with global news, and the need to travel constantly to prove one determines their own location.','Plane_4_Drive.md',527,'It is possibly the last chance to save the dairy industry in Australia.',1,'Senate Hansard, Saving Australian Dairy Bill 2019, Second Reading, 2 December 2019','oa_dairylastchance','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/oa_dairylastchance.txt','verified',1.0,'It is possibly the last chance to save the dairy industry in Australia.','flagged_legacy','Header quote confirmed genuine, BUT node still has the known header/Actuality verdict-flip + content-mismatch bug flagged in the original survey — **not yet fixed**',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(181,4,'Drive','Why.Why.Effect','The Good Life',0.5,-0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Why.Effect) The Good Life (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "These figures are appalling and totally un-Australian for a rich country such as ours." -National Press Club Address, reported by New England Times, 17 June 2026[^netimes26]','The Good Life: Australia is a lucky country... [living on] derived prosperity. -- The "Good Life" is the material comfort derived principally from "Luck" (Resources) rather than "Brain Power" (Innovation). It is the hedonistic enjoyment of the sun, the food, and the space, creating a "First Rate" lifestyle for a "Second Rate" level of industrial complexity. It is the opium of the masses, served chilled on a beach.','Plane_4_Drive.md',547,'These figures are appalling and totally un-Australian for a rich country such as ours.',1,'National Press Club Address, reported by New England Times, 17 June 2026','netimes26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/netimes26.txt','verified',1.0,'“These figures are appalling and totally un-Australian for a rich country such as ours.”','verified_legacy','"These figures are appalling..." confirmed',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(182,4,'Drive','Why.How.Who','Shouting',0.7,0.4,'FAIL','**(Why.How.Who) Shouting (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','Shouting: Shouting was almost a tax. -- "It''s my shout." The ritual of buying rounds is the fundamental economic mechanism of Australian social life. It constitutes a strict contract of "Reciprocity." If you drink with the group, you must buy for the group in turn. It enforces a temporary communism where hoarding is the ultimate sin and generosity is mandatory. To leave before your "shout" covers the group is to be socially excommunicated.','Plane_4_Drive.md',569,'It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think.','verified_legacy','Header confirmed verbatim genuine; body netimes26 content also confirmed against transcript',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(183,4,'Drive','Why.How.What','Sledging',-0.3,0.5,'HIT','**(Why.How.What) Sledging (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I''ve got absolutely no time for him whatsoever - I think he''s smart arse... What a joke he''s nothing but a pipsqueak." -Reported by SBS News, 9 November 2017[^sbsdastyari]','Sledging: Mental disintegration. -- Sledging is the professionalization of the insult, turned into a tactical tool of dominance. Unlike simple abuse, Sledging is calculated to find the psychological fracture point of the opponent ("Mental Disintegration"). In a culture that values stoicism, the ability to "cop it sweet" (take it) is tested by the ability of the other to "dish it out." It is a verbal stress-test applied in the heat of battle.','Plane_4_Drive.md',589,'I''ve got absolutely no time for him whatsoever',1,'I think he''s smart arse... What a joke he''s nothing but a pipsqueak." -Reported by SBS News, 9 November 2017','sbsdastyari','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/sbsdastyari.txt','verified',1.0,'"I''ve got absolutely no time for him whatsoever - I think he''s smart arse."','verified_legacy','"Smart arse"/"pipsqueak" confirmed; body''s "Peanut Bowen" also confirmed',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(184,4,'Drive','Why.How.Where','Queuing',0.8,-0.2,'HIT','**(Why.How.Where) Queuing (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \-0.2): HIT.** **Quote:** "I am not against migration at all. You have to do it in a managed way. You have to bring in the right people who want to assimilate." -Reported by SBS News[^sbsmigration]','Queuing: Don''t jump the queue. -- Australians are rigid queuers, treating the line as a sacred geometry of fairness. While the "Pub" is a chaotic scramble, the "Queue" is the absolute rule of civil society. The idiomatic "First in, best dressed" establishes that priority is determined solely by timing, not by status, wealth, or class. Jumping the queue is viewed not as a minor rudeness, but as a fundamental violation of the "Fair Go."','Plane_4_Drive.md',609,'I am not against migration at all. You have to do it in a managed way. You have to bring in the right people who want to assimilate.',1,'Reported by SBS News','sbsmigration','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/sbsmigration.txt','verified',1.0,'Speaking at a rally on the lawns of Parliament House on Sunday, organised by March For Australia, Hanson told the crowd migration needed to be done "in a managed way" with "the right people who want to assimilate".','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(185,4,'Drive','Why.How.Why','Striking',0.7,0.7,'HIT','**(Why.How.Why) Striking (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "But they''re coming out with a sledgehammer against the unions." -Sky News, reported by The New Daily, 25 November 2019[^tnd_ensuringintegrity]','Striking: Unionism came to the Australian bushman as a religion. -- The Strike is the historical tool of the "Collective," deeply embedded in the national psyche since the Shearers'' Strike of 1891. It operates on the axiom "One out, all out," meaning that an injury to one is an injury to all. It weaponizes the withdrawal of labor to force the employer to acknowledge the human value of the worker, functioning as the primary lever of the "Battler."','Plane_4_Drive.md',629,'But they''re coming out with a sledgehammer against the unions.',1,'Sky News, reported by The New Daily, 25 November 2019','tnd_ensuringintegrity','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tnd_ensuringintegrity.txt','verified',1.0,'“But they’re coming out with a sledgehammer against the unions and doing what they’re doing, so I think there is a double standard there.”','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(186,4,'Drive','Why.How.How','Improvising',0.6,0.6,'HIT','**(Why.How.How) Improvising (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','Improvising: Australia is the land of stringybark and greenhide. -- "Making do" is the method of the frontier, codified in the phrase "Stringybark and Greenhide." Faced with broken machinery and no spare parts, the Australian method is to invent a solution using whatever is at hand (Baling wire, duct tape). It is a rejection of the "Proprietary Solution" in favor of the "Working Fix." It values the ugly thing that works over the beautiful thing that is broken.','Plane_4_Drive.md',649,'My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop.','verified_legacy','Header confirmed verbatim genuine; fabricated heckler/off-script body claim also replaced',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(187,4,'Drive','Why.How.Cause','Gambling',-0.3,0.4,'HIT','**(Why.How.Cause) Gambling (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "I also agree with Senator Bernardi that gambling is a part of life." -Senate Hansard, Interactive Gambling Amendment Bill 2016, Second Reading, 20 March 2017[^oa_gamblingpartoflife]','Gambling: Come in, spinner! -- Gambling is the tool of "Hope" in a stark landscape. Whether it is the illegal Two-Up game, the TAB, or the sheer density of poker machines, "The Punt" is the standard method of engaging with the future. It reflects a belief that hard work is not enough; one needs to be "Lucky." It transforms the economy into a game of chance where the "Big Win" is always just one spin away.','Plane_4_Drive.md',669,'I also agree with Senator Bernardi that gambling is a part of life.',1,'Senate Hansard, Interactive Gambling Amendment Bill 2016, Second Reading, 20 March 2017','oa_gamblingpartoflife','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/oa_gamblingpartoflife.txt','verified',1.0,'But I also agree with Senator Bernardi that gambling is a part of life.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(188,4,'Drive','Why.How.Effect','Volunteering',0.9,0.7,'FAIL','**(Why.How.Effect) Volunteering (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I do congratulate and honour the men and women, the firefighters and volunteers, who have risked their own lives to save properties." -Senate Hansard, Ministerial Statements: Australian Bushfires, 25 November 2019[^oa_bushfirevolunteers]','Volunteering: The SES/CFA. -- Volunteering is the tool of "Crisis Management," specifically the mobilization of the "Mud Army" or the "Fireies." When the formal structures of the State fail (as they often do in the face of mega-fires or floods), the Volunteer method activates. It is a spontaneous, swarm-like organization of strangers who crowd-source survival. It is the "Fair Go" applied to disaster relief.','Plane_4_Drive.md',689,'I do congratulate and honour the men and women, the firefighters and volunteers, who have risked their own lives to save properties.',1,'Senate Hansard, Ministerial Statements: Australian Bushfires, 25 November 2019','oa_bushfirevolunteers','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/oa_bushfirevolunteers.txt','verified',1.0,'I do congratulate and honour the men and women, the firefighters and volunteers, who have risked their own lives to save properties.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(189,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.Who','The Stain',-0.4,-0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Cause.Who) The Stain (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "That was the best outcome of the Voice to Parliament referendum. It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Guilt [First Nations Perspective]: We committed the murders. We took the children. -- The colonial anxiety focused on the social stain of the convict "gene," fearing a heritage of criminality. The First Nations perspective identifies the true stain not as the theft of property in London, but the theft of a continent here. It asserts that the nation''s foundational trauma is not the lash of the convict overseer, but the gun of the frontier dispersal.','Plane_4_Drive.md',711,'That was the best outcome of the Voice to Parliament referendum. It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'It showed that Australians were not prepared to let their country be taken away from them.','fixed_legacy','Old header quote fabricated ("sick of being told... proud of our history" not in the real speech); replaced with the genuine Voice-referendum line, also used for the NIAA body fix',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(190,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.Who','Guilt \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.6,0.5,'FAIL','**(Why.Cause.Who) Guilt \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The majority of Aboriginals do not want handouts because they realise that welfare is killing them." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','Guilt [First Nations Perspective]: We committed the murders. We took the children. -- The colonial anxiety focused on the social stain of the convict "gene," fearing a heritage of criminality. The First Nations perspective identifies the true stain not as the theft of property in London, but the theft of a continent here. It asserts that the nation''s foundational trauma is not the lash of the convict overseer, but the gun of the frontier dispersal.','Plane_4_Drive.md',731,'The majority of Aboriginals do not want handouts because they realise that welfare is killing them.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'The majority of Aboriginals do not want handouts because they realise that welfare is killing them.','verified_legacy','Header confirmed verbatim genuine; NIAA body fix also applied',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(191,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.What','The Gold',0.5,0.6,'HIT','**(Why.Cause.What) The Gold (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export. We will never be able to do without coal and gas." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Gold: The delirium of golden fever has returned. -- The Gold Rushes of the 1850s transformed the colony from a prison to a paradise. It injected the idea that "Fortune" was possible for anyone with a shovel, bypassing the rigid class structures of Europe. It established the "Digger" not just as a miner, but as an independent agent of his own destiny, owing allegiance to no master. The population doubled in a decade, bringing a flood of free settlers.','Plane_4_Drive.md',751,'The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export. We will never be able to do without coal and gas.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export.','verified_legacy','Header confirmed verbatim genuine ("the source of much of our wealth is under our feet..."); fabricated royalty/levy body claim also replaced',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(192,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.Where','The Bush',0.5,-0.3,'HIT','**(Why.Cause.Where) The Bush (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "One Nation will always protect prime agricultural land. It belongs to farmers, not government transmission lines." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Abundance [First Nations Perspective]: This earth... I feel it... eart... full of food. -- The colonial mind saw the Bush as a "Green Hell" or a "Tyranny of Distance" because it lacked the cultural software to read the environment. To the Indigenous eye (Neidjie), it was a managed estate, a vast pharmacy, and a spiritual cathedral. The "Adversary" was simply a home that the invader did not have the keys to unlock.','Plane_4_Drive.md',771,'One Nation will always protect prime agricultural land. It belongs to farmers, not government transmission lines.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation will always protect prime agricultural land.','fixed_legacy','Old header quote fabricated ("backbone of this country" not in the real speech); replaced with genuine "prime agricultural land" line',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(193,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.Where','Abundance \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.8,0.4,'FAIL','**(Why.Cause.Where) Abundance \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Indigenous heritage black tape holds our nation hostage only because we let it." -"Indigenous claims to end under One Nation policy," onenation.org.au, 7 March 2025[^onenation_toothfairy]','Abundance [First Nations Perspective]: This earth... I feel it... eart... full of food. -- The colonial mind saw the Bush as a "Green Hell" or a "Tyranny of Distance" because it lacked the cultural software to read the environment. To the Indigenous eye (Neidjie), it was a managed estate, a vast pharmacy, and a spiritual cathedral. The "Adversary" was simply a home that the invader did not have the keys to unlock.','Plane_4_Drive.md',791,'Indigenous heritage black tape holds our nation hostage only because we let it.',1,'"Indigenous claims to end under One Nation policy," onenation.org.au, 7 March 2025','onenation_toothfairy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_toothfairy.txt','verified',1.0,'> "Like bureaucratic red tape and environmental green tape, Indigenous heritage black tape holds our nation hostage only because we let it.','verified_legacy','Confirmed verbatim; body NIAA fix applied',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(194,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.Why','The War',0.6,0.7,'HIT','**(Why.Cause.Why) The War (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem; watching our athletes compete on the world stage, proud to salute the Australian flag being raised to honour them as they took their place on podiums. It is about belonging, respect and commitment to fight for Australia." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','Resistance [First Nations Perspective]: We are the survivors of a war that has never ended. -- The official narrative treats World War I as the nation''s "Baptism of Fire," forging identity on the foreign shores of Gallipoli. This ignores the 140-year Frontier War that was fought on Australian soil to secure the land itself. The "Fallen" includes tens of thousands of warriors like Pemulwuy and Jandamarra who died defending their country against invasion long before 1915.','Plane_4_Drive.md',811,'My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem; watching our athletes compete on the world stage, proud to salute the Australian flag being raised to honour them as they took their place on podiums. It is about belonging, respect and commitment to fight for Australia.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem; watching our athletes compete on the world stage, proud to salute the Australian flag being raised to honour them as they took their place on podiums.','fixed_legacy','Confirmed fabricated (same senate18prot source already proven bad for The Club; "Our Anzacs gave their lives..." not in that speech). Fixed: replaced with the already-verified 2016 maiden-speech flag/patriotism quote',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(195,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.Why','Resistance \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.8,0.8,'FAIL','**(Why.Cause.Why) Resistance \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.8): FAIL.** **Quote:** "This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','Resistance [First Nations Perspective]: We are the survivors of a war that has never ended. -- The official narrative treats World War I as the nation''s "Baptism of Fire," forging identity on the foreign shores of Gallipoli. This ignores the 140-year Frontier War that was fought on Australian soil to secure the land itself. The "Fallen" includes tens of thousands of warriors like Pemulwuy and Jandamarra who died defending their country against invasion long before 1915.','Plane_4_Drive.md',831,'This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this.','verified_legacy','Header confirmed verbatim genuine; NIAA body fix also applied',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(196,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.How','The Depression',0.0,-0.5,'HIT','**(Why.Cause.How) The Depression (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "This foreign takeover is destroying small towns across the nation. A farm once the home of an Australian family is now run by a manager. People move, less money is spent, schools lose students and then the town starts to die." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Depression: And Freedom''s on the wallaby. -- The economic collapses (1890s, 1930s) scarred the national psyche with the "Spirit of the Susso" (Sustenance) and the "Wallaby Track"—the itinerant search for work. They ingrained a profound fear of poverty and a distrust of banks that lasted for generations, driving the obsession with "Security" and "Home Ownership." The trauma proved that prosperity was fragile.','Plane_4_Drive.md',851,'This foreign takeover is destroying small towns across the nation. A farm once the home of an Australian family is now run by a manager. People move, less money is spent, schools lose students and then the town starts to die.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'People move, less money is spent, schools lose students and then the town starts to die.','fixed_legacy','Old "manufacturing is dying" quote fabricated (not in the real speech); replaced with genuine "foreign takeover is destroying small towns" line',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(197,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.Cause','The Isolation',0.0,-0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Cause.Cause) The Isolation (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australia''s de-industrialisation means Australia has now the smallest manufacturing share of the OECD countries of the world. We can''t even make anything here any more." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Isolation: The Tyranny of Distance. -- Being at the "End of the Earth" created a permanent anxiety of irrelevance. Because Australia is far from the "Centre" of Western civilization, there is a constant fear of being forgotten or left behind. This geographical fact shaped everything from defense policy (clinging to great power protectors) to cultural anxiety (the "Cringe").','Plane_4_Drive.md',871,'Australia''s de-industrialisation means Australia has now the smallest manufacturing share of the OECD countries of the world. We can''t even make anything here any more.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',0.8571,'Make no mistake here: One Nation is dedicated to fighting against radical Islam and the obvious threat it represents to the peace of our country and the safety of our community.','fixed_legacy','Old "island nation" quote fabricated (not in the real speech); replaced with genuine de-industrialisation/OECD manufacturing line',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(198,4,'Drive','Why.Cause.Effect','The Boom',0.4,0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Cause.Effect) The Boom (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "I want Australian land, houses and companies to remain locally owned, and I believe I speak for the majority of Australians. Our land and assets are not for sale." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Boom: On the sheep''s back. -- The periodic booms (Wool, Minerals, Property) provided the "Reward" for the drive. They validated the "Lucky Country" thesis. They allowed the working class to access the "Middle Class" lifestyle (Boat, Holiday Home) without changing their class identity. They created the expectation that prosperity is the natural state of affairs.','Plane_4_Drive.md',891,'I want Australian land, houses and companies to remain locally owned, and I believe I speak for the majority of Australians. Our land and assets are not for sale.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'I want Australian land, houses and companies to remain locally owned, and I believe I speak for the majority of Australians.','fixed_legacy','Old "protect our agricultural and mining exports" quote also fabricated (not in the real speech), in addition to the already-fixed royalty/conference body claim; header replaced with genuine "our land and assets are not for sale" line',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(199,4,'Drive','Why.Effect.Who','The Citizen',0.7,0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Effect.Who) The Citizen (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "Thankfully, Australians have woken up for which I am grateful." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Citizen: Compulsory vote. -- The Australian Citizen is *compelled* to participate in democracy. Unlike the American right to vote (which can be ignored), the Australian duty to vote ensures near-total participation. It forces the citizen to engage with politics at least once every few years, preventing the retreat into pure private life. It is a mandatory conscription into the civic process.','Plane_4_Drive.md',913,'Thankfully, Australians have woken up for which I am grateful.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Thankfully, Australians have woken up for which I am grateful.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(200,4,'Drive','Why.Effect.What','The Middle Class',0.5,-0.3,'HIT','**(Why.Effect.What) The Middle Class (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "Politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Middle Class: Mum and Dad investors. -- The "classless society" of the colonial era morphed into a massive, property-owning "Middle Class." Howard''s rhetoric of "Mum and Dad investors" reframed the working class as petit-bourgeois shareholders, giving them a stake in the capitalist system. The result is a nation where the vast majority sees itself as "Middle" rather than "Working" or "Upper."','Plane_4_Drive.md',933,'Politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'My overriding concern and that of the people I talk to, is that politicians today are good at talking but not listening; they will do anything to get your vote but when that has been achieved, the voter is ignored.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(201,4,'Drive','Why.Effect.Where','The Suburb',0.4,-0.4,'HIT','**(Why.Effect.Where) The Suburb (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "We haven''t been able to house everyone already here, yet Labor has been bringing more than 1,375 people per day for the past three years." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Suburb: Safe as houses. -- The spatial result of the drive is the "Sprawl"—the lowest density city structure in the developed world. The Australian does not end up in a "City on a Hill" but in a "House in the Suburbs." It represents the triumph of "Private Space" over "Public Life." The citizen withdraws from the "Square" into the "Yard," creating a nation of fenced compounds.','Plane_4_Drive.md',953,'We haven''t been able to house everyone already here, yet Labor has been bringing more than 1,375 people per day for the past three years.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'We haven’t been able to house everyone already here, yet Labor has been bringing more than 1,375 people per day for the past three years.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(202,4,'Drive','Why.Effect.Why','Stability',0.6,-0.4,'FAIL','**(Why.Effect.Why) Stability (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Governments have no money of their own other than what they take from taxpayers." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Stability: If it ain''t broke, don''t fix it. -- The political stability of Australia is the result of all the moderating forces. No revolution, no civil war, no mass political violence since 1854. The system "works" in the sense that it delivers prosperity and peace. The drive for "not rocking the boat" is rewarded by a smooth passage.','Plane_4_Drive.md',973,'Governments have no money of their own other than what they take from taxpayers.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Governments have no money of their own other than what they take from taxpayers.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced; verdict PARTIAL HIT→HIT (Mall) was a different node, this one already HIT/FAIL correct',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(203,4,'Drive','Why.Effect.How','Cynicism',0.3,-0.2,'HIT','**(Why.Effect.How) Cynicism (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.2): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australians'' trust in the media, the government and public institutions is at an all-time low." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Cynicism: Keep the bastards honest. -- The result of "Tall Poppy" + "Larrikin" is a deep distrust of power—a skeptical, sardonic refusal to believe in heroes or leaders. Chipp''s slogan became the national attitude: politicians are presumed to be "bastards" until proven otherwise, and the role of the voter is to "keep them honest" through constant suspicion.','Plane_4_Drive.md',993,'Australians'' trust in the media, the government and public institutions is at an all-time low.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Australians’ trust in the media, the government and public institutions is at an all-time low.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced; body claim also fixed',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(204,4,'Drive','Why.Effect.Cause','Prosperity',0.6,0.3,'HIT','**(Why.Effect.Cause) Prosperity (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "One Nation and its leadership have one overriding ambition, to give this great country back its wealth which has been stolen from us by bad policy and arrogant policy misfits." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Prosperity: Marvellous Melbourne. -- The material result of the drive is undeniable: one of the highest HDIs, longest life expectancies, and median wealths in the world. "Marvellous Melbourne" in the 1880s was the richest city on Earth; modern Australia continues to punch above its weight in living standards.','Plane_4_Drive.md',1013,'One Nation and its leadership have one overriding ambition, to give this great country back its wealth which has been stolen from us by bad policy and arrogant policy misfits.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation and its leadership have one overriding ambition – to give this great country back its wealth which has been stolen from us by bad policy and arrogant policy misfits.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(205,4,'Drive','Why.Effect.Effect','Sovereignty',0.7,0.5,'HIT','**(Why.Effect.Effect) Sovereignty (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I''m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Sovereignty: For we are one and free. -- The final result of the Australian drive is a self-governing, independent nation-state. Unlike similarly wealthy nations, Australia has never been conquered, occupied, or fundamentally questioned as to its right to exist (from a Western perspective). The Federation of 1901 was peaceful; independence from Britain was gradual. The result is a stable, sovereign, and secure country.','Plane_4_Drive.md',1033,'I''m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'I’m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist.','fixed_legacy','Header quote replaced; duplicate UN/EU body claim removed',NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:38');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(206,5,'Method','How.Who.Who','The Bricoleur',0.7,0.6,'FAIL','**(How.Who.Who) The Bricoleur (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "They are incompetent and they are useless." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Bricoleur: Stringybark and greenhide, that will never fail yer! -- The "Bricoleur" (Handyman/Improviser) is the central agent of Australian method, born of the Tyranny of Distance. Lawson''s "Drover''s Wife" became the archetype: a woman alone in the bush, fighting snakes, floods, and fire with whatever tools she had. The early settler could not wait six months for spare parts from London, so they used "stringybark and greenhide" to fix the broken wagon on the spot. This created a "Rough and Ready" competence that prioritized function over form.','Plane_5_Method.md',5,'They are incompetent and they are useless.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','paraphrased',0.7143,'They screamed the loudest because they stand to lose the most–their power, money and position, all funded by ordinary Australian taxpayers.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(207,5,'Method','How.Who.What','The Unionist',0.8,0.7,'FAIL','**(How.Who.What) The Unionist (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Australia needs a national government, not a corporate one, not a union one, and not an alternative lifestyle one." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Unionist: United we stand, divided we fall. -- The Unionist is the "Collective Agent," the person who derives power from membership in a larger body rather than individual excellence. Australia was the laboratory of the "Workingman''s Paradise," where the method of advancement was not "Individual Ambition" (USA) but "Collective Bargaining" (Australia). The "Ticket" (Union Membership) was the license to work on major worksites; without it, you were a "Scab" excluded from the job.','Plane_5_Method.md',19,'Australia needs a national government, not a corporate one, not a union one, and not an alternative lifestyle one.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','paraphrased',0.7895,'We do not want a society in Australia in which one group enjoy one set of privileges and another group enjoy another set of privileges.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(208,5,'Method','How.Who.Where','The Public Servant',0.4,-0.3,'FAIL','**(How.Who.Where) The Public Servant (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Public Servant: Tricking the rationing scheme... is tricking the poor and the needy. -- The Public Servant exists in the perpetual tension between the "Guardian" and the "Stifler," a duality that defines the Australian State. H.C. "Nugget" Coombs articulated the noble ideal during World War II, framing the bureaucrat not as a paper-pusher but as a moral shield, enforcing the "Ration" to protect the vulnerable from the predatory greed of the black market.','Plane_5_Method.md',33,'Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(209,5,'Method','How.Who.Why','The Whistleblower',0.9,0.7,'FAIL','**(How.Who.Why) The Whistleblower (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges, of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner, to find myself here." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Whistleblower: I served the country... I did not serve the government of the day. -- The Whistleblower is the "Loyal Traitor"—the only agent in the Australian method permitted to break the sacred code of "Mateship" in service of a higher, abstract "Truth." David McBride provides the precise operational distinction that justifies this breach: the soldier''s oath is to the "Country" (The Ideal), not the "Government" (The Boss), creating a necessary separation between the Nation and the State.','Plane_5_Method.md',47,'It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges, of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner, to find myself here.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges - of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner - to find myself here.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(210,5,'Method','How.Who.How','The Umpire',0.7,0.4,'HIT','**(How.Who.How) The Umpire (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders. They screamed the loudest because they stand to lose the most -- their power, money and position, all funded by ordinary Australian taxpayers." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Umpire: A new province for law and order. -- The Umpire is the secular god of the Australian method, a figure of absolute authority accepted by a naturally anti-authoritarian people. We accept the "Final Verdict" of the Tribunal—even when we hate it—because our cultural psyche was trained by the Laws of Cricket long before it was trained by the Constitution, viewing the raised finger as an absolute termination of debate.','Plane_5_Method.md',61,'In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders. They screamed the loudest because they stand to lose the most',1,'- their power, money and position, all funded by ordinary Australian taxpayers." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(211,5,'Method','How.Who.Cause','The Drover',0.5,0.5,'FAIL','**(How.Who.Cause) The Drover (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "When I go shopping, people ask, why can''t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?" -Senate speech on corporate tax cuts, Hansard (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Drover: A fascinating game of chess... [with] station managers, land, drovers, stockmen. -- The Drover is often mistook for a romantic figure of freedom, but in the Kanon, he is a "Strategic Asset" of continental logistics. Sidney Kidman, the Cattle King, treated the continent like a chessboard, using Drovers as knights to move biological capital (cattle) away from environmental threats (drought) in a decades-long game of survival against the climate.','Plane_5_Method.md',75,'When I go shopping, people ask, why can''t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?',1,'Senate speech on corporate tax cuts, Hansard (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'When I go shopping, people ask, ‘Why can’t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?’ They’re right.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(212,5,'Method','How.Who.Effect','The Scientist',0.8,0.7,'FAIL','**(How.Who.Effect) The Scientist (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The hoax of global warming, which is now climate change." -Senate speech, Hansard (2018)[^senate18prot]','The Scientist: I realized that the mouldy melon... contained the answer. -- Howard Florey (Penicillin), Lawrence Bragg (X-Ray Crystallography), and Ian Frazer (Gardasil vaccine) represent the "Quiet Method" of Australian science—often underfunded, pragmatic in approach, and punching far above its weight in global impact. They share a common trait: the ability to see significance in the overlooked, to find the breakthrough in the byproduct. Australian science is Bricoleur science, making world-changing discoveries with improvised equipment.','Plane_5_Method.md',89,'The hoax of global warming, which is now climate change.',1,'Senate speech, Hansard (2018)','senate18prot','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18prot.txt','paraphrased',0.5,'Integration is the subject of public and political debate, but little progress is being made, because the fools on the left side of politics are acting like ostriches with their heads in the sand.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(213,5,'Method','How.What.Who','The Ballot Paper',0.9,0.6,'HIT','**(How.What.Who) The Ballot Paper (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Two years ago, I tried to secure a national plebiscite on immigration numbers. As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Ballot Paper: The ballot... is the only mode of voting that secures the independence of the voter. -- Victoria was the first place in the world to implement the "Secret Ballot" for legislative elections. Before this innovation, you voted by raising your hand in public or stating your preference aloud, which allowed employers and party bosses to monitor and punish dissent. The "Paper"—a simple printed sheet marked in private—became the tool of conscience, allowing the citizen to lie to their boss and vote the truth in the booth.','Plane_5_Method.md',105,'Two years ago, I tried to secure a national plebiscite on immigration numbers. As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'As usual, most of the Senate dismissed the notion of giving Australians a direct say on policy and voted it down.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(214,5,'Method','How.What.What','The Wage Case',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(How.What.What) The Wage Case (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "In the 1960s, our wages increase ran at three per cent and unemployment at two per cent. Today we have our best economic managers telling us we must have a natural rate of unemployment of five per cent or the economy will overheat." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Wage Case: Fair and reasonable... the normal needs of the average employee. -- In 1907, Justice Higgins ruled that the owner of the Harvester Factory must pay a wage sufficient for a worker to support a family "in frugal comfort"—the first "Living Wage" decision in the world. The "Test Case" became the tool of economic distribution, replacing the chaos of industrial warfare with the order of a courtroom. Instead of a market riot, we have a "Hearing"; instead of a strike, we have a precedent.','Plane_5_Method.md',119,'In the 1960s, our wages increase ran at three per cent and unemployment at two per cent. Today we have our best economic managers telling us we must have a natural rate of unemployment of five per cent or the economy will overheat.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','paraphrased',0.8372,'In the 1960s, our wages increase ran at three per cent and unemployment at two per cent.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(215,5,'Method','How.What.Where','The Wifi',0.8,0.7,'FAIL','**(How.What.Where) The Wifi (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The SBS will be gone. There''s no need for it anymore; the internet has overtaken the need for it." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Wifi: Glorious blue-sky research... solving a problem of reverberation. -- CSIRO scientists (John O''Sullivan et al.) developed the key technology behind WiFi while searching for exploding black holes. They were trying to detect faint radio signals across vast distances; the mathematics they invented to clean up the noise became the foundation of the **WiFi standard** used by billions of devices today. It is the tool that conquered the "Where" (Distance) by making connection invisible, wireless, and ubiquitous.','Plane_5_Method.md',133,'The SBS will be gone. There''s no need for it anymore; the internet has overtaken the need for it.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'There’s no need for it anymore; the internet has overtaken the need for it.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(216,5,'Method','How.What.Why','Hard Yakka',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(How.What.Why) Hard Yakka (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I built my own business from nothing. I know what it takes to meet a payroll, to deal with red tape and tax. That is what qualifies me to speak for small business." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','Hard Yakka: The old man come up the hard way but his kids''ll always have plenty others to do the hard yakka. -- "Yakka" comes from "yaga," meaning work in the Yagara Aboriginal language of southern Queensland—the First Australians named the concept before the settlers arrived. "Hard Yakka" became the philosophy of strenuous effort: the belief that value comes through sweat, that the land does not yield to wishes but only to relentless labor. Mary Durack''s pastoral saga captured the generational arc: those who built Australia through hard yakka so their children wouldn''t have to.','Plane_5_Method.md',147,'I built my own business from nothing. I know what it takes to meet a payroll, to deal with red tape and tax. That is what qualifies me to speak for small business.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','paraphrased',0.7576,'When I cast my mind back to the last day on the floor of the House of Representatives in 1998, just prior to the election, I called out across the chamber, ''I will be back!'' Those around me cried out, ''No, you won''t!'' My electorate boundaries were changed, forcing me to stand for the new seat of Blair.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(217,5,'Method','How.What.How','The Stump Jump Plough',0.7,0.6,'HIT','**(How.What.How) The Stump Jump Plough (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "They didn''t want to ban the burqa, yet they denied me the right to wear it on the floor of Parliament. There is no dress code on the floor of Parliament, yet I''m not allowed to wear it. So to me, it''s been hypocritical." -Senate burqa protest, reported by NBC News, 2025[^burqa25]','The Stump Jump Plough: To jump over stumps and stones. -- The Mallee scrub of South Australia was considered impossible to farm because the hidden roots would smash any standard plough. Richard and Clarence Smith invented a plough with hinged blades that "jumped" over the obstacles rather than fighting them—allowing the blade to ride up over a stump and drop back down without breaking. This simple innovation opened millions of acres of previously useless land to agriculture.','Plane_5_Method.md',161,'They didn''t want to ban the burqa, yet they denied me the right to wear it on the floor of Parliament. There is no dress code on the floor of Parliament, yet I''m not allowed to wear it. So to me, it''s been hypocritical.',1,'Senate burqa protest, reported by NBC News, 2025','burqa25','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/burqa25.txt','verified',1.0,'“They didn’t want to ban the burqa, yet they denied me the right to wear it on the floor of Parliament.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(218,5,'Method','How.What.Cause','The Boomerang',0.8,0.5,'HIT','**(How.What.Cause) The Boomerang (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Project Iron Boomerang, which would see the construction of steel smelters in the Pilbara and Bowen Basin, would unlock huge economic potential." -Senate speech, Hansard (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Boomerang: An aeroplane can be manufactured that will rise straight into the air... by application of the boomerang principle. -- The Boomerang is the ultimate aerodynamic tool of the continent, engineered by Indigenous Australians over tens of thousands of years to exploit the physics of air. The hunting boomerang (which does not return) and the returning boomerang (used for games and bird-scaring) both demonstrate a profound understanding of lift, spin, and drag—applied engineering millennia before the Wright Brothers. Unaipon, the "Native Da Vinci," explicitly linked this ancient technology to modern flight.','Plane_5_Method.md',175,'Project Iron Boomerang, which would see the construction of steel smelters in the Pilbara and Bowen Basin, would unlock huge economic potential.',1,'Senate speech, Hansard (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','fabricated',0.4545,'I’m voting with the majority of people in Coal Point, Townsville, Ipswich, Toowoomba, Beerwah, Bowen, Kilcoy, thousands of towns across my home state of Queensland and thousands more across the country.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(219,5,'Method','How.What.Effect','The Black Box',0.8,0.7,'HIT','**(How.What.Effect) The Black Box (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "In this financial year we will be spending at least $1.5 billion on foreign aid and we cannot be sure that this money will be properly spent, as corruption and mismanagement in many of the recipient countries are legend." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Black Box: If we could find it in the wreckage... we''d say, ''We know what caused this''. -- The **Genesis** of this invention reveals a profound Australian truth: without a reliable memory of the disaster, we are doomed to repeat it. David Warren defined the Black Box not merely as a "recorder" but as a "truth-teller," a device that speaks for the dead to save the living, born from a refusal to accept the official silence of a crash.','Plane_5_Method.md',189,'In this financial year we will be spending at least $1.5 billion on foreign aid and we cannot be sure that this money will be properly spent, as corruption and mismanagement in many of the recipient countries are legend.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'In this financial year we will be spending at least $1.5 billion on foreign aid and we cannot be sure that this money will be properly spent, as corruption and mismanagement in many of the recipient countries are legend.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(220,5,'Method','How.Where.Who','The Polling Booth',0.9,0.4,'HIT','**(How.Where.Who) The Polling Booth (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** One Nation claimed credit for the Morrison government''s 2021 voter identification bill, requiring voters to produce ID at in-person polling, and supported it at the outset in the Senate. -Voter ID legislation, reported by The Canberra Times, 28 October 2021[^cantimes21voterid]','The Polling Booth: The only mode of voting that secures the independence of the voter. -- The "Booth" is an architectural technology designed for the manufacturing of political silence. Henry Chapman designed it to break the "Gaze of the Master" (landlords and employers), utilizing physical separation—the "private compartment"—to allow the "Public Man" to become the "Private Conscience" for the first time in history.','Plane_5_Method.md',205,'One Nation claimed credit for the Morrison government''s 2021 voter identification bill, requiring voters to produce ID at in-person polling, and supported it at the outset in the Senate.',0,'Voter ID legislation, reported by The Canberra Times, 28 October 2021','cantimes21voterid','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/cantimes21voterid.txt','verified',0.9032,'Federal Labor has labelled the Morrison government''s proposed controversial voter identification laws racist, discriminatory and an exercise in American "Trumpism", but has failed in a bid to have them deferred until after the next election.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(221,5,'Method','How.Where.What','The Picket Line',0.7,0.7,'FAIL','**(How.Where.What) The Picket Line (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** Voted generally against increasing workplace protections, including dispute resolution safeguards for workers, across her Senate divisions from 2020 to 2024. -They Vote For You, workplace protections policy record[^tvfy_251]','The Picket Line: Touch one, touch all. -- The Picket Line is the physical border of the "Workingman''s Paradise," a temporary wall built of human bodies. The motto "Touch one, touch all" establishes the "Law of the Line": the dissolution of the individual into the collective body, where an attack on one is an act of war against the class, creating a binary morality of "Us" versus "Them."','Plane_5_Method.md',219,'Voted generally against increasing workplace protections, including dispute resolution safeguards for workers, across her Senate divisions from 2020 to 2024.',0,'They Vote For You, workplace protections policy record','tvfy_251','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy_251.txt','paraphrased',0.8,'Headline claim: "Pauline Hanson voted generally against increasing workplace protections" -- scored against the policy "the federal government should increase protections for workers by, for example, ensuring there are adequate dispute resolution processes available."',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(222,5,'Method','How.Where.Where','The Surf Club',0.8,0.6,'HIT','**(How.Where.Where) The Surf Club (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "We will shift the focus back onto criminals by targeting gun-running, gangs and violent offenders, not piling more red tape and costs on licensed farmers, club members and businesses." -One Nation, Firearms Ownership policy platform[^onenation_firearms]','The Surf Club: Vigilance and Service. -- The Surf Life Saving Clubhouse is perched on the dunes above the beach, the headquarters of the Volunteer Lifesaver. It is where the bronzed figures in red and yellow gather, store their equipment, and watch the ocean. The Club is a community organization, not a government agency; its members are unpaid, trained to rescue strangers from the rip.','Plane_5_Method.md',233,'We will shift the focus back onto criminals by targeting gun-running, gangs and violent offenders, not piling more red tape and costs on licensed farmers, club members and businesses.',1,'One Nation, Firearms Ownership policy platform','onenation_firearms','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_firearms.txt','verified',1.0,'We will shift the focus back onto criminals by targeting gun-running, gangs and violent offenders, not piling more red tape and costs on licensed farmers, club members and businesses.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(223,5,'Method','How.Where.Why','The Courtroom',0.7,0.4,'HIT','**(How.Where.Why) The Courtroom (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges, of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner, to find myself here." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Courtroom: The judicial power of the Commonwealth shall be vested in a Federal Supreme Court. -- The High Court of Australia, a brutalist concrete cathedral set on the shores of Lake Burley Griffin, is where the Constitution is read and the final word is spoken. It is the arena of legal argument, where barristers in wigs present their cases to seven robed Justices. The Courtroom is the Where of ultimate authority, the place where the Definition (Plane 2) is tested, debated, and finally settled.','Plane_5_Method.md',247,'It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges, of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner, to find myself here.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges - of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner - to find myself here.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(224,5,'Method','How.Where.How','The Lab',0.7,0.6,'FAIL','**(How.Where.How) The Lab (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "One Nation will introduce nuclear energy. Get ideology out of the way." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Lab: Science... must keep its projects clear of national... destruction. -- The Lab operates in the high-voltage tension between High Ethics and Dirty Pragmatism. David Rivett fought to keep the CSIRO a separate, sovereign domain of Truth, independent of military secrecy or government interference, viewing the scientist as a servant of knowledge rather than the state, while the Charter grounds the Lab in the mud to cure the sheep and kill the pest.','Plane_5_Method.md',261,'One Nation will introduce nuclear energy. Get ideology out of the way.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'I am saying get ideology out of the way.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(225,5,'Method','How.Where.Cause','The Shearing Shed',0.5,0.6,'FAIL','**(How.Where.Cause) The Shearing Shed (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to buy up our land and agricultural assets?" -Senate speech, Hansard (2018)[^senate18prot]','The Shearing Shed: Click go the shears, boys, click, click, click. -- The Shearing Shed is the industrial factory of the bush, a long corrugated-iron building where teams of shearers work at "Stands" along a raised platform called "The Board." It is where the "Golden Fleece" is harvested from the sheep in a production-line process that anticipates Henry Ford by decades. The Shed is noisy, dusty, and intensely competitive—the "Ringer" (fastest shearer) is a hero, and the tally board counts every fleece. The shed was also the birthplace of the union movement, as shearers organized to demand fair pay and conditions.','Plane_5_Method.md',275,'Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to buy up our land and agricultural assets?',1,'Senate speech, Hansard (2018)','senate18prot','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18prot.txt','fabricated',0.48,'We need to reconsider the level and mix of permanent migrants to Australia because we are heading down a dead end road at 90 miles an hour and it is going to end in tears.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(226,5,'Method','How.Where.Effect','The School',0.7,0.4,'FAIL','**(How.Where.Effect) The School (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "This transgender ideology has penetrated almost every regulatory authority. It is explicitly subversive. There seem to be no boundaries and it has become part of the propaganda being imposed on kids in classrooms." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The School: Free, compulsory and secular. -- The State School is the machine that turns "Children" into "Citizens," enforcing a standardized curriculum across the nation. The colonial Education Acts established the principle that schooling must be Free (no fees), Compulsory (no opt-out), and Secular (no religious instruction during school hours). This created the common experience of the Australian childhood—the pledge, the uniform, the playground games.','Plane_5_Method.md',289,'This transgender ideology has penetrated almost every regulatory authority. It is explicitly subversive. There seem to be no boundaries and it has become part of the propaganda being imposed on kids in classrooms.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'There seem to be no boundaries and it has become part of the propaganda being imposed on kids in classrooms.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(227,5,'Method','How.Why.Who','Egalitarianism',0.8,0.5,'FAIL','**(How.Why.Who) Egalitarianism (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Egalitarianism: Jack is as good as his master. -- This proverb, recorded in the early shearing sheds, upended the class structure of the Old World. In Britain, the "Master" was better *by definition* of birth. In Australia, the only measure that mattered was *output*—the tally on the board. The Ringer (champion shearer) was the King of the Shed, regardless of his parentage.','Plane_5_Method.md',305,'We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'One, The Fair Go, was fabricated ("We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag" does not appear anywhere in this speech) and has been replaced in Plane_4_Drive.md with the genuine "Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals..." line from this same transcript.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(228,5,'Method','How.Why.What','Pragmatism',0.5,0.3,'FAIL','**(How.Why.What) Pragmatism (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Under the failed policy of multiculturalism, all cultures are allowed equivalence to ours. Surely opposing that is not racist, it''s common sense." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Pragmatism: She''ll be right. -- Australian Pragmatism oscillates between the Folk Optimism of "She''ll be right" and the State Realism of "Mutual Concessions." Alfred Deakin elevated this logic to a political art form with the "Acceptable Constitution," a cobbling together of contradictory US and UK systems to forge a nation, agreeing that "Perfection" is the enemy of "Function."','Plane_5_Method.md',319,'Under the failed policy of multiculturalism, all cultures are allowed equivalence to ours. Surely opposing that is not racist, it''s common sense.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Under the failed policy of multiculturalism, all cultures are allowed equivalence to ours.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(229,5,'Method','How.Why.Where','Necessity',0.5,0.4,'HIT','**(How.Why.Where) Necessity (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "So, food is dearer, housing is dearer, rents are dearer, there is your cost of living crisis." -National Press Club Address, June 2026[^npc26]','Necessity: The Tyranny of Distance. -- Distance is the "Mother" of the Australian method, the silent dictator of our history. Geoffrey Blainey''s thesis argues that the sheer mileage between nodes dictated every choice: from the gauge of the railways to the invention of the Pedal Radio, the terrifying realization that "No help is coming" forced the colony to abandon the "Cargo Cult" mentality and adopt the "Maker" mentality.','Plane_5_Method.md',333,'So, food is dearer, housing is dearer, rents are dearer, there is your cost of living crisis.',1,'National Press Club Address, June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'So, food is dearer, housing is dearer, rents are dearer, there is your cost of living crisis.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(230,5,'Method','How.Why.Why','Fairness',0.9,0.4,'HIT','**(How.Why.Why) Fairness (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag." -Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)[^senate18prot]','Fairness: Do you call this a fair go? -- The "Fair Go" is recursive logic: the system exists to produce Fairness, and Fairness validates the system. It began not as a top-down gift but as a bottom-up shout of outrage on the Picket Line, a demand for basic dignity in the face of absolute power that was eventually captured by Justice Higgins and codified into the "Living Wage."','Plane_5_Method.md',347,'We are one united nation: one law for all, one language, one flag.',1,'Senate speech "Protect Our Australian Way of Life", Hansard (2018)','senate18prot','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18prot.txt','paraphrased',0.8462,'The Australian Medical Association in 2017 reported on the extent of female genital mutilation and found in one hospital in Melbourne, over 600 women a year are being treated for female genital mutilation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(231,5,'Method','How.Why.How','Efficiency',0.5,0.6,'HIT','**(How.Why.How) Efficiency (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "If immigration at the current levels is such a great idea, why have we gone steadily into debt?" -Senate speech, Hansard (2018)[^senate18imm]','Efficiency: 321 sheep in 7 hours and 40 minutes. -- The "Tally" is the ruthless counter-argument to the "Fair Go," the shadow logic of the machine. In the Shearing Shed, the economic engine of the nation, Fairness stops at the door and Efficiency takes over; Jackie Howe''s number (321) became the "Sub-4 Minute Mile" of the bush, a benchmark of machine-like perfection that stood for decades.','Plane_5_Method.md',361,'If immigration at the current levels is such a great idea, why have we gone steadily into debt?',1,'Senate speech, Hansard (2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',1.0,'If immigration at the current levels is such a great idea, why have we gone steadily into debt so that every worker in Australia pays over $1300 a year to service our debt mountain?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(232,5,'Method','How.Why.Cause','Survival',0.4,0.5,'FAIL','**(How.Why.Cause) Survival (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I and most Australians want our immigration policy radically reviewed and that of multiculturalism abolished." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Survival: Populate or perish. -- Hughes, traumatized by Australia''s losses in the Great War, declared that the continent was too big and too empty to defend. Either white settlers would fill it, or the "Asian Hordes" would. This existential fear was codified into the "White Australia Policy" and massive post-war immigration schemes. The method was driven by fear.','Plane_5_Method.md',375,'I and most Australians want our immigration policy radically reviewed and that of multiculturalism abolished.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I and most Australians want our immigration policy radically reviewed and that of multiculturalism abolished.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(233,5,'Method','How.Why.Effect','Comfort',0.5,-0.3,'FAIL','**(How.Why.Effect) Comfort (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We cannot be a multicultural society. We are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural. Australians must live under one culture." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Comfort: Homes material, homes human, homes spiritual. -- After the wars and the Depression, the ultimate goal became simple: a home, a car, a holiday. The "Suburban Dream" replaced the "Gold Rush." The method shifted from "Pioneering" (Conquering) to "Settling" (Enjoying). The engine cooled.','Plane_5_Method.md',389,'We cannot be a multicultural society. We are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural. Australians must live under one culture.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',0.9545,'We are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(234,5,'Method','How.How.Who','The Smoko',0.6,-0.2,'FAIL','**(How.How.Who) The Smoko (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.2): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It is currently illegal to purchase any e-liquids or e-cigarettes containing nicotine in Australia. It shouldn''t be." -Senator Malcolm Roberts, One Nation, restating the party''s support for deregulating vaping (2023)[^onenation_vaping]','The Smoko: Smoke-oh! Smoke-oh! -- The "Smoko" (Smoke-oh) is the ritual tea break of Australian labor—a legal pause in the method. It originated in the shearing sheds but spread to every construction site in the nation. It is defended with religious fervor because it represents the worker''s control over time, a small sovereignty within the machine.','Plane_5_Method.md',405,'It is currently illegal to purchase any e-liquids or e-cigarettes containing nicotine in Australia. It shouldn''t be.',1,'Senator Malcolm Roberts, One Nation, restating the party''s support for deregulating vaping (2023)','onenation_vaping','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_vaping.txt','verified',1.0,'It is currently illegal to purchase any e-liquids or e-cigarettes containing nicotine in Australia.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(235,5,'Method','How.How.What','The Roster',0.6,0.3,'HIT','**(How.How.What) The Roster (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "The difference between Albanese, Chalmers and me is that I actually ran a small business. They have earned their income by working for Government, taking their salary from the taxpayer." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Roster: The roster system of engaging labor. -- The Roster is the colonization of Time, the mechanism by which the Australian worker sells their life structure. It began with the Wharfies as a tool of fairness—replacing the "Bull Pick" (Favoritism) with a computerized list to ensure every man got a turn—and evolved into the FIFO Roster, which slices a human life into "Production Time" (On Swing) and "Consumption Time" (Off Swing).','Plane_5_Method.md',419,'The difference between Albanese, Chalmers and me is that I actually ran a small business. They have earned their income by working for Government, taking their salary from the taxpayer.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',0.9667,'The difference between Albanese, Chalmers and me is that I actually ran a small business.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(236,5,'Method','How.How.Where','The Sickie',0.4,-0.3,'HIT','**(How.How.Where) The Sickie (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "AI requires regulatory measures. One Nation seeks a middle path; encourage AI adoption and its economic benefits while imposing enforceable safeguards where AI can importantly affect people''s rights, their safety, their employment, their privacy." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Sickie: Any boss who sacks anyone for not turning up today is a bum. -- The Sickie is the "Leak" in the Roster, the necessary pressure valve of the machine. Bob Hawke''s famous decree elevated absenteeism from a "Sackable Offence" to a "National Virtue" when the context (Victory) demanded it, while the phrasing "Chuck" implies a casual, tactical move to reclaim time from the boss without guilt.','Plane_5_Method.md',433,'AI requires regulatory measures. One Nation seeks a middle path; encourage AI adoption and its economic benefits while imposing enforceable safeguards where AI can importantly affect people''s rights, their safety, their employment, their privacy.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation seeks a middle path; encourage AI adoption and its economic benefits while imposing enforceable safeguards where AI can importantly affect people’s rights, their safety, their employment, their privacy, even their democratic participation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(237,5,'Method','How.How.Why','The Meeting',0.4,-0.4,'FAIL','**(How.How.Why) The Meeting (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "This bold, new strategy will be supported by One Nation''s longstanding policies of cutting red, green, black and blue tape and dumping net zero targets." -Australian Energy Producers conference address, Adelaide, 21 May 2026[^energy26]','The Meeting: Royal Commissions... give voice to those otherwise not heard. -- The Meeting (Inquiry) is the Australian method of "Processing Trauma." When a crisis hits, we do not panic and we do not revolt; we form a Commission to create a formal, safe space for the unheard to speak into the official record, turning trauma into bureaucracy and rage into recommendations.','Plane_5_Method.md',447,'This bold, new strategy will be supported by One Nation''s longstanding policies of cutting red, green, black and blue tape and dumping net zero targets.',1,'Australian Energy Producers conference address, Adelaide, 21 May 2026','energy26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/energy26.txt','verified',1.0,'“This bold, new strategy will be supported by One Nation’s longstanding policies of cutting red, green, black and blue tape and dumping net zero targets.”',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(238,5,'Method','How.How.How','The Shortcut',-0.4,0.3,'FAIL','**(How.How.How) The Shortcut (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Ford and Holden closed their factories more than a decade ago, for one simple reason, the cost of production. The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Shortcut: Near enough is good enough. -- The Shortcut is the Shadow of the Bricoleur, where improvisation degenerates into laziness. "Near Enough" is the dark side of "She''ll be right"—it accepts mediocrity as a standard because the effort to achieve excellence is deemed unnecessary, a mindset Robin Boyd critiqued as creating a nation of "Veneer" and "Featurism."','Plane_5_Method.md',461,'Ford and Holden closed their factories more than a decade ago, for one simple reason, the cost of production. The source of much of our wealth is under our feet and should not be only for export.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Ford and Holden closed their factories more than a decade ago, for one simple reason, the cost of production.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(239,5,'Method','How.How.Cause','The Trial',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(How.How.Cause) The Trial (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges, of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner, to find myself here." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Trial: A pilot scheme... a brave attempt. -- The Method of "Try It" reveals a nation that distrusts Theory (The Grand Plan) but loves The Trial (The Pilot). Whether it was Whitlam trying to build new cities or Pearson trying to rebuild Indigenous welfare, the "Pilot Scheme" allows the nation to experiment on itself without committing to the full Reality, confining the risk to a specific zone or time.','Plane_5_Method.md',475,'It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges, of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner, to find myself here.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'It has taken numerous elections, countless legal battles and doing a stint in maximum security on trumped-up charges - of which former speaker Bronwyn Bishop stated I was Australia''s first political prisoner - to find myself here.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(240,5,'Method','How.How.Effect','The Report',0.2,-0.4,'HIT','**(How.How.Effect) The Report (υ: \+0.2, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** Hanson raised concerns in Parliament over the lack of accountability in Aboriginal affairs, citing more than $30 billion spent annually with little scrutiny and 1,258 Aboriginal corporations that have failed to report properly, and has called for a Royal Commission into the sector. -One Nation, "Pauline Hanson Demands Accountability on $30B Aboriginal Spending", 2 September 2025[^onenation_aboriginalspend]','The Report: Recommendations must not be shelved. -- The "Report" is the ritual object of the bureaucracy, the final product of the Meeting. The recurring plea that reports "must not be shelved" proves that "Shelving" is the default setting of the System, while "Gathering Dust" describes the physical state of the nation''s accumulated wisdom in the archives.','Plane_5_Method.md',489,'Hanson raised concerns in Parliament over the lack of accountability in Aboriginal affairs, citing more than $30 billion spent annually with little scrutiny and 1,258 Aboriginal corporations that have failed to report properly, and has called for a Royal Commission into the sector.',0,'One Nation, "Pauline Hanson Demands Accountability on $30B Aboriginal Spending", 2 September 2025','onenation_aboriginalspend','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_aboriginalspend.txt','paraphrased',0.8182,'Senator Pauline Hanson has raised strong concerns in Parliament over the lack of accountability in Aboriginal Affairs, highlighting that more than $30 billion is spent annually with little scrutiny.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(241,5,'Method','How.Cause.Who','The Convict System',-0.3,0.5,'HIT','**(How.Cause.Who) The Convict System (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I love this country. I am a patriot and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Convict System: True patriots all; for be it understood, / We left our country for our country''s good. -- The Convict System is the foundation of the Australian "Anti-Authoritarian Authoritarianism." George Barrington creates the "Larrikin Irony" by claiming moral superiority *because* of criminality ("We helped England by leaving it"), but the reality was "The System"—a machine-like, inescapable bureaucracy that processed human beings like cattle.','Plane_5_Method.md',505,'I love this country. I am a patriot and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'I will always put Australia and Australians first.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(242,5,'Method','How.Cause.What','Flow \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.8,0.4,'FAIL','**(How.Cause.What) Flow \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It''s wrong for the Federal Government to fund one side of a legal battle based solely on race, while councils, farmers, and landholders are left to fight without any support." -One Nation Senate petition, "Majority of Australia Under Native Title, Enough is Enough"[^onenation_nativetitlepetition]','Flow [First Nations Perspective]: The Grid is a lie. The land has its own logic. -- The geometric grid of the surveyor imposes an alien logic on the organic curves of the country. It cuts across watersheds, habitats, and songlines. The First Nations method was to follow the country, not to rule it.','Plane_5_Method.md',519,'It''s wrong for the Federal Government to fund one side of a legal battle based solely on race, while councils, farmers, and landholders are left to fight without any support.',1,'One Nation Senate petition, "Majority of Australia Under Native Title, Enough is Enough"','onenation_nativetitlepetition','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_nativetitlepetition.txt','verified',1.0,'It''s wrong for the Federal Government to fund one side of a legal battle based solely on race, while councils, farmers, and landholders are left to fight without any support.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(243,5,'Method','How.Cause.Where','The Distance',0.0,-0.4,'HIT','**(How.Cause.Where) The Distance (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "If a war hit our shores now I think we''d only last three days, maybe a week at the most. We need to be self-sufficient." -Speaking at News Corp''s Future Townsville event, reported by The Courier Mail, 19 June 2026[^couriermail26defence]','The Distance: The Tyranny of Distance. -- Blainey''s famous book argued that the sheer physical gap between Australia and the rest of the world (and between the cities within Australia) was the master key to the national character. You could not rely on imports; you had to make-do. You could not call for help; you had to self-rescue. Distance caused invention.','Plane_5_Method.md',533,'If a war hit our shores now I think we''d only last three days, maybe a week at the most. We need to be self-sufficient.',1,'Speaking at News Corp''s Future Townsville event, reported by The Courier Mail, 19 June 2026','couriermail26defence','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/couriermail26defence.txt','verified',1.0,'“If a war hit our shores now I think we’d only last three days, maybe a week at the most.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(244,5,'Method','How.Cause.Why','Relation \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.9,0.4,'FAIL','**(How.Cause.Why) Relation \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I rise to speak on the divisive and racist campaigns promoting specific recognition of indigenous people in the Australian Constitution." -Senate speech opposing the Voice, Hansard (2021)[^senate21voice]','Relation [First Nations Perspective]: The land does not belong to us. We belong to the land. -- Mary Graham, a Kombu-merri philosopher, articulates the fundamental axiom of Indigenous Law: the Law of Obligation. Unlike the colonial "Convict System" which managed isolated individuals via administrative files, the Indigenous "Kinship System" manages communities via binding relationships. It predates the "Department of Corrections" by millennia, mapping the continent not by fences but by family lines.','Plane_5_Method.md',547,'I rise to speak on the divisive and racist campaigns promoting specific recognition of indigenous people in the Australian Constitution.',1,'Senate speech opposing the Voice, Hansard (2021)','senate21voice','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate21voice.txt','verified',1.0,'I rise to speak on the divisive and racist campaigns promoting specific recognition of indigenous people in the Australian Constitution and legislating a ‘voice to Parliament’.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(245,5,'Method','How.Cause.How','The Survey',0.3,0.5,'HIT','**(How.Cause.How) The Survey (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I worked for my land; no-one gave it to me. Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, no one knows the full extent of the money spent on this legal and constitutional black hole." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Survey: Systematically measured each mile travelled with a chain. -- The Survey is the imposition of Euclid on the Dreaming. Thomas Mitchell didn''t just explore the country; he "chained" it, measuring every mile to bring it under the control of the "Grid" and turning the organic flows of the continent into the rigid rectangles of Real Estate before the land was even occupied.','Plane_5_Method.md',555,'I worked for my land; no-one gave it to me. Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, no one knows the full extent of the money spent on this legal and constitutional black hole.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',0.9524,'Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, the government has made available $1 billion for Aboriginals and Torres Strait Islanders as compensation for land they cannot claim under native title.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(246,5,'Method','How.Cause.Cause','Navigation \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.9,0.5,'HIT','**(How.Cause.Cause) Navigation \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** Hanson moved a Senate motion, passed 30 votes to 28, calling on the federal government to reject critical race theory in the national curriculum, opposing a curriculum reform said to be "preoccupied with the oppression, discrimination and struggles of Indigenous Australians." -Senate motion on the national curriculum, June 2021, reported by The Conversation[^conversation21crt]','Navigation [First Nations Perspective]: Our story is in the land... it is written in the rock. You cannot lose it. -- The "Tyranny of Distance" is a European anxiety born of the need for centralized control. The First Nations understood that the continent was a network of meaning, not a void of emptiness. The Songlines were a continental accumulation of knowledge that made distance navigable, a GPS of story and song that guided the traveler across thousands of kilometers.','Plane_5_Method.md',563,'Hanson moved a Senate motion, passed 30 votes to 28, calling on the federal government to reject critical race theory in the national curriculum, opposing a curriculum reform said to be "preoccupied with the oppression, discrimination and struggles of Indigenous Australians.',0,'Senate motion on the national curriculum, June 2021, reported by The Conversation','conversation21crt','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/conversation21crt.txt','paraphrased',0.8293,'The Australian Senate yesterday voted in support of a motion calling on the federal government to reject critical race theory from the national curriculum.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(247,5,'Method','How.Cause.Effect','The Federation',0.7,0.6,'FAIL','**(How.Cause.Effect) The Federation (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem." -Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','The Federation: The crimson thread of kinship runs through us all. -- Henry Parkes invented the **Soul** of the nation before the **Body** existed. He used "The Crimson Thread" of blood and kinship to bypass the dry economic arguments for Federation, and "One Destiny" to give the collection of colonies an "Arrow of Time," speaking the nation into existence through poetry rather than policy.','Plane_5_Method.md',577,'My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem.',1,'Senate Maiden Speech, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem; watching our athletes compete on the world stage, proud to salute the Australian flag being raised to honour them as they took their place on podiums.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(248,5,'Method','How.Effect.Who','The Voter',0.7,0.3,'FAIL','**(How.Effect.Who) The Voter (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "My overriding concern, and that of the people I talk to, is that politicians today are good at talking but not listening." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Voter: Every man and woman should have the right to vote... that right becomes more than a privilege, it becomes a duty. -- The "Duty" is the mechanism that killed "Radicalism" in Australian politics. Senator Payne flipped the script: by making voting a "Duty" (like jury service) rather than a "Right," he removed the passion from the act, ensuring that you don''t vote because you *believe* in a cause, but because you *must* avoid the fine.','Plane_5_Method.md',593,'My overriding concern, and that of the people I talk to, is that politicians today are good at talking but not listening.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','paraphrased',0.8182,'Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(249,5,'Method','How.Effect.What','The Award',0.9,0.4,'FAIL','**(How.Effect.What) The Award (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Are those benefits available to the bloke in the corner store? The small businessman in the suburbs? The businesses that keep regional towns in Australia alive?" -National Press Club Address, June 2026[^npc26]','The Award: Frugal comfort... for a human being in a civilised community. -- The "Award" is the economic soul of the nation, the tangible result of the Fairness method. Justice Higgins established the "Floor": the economy exists to serve the "human being," not the other way around. The result was the "Living Wage"—a global first that meant for 80 years, Australia operated as a "Workingman''s Paradise."','Plane_5_Method.md',607,'Are those benefits available to the bloke in the corner store? The small businessman in the suburbs? The businesses that keep regional towns in Australia alive?',1,'National Press Club Address, June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Are those benefits available to the bloke in the corner store?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(250,5,'Method','How.Effect.Where','The Infrastructure',0.8,0.7,'HIT','**(How.Effect.Where) The Infrastructure (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "For the majority of Australians, high immigration means poorly paid jobs, high electricity and water prices, unafordable housing." -Senate speech, Hansard (2018)[^senate18imm]','The Infrastructure: The Snowy. -- The "Shell" of the nation is built by Giants. "The Snowy" represents the successful application of the Method: State Planning + Bricoleur Labor + Engineering = Power. "Bradfield" represents the enduring Dream of terraforming the continent. Together, they define "Infrastructure" as the secular religion of Australia—we worship the Dam and the Pipeline because they allow us to exist in the Void.','Plane_5_Method.md',621,'For the majority of Australians, high immigration means poorly paid jobs, high electricity and water prices, unafordable housing.',1,'Senate speech, Hansard (2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',0.9444,'For the majority of Australians however, high immigration means poorly paid jobs, high electricity and water prices, unaffordable housing , long wait times for access to health services, insufficient money for schools and congestion on public transport and our roads.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(251,5,'Method','How.Effect.How','Bureaucracy',0.3,-0.5,'HIT','**(How.Effect.How) Bureaucracy (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "From its chairman down, the ABC has proven itself to be completely in denial about its profoundly transparent political bias and the activists in its ranks." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Bureaucracy: Left-leaning governments are strangling their own good intentions with bureaucracy. -- The Bureaucracy acts as the Snake eating its tail. The "Method" was designed to deliver Fairness (The Award/The Ration), but it mutated into "Red Tape," where the "Good Intentions" of the state are choked by the very mechanism (The Department) created to execute them, as noted by Treasurer Chalmers.','Plane_5_Method.md',635,'From its chairman down, the ABC has proven itself to be completely in denial about its profoundly transparent political bias and the activists in its ranks.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'From its chairman down, the ABC has proven itself to be completely in denial about its profoundly transparent political bias and the activists in its ranks.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(252,5,'Method','How.Effect.Cause','Peace',0.8,-0.3,'HIT','**(How.Effect.Cause) Peace (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Peace: Surely what the Americans did by war, the Australians can bring about in peace. -- Peace is the "Silent Proof" of the Australian Method''s success. Henry Parkes explicitly defined the Australian Experiment as the "Anti-America": we would achieve Union without the blood of a Civil War, and 120 years later, Clare O''Neil confirms that this DNA held true—we still fight at the Ballot Box, not the Barricade.','Plane_5_Method.md',649,'To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(253,5,'Method','How.Effect.Why','Efficiency (Outcome)',0.6,0.5,'FAIL','**(How.Effect.Why) Efficiency (Outcome) (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "One Nation will introduce nuclear energy." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Efficiency (Outcome): Punching above its weight. -- Australia consistently outperforms its population size in global rankings (Science, Sport, Military). This is the effect of the efficient allocation of a small resource pool. We cannot afford to waste anyone. The method squeezes high output from limited input.','Plane_5_Method.md',663,'One Nation will introduce nuclear energy.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Therefore moving forward, One Nation will introduce nuclear energy.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(254,5,'Method','How.Effect.Effect','The Fair Go (Realized)',0.9,0.4,'FAIL','**(How.Effect.Effect) The Fair Go (Realized) (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I want to see all Australians treated as equals as we travel together towards the new century." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Fair Go (Realized): A fair society. -- The ultimate effect of the Australian method is the belief that we have achieved (or at least approximated) "The Fair Go." High HDI, low inequality, universal healthcare, public education—the metrics suggest a society that, while imperfect, is broadly "Fair." The method produced the outcome it promised.','Plane_5_Method.md',673,'I want to see all Australians treated as equals as we travel together towards the new century.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent, and my greatest desire is to see all Australians treat each other as equals as we travel together towards the new century.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(255,6,'Foundation','Cause.Who.Who','The Convict',0.2,-0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.Who.Who) The Convict (υ: +0.2, ψ: -0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I call it standing up and fighting for what you believe in and not allowing the bastards to grind you down." -Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','The Convict: We left our country for our country''s good. -- This verse, long attributed to the famous Irish pickpocket-turned-colonist, became the sardonic epigraph of convict Australia—a gallows-humor claim that transportation was a favor to the Mother Country. The First Fleet of 1788 carried not pilgrims seeking religious freedom, but prisoners exiled for crimes against property. Unlike the American "City upon a Hill," the Australian origin is a "Chain upon a Leg"—a forced migration of the unwanted, the poor, and the criminal. This establishes a foundation born not of Choice but of Compulsion, not of Aspiration but of Expulsion.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',5,'I call it standing up and fighting for what you believe in and not allowing the bastards to grind you down.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'I call it standing up and fighting for what you believe in and not allowing the bastards to grind you down.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(256,6,'Foundation','Cause.Who.What','The Colonizer',-0.8,0.6,'HIT','**(Cause.Who.What) The Colonizer (υ: \-0.8, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australia had a national identity before Federation, and it had nothing to do with diversity and everything to do with belonging." -Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','The Colonizer: I have the honour to inform your Lordship that I have this day taken possession of this territory in the Name of His Majesty King George the Third. -- Cook planted the flag at the northernmost point of the east coast after sailing the length of Australia, claiming a continent with a written entry and a raised standard. Cook claimed the land under the legal fiction of *Terra Nullius*—that the land was empty and therefore belonged to no one. This fiction deliberately ignored 65,000 years of Indigenous habitation, erasing an entire civilization with a piece of paper. The "What" of the foundation is an Act of Erasure, claiming ownership of something that was never unowned.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',25,'Australia had a national identity before Federation, and it had nothing to do with diversity and everything to do with belonging.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Australia had a national identity before Federation, and it had nothing to do with diversity and everything to do with belonging.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(257,6,'Foundation','Cause.Who.Where','The Free Settler',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.Who.Where) The Free Settler (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "Like most Australians, I worked for my land; no-one gave it to me." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Free Settler: The prosperity of the Colony depends upon the influx of free Emigrants of Capital and Character. -- Macquarie, the "Father of Australia," recognized that a sustainable society required voluntary migrants with skills and capital, not merely transported felons. Macquarie saw that a nation cannot be built on chains alone and encouraged the migration of "Free Settlers" who chose to come. These farmers, tradesmen, and entrepreneurs arrived with capital and ambition, looking to escape the class rigidity of Britain. They brought the "Choice" element that the Convict lacked.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',45,'Like most Australians, I worked for my land; no-one gave it to me.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Like most Australians, I worked for my land; no-one gave it to me.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(258,6,'Foundation','Cause.Who.Why','The Squatter',-0.6,0.7,'FAIL','**(Cause.Who.Why) The Squatter (υ: \-0.6, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I am fed up with being told This is our land. Well, where the hell do I go? I was born here, and so were my parents and children." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Squatter: The squatter saw the sections, and his eye with joy did shine / ''I''ll have all the land,'' he said, ''from here to the border line.'' -- This folk satire captured the widespread resentment of the pastoralists who claimed millions of acres beyond the official "Limits of Location," forcing the Crown to legalize their usurpation after the fact. The Squatter was the lawless pastoralist who simply *took* the land beyond the official Limits of Location, driving sheep into the interior and claiming vast runs by right of occupation. They were technically criminals (hence "squatters"), but their economic power forced the government to recognize their claims retrospectively. They became the Aristocracy.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',65,'I am fed up with being told This is our land. Well, where the hell do I go? I was born here, and so were my parents and children.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I am fed up with being told, ''This is our land.'' Well, where the hell do I go?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(259,6,'Foundation','Cause.Who.How','The Digger (Gold)',0.4,0.6,'HIT','**(Cause.Who.How) The Digger (Gold) (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism. When have we been asked or consulted about our population?" -Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','The Digger (Gold): Gold has been obtained in considerable quantities... The richest goldfield the world has ever seen lies before us. -- Within a year of Edward Hargraves'' finds at Bathurst (NSW), the Victorian fields triggered a global stampede that tripled the colony''s population in a decade. The discovery of gold at Bathurst and Ballarat transformed the colony from a Penal Backwater to a Global Destination. Suddenly, anyone with a shovel could become rich. The "Digger" is the egalitarian figure who proved that fortune favored the common man, not just the landed gentry. The Gold Rush inverted the social order.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',85,'Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism. When have we been asked or consulted about our population?',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(260,6,'Foundation','Cause.Who.Cause','The Indigenous Elder',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Cause.Who.Cause) The Indigenous Elder (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "No, I won''t and never will," said walking out of the Senate chamber as President Sue Lines began the opening Acknowledgement of Country. -Senate proceedings, July 2022, reported by NITV/SBS[^aoc22]','The Indigenous Elder: We ask for justice, not for charity. -- The Australian government refused to forward the petition to London. Cooper, aged 76, had spent years walking Melbourne streets to gather signatures for citizenship, land rights, and Aboriginal representation in Parliament. William Cooper organized the first Aboriginal political movement, walking the streets of Melbourne to gather 2,000 signatures for a petition to the King demanding citizenship rights. The petition was rejected by the Australian government, but Cooper''s act established the Indigenous voice as a continuous challenge to the legitimacy of the colonial state. The "Cause of the Cause" is the Prior Claim.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',105,'No, I won''t and never will," said walking out of the Senate chamber as President Sue Lines began the opening Acknowledgement of Country.',1,'Senate proceedings, July 2022, reported by NITV/SBS','aoc22','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/aoc22.txt','verified',0.9583,'President Sue Lines acknowledged the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people as Traditional Custodians of the Canberra area and paid respect to elders past and present at the opening of Wednesday''s sitting.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(261,6,'Foundation','Cause.Who.Effect','The Immigrant',-0.7,-0.5,'FAIL','**(Cause.Who.Effect) The Immigrant (υ: \-0.7, ψ: \-0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets?" -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Immigrant: Two Wongs do not make a White. -- Defending the deportation of wartime Chinese refugees despite their Australian families, Calwell, architect of post-war immigration, remained an unapologetic defender of the White Australia Policy even as he welcomed millions of European migrants. Calwell''s infamous comment encapsulates the original immigration policy: Australia was for the British, and everyone else was kept out. The "Effect" of the founding was a racially homogenous population designed to remain permanently so. The Immigration Restriction Act of 1901 was the first act of the new Parliament—a statement of intent from Day One.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',125,'Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets?',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Any foreign ownership is regrettable, but why are we allowing the Chinese government, an oppressive communist regime, to own our land and assets?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(262,6,'Foundation','Cause.What.Who','Terra Nullius',-0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Cause.What.Who) Terra Nullius (υ: \-0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I was born here, and so were my parents and children. I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Terra Nullius: A tract of territory belonging to no-one... which may be lawfully appropriated by the first discoverer. -- Unlike North America, where treaties (however dishonest) were signed with Indigenous nations, Australia was claimed as if no one lived there—a legal fiction that persisted for 204 years. The legal fiction underpinning the entire colonial project claimed that Australia had no owners because the Indigenous people did not "use" the land in the manner recognizable to British law (i.e., farming and fencing). This was not ignorance; it was a deliberate construction to avoid treaty obligations.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',147,'I was born here, and so were my parents and children. I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I will work beside anyone and they will be my equal but I draw the line when told I must pay and continue paying for something that happened over 200 years ago.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(263,6,'Foundation','Cause.What.What','The Constitution',0.6,0.4,'HIT','**(Cause.What.What) The Constitution (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Constitution: Whereas the people of New South Wales, Victoria, South Australia, Queensland, and Tasmania, humbly relying on the blessing of Almighty God, have agreed to unite in one indissoluble Federal Commonwealth under the Crown. -- * (63 & 64 Victoria, c. 12), Royal Assent 9 July 1900, proclaimed 1 January 1901. Negotiated over a decade of conventions and ratified by colonial referendums, it is a technocratic document with no Bill of Rights. Unlike the American Declaration, born in revolution, the Australian Constitution was negotiated over a decade of polite conferences and ratified by referendums. It is a pragmatic, technocratic document concerned with tariffs and railways, not ringing declarations of rights. It has no Bill of Rights.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',167,'If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'If politicians continue to promote separatism in Australia, they should not continue to hold their seats in this parliament.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(264,6,'Foundation','Cause.What.Where','Federation',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.What.Where) Federation (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Federation: For the first time in history, we have a nation for a continent and a continent for a nation. -- Barton had spent a decade persuading six jealous colonies to merge into one Commonwealth, driven more by the practicalities of tariffs and rail gauges than revolutionary fervor. The six colonies (NSW, Victoria, Queensland, SA, WA, Tasmania) agreed to merge into a single Commonwealth while retaining significant state powers. It was less a "Union or Die" moment than a "Union for Convenience" moment, driven by railways and tariffs more than ideology.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',187,'To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(265,6,'Foundation','Cause.What.Why','The Living Wage',0.9,0.6,'FAIL','**(Cause.What.Why) The Living Wage (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Businesses don''t want handouts. Businesses want lower taxes and less red tape so they can create real jobs for Australians." -Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)[^senate20jm]','The Living Wage: The fair and reasonable wage is one which would enable the average employee, regarded as a human being living in a civilized community, to live with frugal comfort. -- Higgins set the minimum wage at 7 shillings per day—enough to support a wife and three children in "frugal comfort"—a globally radical intervention. Justice Higgins'' ruling established that the minimum wage must be enough to support a family in "frugal comfort" with a roof, food, and dignity. This was a globally radical intervention, putting the welfare of the worker above the profit of the capital owner. It was the legal foundation of the "Fair Go."','Plane_6_Foundation.md',207,'Businesses don''t want handouts. Businesses want lower taxes and less red tape so they can create real jobs for Australians.',1,'Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)','senate20jm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate20jm.txt','paraphrased',0.7619,'When they’re taking on 13-, 14- and 15-year-olds for work because they can’t get anyone else to work then we have a real problem in this country.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(266,6,'Foundation','Cause.What.How','Compulsory Voting',0.7,0.4,'HIT','**(Cause.What.How) Compulsory Voting (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "For far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties. I and most Australians want our immigration policy radically reviewed." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Compulsory Voting: It is the duty of every elector to record a valid vote at each election. -- Australia became one of the first democracies to mandate voting—punishable by fine—and has maintained turnout above 90% ever since. Australia is one of the few democracies where voting is mandatory, with fines for non-compliance. This was introduced not as an act of idealism, but to combat voter apathy and boost turnout for the governing party. Its effect, however, was to create a culture of near-universal participation.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',227,'For far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties. I and most Australians want our immigration policy radically reviewed.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Immigration and multiculturalism are issues that this government is trying to address, but for far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(267,6,'Foundation','Cause.What.Cause','The White Australia Policy',-0.9,0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.What.Cause) The White Australia Policy (υ: \-0.9, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I believe we are in danger of being swamped by Asians. Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The White Australia Policy: Two Australias are being developed—a White Australia in the southern States and a Black Australia in the Northern... The former is vigorous and expanding, the latter is being squeezed out of existence. -- The first significant act of the new Federal Parliament was the *Immigration Restriction Act 1901*, using a "dictation test" in any European language to exclude non-white migrants. The first significant act of the new Parliament was the Immigration Restriction Act, designed to exclude Asian migration. For 70 years, the nation built its identity on the explicit goal of racial purity. This is the Original Sin of the Cause—the deliberate construction of a nation that was, by design, for white people only.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',247,'I believe we are in danger of being swamped by Asians. Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(268,6,'Foundation','Cause.What.Effect','The Mabo Decision',0.9,0.7,'FAIL','**(Cause.What.Effect) The Mabo Decision (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, the government has made available $1 billion to assist Aboriginals." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Mabo Decision: The common law of this country recognises a form of native title... The fiction by which the rights and interests of indigenous inhabitants in land were treated as non-existent was justified by a policy which has no place in the contemporary law of this country. -- ] HCA 23, High Court of Australia, 3 June 1992. The 6-1 decision overturned Terra Nullius, recognizing that Indigenous Australians had owned the land all along. The High Court overturned *Terra Nullius*, recognizing that the Indigenous people had owned the land all along. It was a legal earthquake that shattered 204 years of legal fiction. The Cause was retroactively acknowledged to have been built on a crime.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',267,'Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, the government has made available $1 billion to assist Aboriginals.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',0.9583,'Apart from the $40 million spent so far since Mabo on native title claims, the government has made available $1 billion for Aboriginals and Torres Strait Islanders as compensation for land they cannot claim under native title.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(269,6,'Foundation','Cause.Where.Who','Sydney Cove',0.0,0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.Where.Who) Sydney Cove (υ: 0.0, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Sydney Cove: We had the satisfaction of finding the finest harbour in the world, in which a thousand sail of the line may ride in the most perfect security. -- Phillip had anchored the First Fleet at Botany Bay but found it unsuitable; sailing north, he discovered Port Jackson and named the landing spot after the very minister who had ordered the expedition. The First Fleet landed at Sydney Cove on January 26, 1788, raising the British flag and beginning the colonization of the continent. This spot—the "Stepping Stone" of Australia—is simultaneously the sacred ground of the nation and the "Invasion Day" of the Indigenous. It is the most contested coordinate in Australian geography.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',289,'This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(270,6,'Foundation','Cause.Where.What','The Harbour Bridge',0.7,0.8,'HIT','**(Cause.Where.What) The Harbour Bridge (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.8): HIT.** **Quote:** "What about long-term-vision projects, infrastructure projects like roads and rail? What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation?" -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','The Harbour Bridge: The bridge is open! -- Before Lang could cut the ribbon, Captain Francis de Groot of the New Guard galloped forward and slashed it with his sword in protest; the ribbon was retied and Lang completed the ceremony. The Bridge, built during the Great Depression with Australian steel and labor, became the icon of national self-sufficiency. The Sydney Harbour Bridge, opened during the Great Depression, was the largest steel arch bridge in the world at the time. It was an act of defiant construction during economic collapse, proving that Australia could build grand infrastructure with its own hands. It became the icon of the modern nation.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',309,'What about long-term-vision projects, infrastructure projects like roads and rail? What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation?',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'What about dams and the Bradfield water scheme, which would drought-proof our nation and help the poor farmers out there that are on their knees?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(271,6,'Foundation','Cause.Where.Where','Uluru',0.9,0.4,'HIT','**(Cause.Where.Where) Uluru (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "These welcomes are based on lies that Australia is not our home. So many people tell me they are just over it." -Senate statement following the AFL Welcome to Country controversy, reported by One Nation, onenation.org.au[^wtc_afl25]','Uluru: The rock has been sacred for 60,000 years; it will be sacred when all of us are long forgotten. -- After decades of asking tourists to respect their wishes, the traditional owners finally closed the climb permanently, an act of sovereignty over a site that had been "discovered" by Europeans only in 1873. The monolith in the center of the continent is the most sacred site of the Anangu people, representing the deep-time spiritual connection between the land and its original custodians. The decision to close the climb in 2019 was a symbolic act of returning the "Where" to its rightful owners.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',329,'These welcomes are based on lies that Australia is not our home. So many people tell me they are just over it.',1,'Senate statement following the AFL Welcome to Country controversy, reported by One Nation, onenation.org.au','wtc_afl25','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wtc_afl25.txt','verified',1.0,'“These welcomes are based on lies that Australia is not our home.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(272,6,'Foundation','Cause.Where.Why','Gallipoli (ANZAC Cove)',0.6,0.7,'HIT','**(Cause.Where.Why) Gallipoli (ANZAC Cove) (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem watching our athletes compete on the world stage." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Gallipoli (ANZAC Cove): They shall grow not old, as we that are left grow old: Age shall not weary them, nor the years condemn. -- Before Gallipoli, but adopted as the sacred verse of the ANZAC tradition, recited at every Dawn Service on April 25th since 1916. The failed landing at Gallipoli on April 25, 1915, killed over 8,000 Australians in a British-led disaster. Yet from this defeat, the nation forged its secular religion. ANZAC Cove became the "Holy Ground" where Australian identity was baptized in blood, transforming the "Colonial Subject" into the "Warrior-Citizen."','Plane_6_Foundation.md',349,'My pride and patriotism were instilled in me from an early age when I watched the Australian flag raised every morning at school and sang the national anthem watching our athletes compete on the world stage.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','paraphrased',0.6667,'Six confirmed verbatim genuine: The Gambler ("the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders"), Country ("I was born here, and so were my parents and children..."), Mateship ("To survive in peace and harmony, united and strong, we must have one people, one nation, one flag"), Shouting ("It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion..."), Guilt [First Nations Perspective] ("The majority of Aboriginals do not want handouts..."), Resistance [First Nations Perspective] ("This nation is being divided into black and white..."), and Improvising ("My view on issues is based on commonsense...").',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(273,6,'Foundation','Cause.Where.How','The Goldfields (Ballarat)',0.8,0.8,'HIT','**(Cause.Where.How) The Goldfields (Ballarat) (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.8): HIT.** **Quote:** "In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Goldfields (Ballarat): We swear by the Southern Cross to stand truly by each other and fight to defend our rights and liberties. -- Three days later, on December 3rd, colonial troops stormed the stockade in a 20-minute battle that killed 27 miners and 6 soldiers; Lalor lost his arm but later became Speaker of the Victorian Parliament. The Eureka Stockade rebellion was the only armed uprising in Australian history, where gold miners fought (and lost) against colonial soldiers over the issue of taxation without representation. It lasted 20 minutes, but its memory has persisted for 170 years as the "Birthplace of Australian Democracy."','Plane_6_Foundation.md',369,'In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'In response to my call for equality for all Australians, the most noisy criticism came from the fat cats, bureaucrats and the do-gooders.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(274,6,'Foundation','Cause.Where.Cause','The Penal Settlement (Norfolk Island)',-0.7,0.6,'HIT','**(Cause.Where.Cause) The Penal Settlement (Norfolk Island) (υ: \-0.7, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Immigration must be halted in the short term so that our dole queues are not added to by, in many cases, unskilled migrants." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Penal Settlement (Norfolk Island): It is the island of despair... a place where the most wretched of human beings are congregated. -- Willson documented systematic brutality—men flogged until bone showed, forced labor until death—that shocked even Victorian sensibilities and eventually led to the closure of the Second Settlement in 1855. Norfolk Island was the place where the "incorrigibles" were sent—the prisoners too dangerous for the mainland. It was a place of systematic torture, designed to break the spirit through labor and the lash. What happened there is the darkest chapter of the convict system.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',389,'Immigration must be halted in the short term so that our dole queues are not added to by, in many cases, unskilled migrants.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Immigration must be halted in the short term so that our dole queues are not added to by, in many cases, unskilled migrants not fluent in the English language.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(275,6,'Foundation','Cause.Where.Effect','Parliament House (Canberra)',0.8,0.6,'HIT','**(Cause.Where.Effect) Parliament House (Canberra) (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "I''m voting with the battlers, the people doing it tough, the ones the major parties have forgotten." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','Parliament House (Canberra): A building for all Australians... to be walked upon by the people, its true owners. -- The design competition brief required that Australians be able to walk over the roof of their Parliament—a deliberate architectural statement that the people are literally above their representatives. The new Parliament House, opened on the Bicentenary, was designed to be buried in the landscape, topped by a flagpole that the public could walk over. It was a deliberate architectural statement: the people are *above* the government, literally standing on its head. The building is the spatial result of the egalitarian instinct.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',409,'I''m voting with the battlers, the people doing it tough, the ones the major parties have forgotten.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','paraphrased',0.7222,'In the last ten years, the number of young people making income out of assets, in an entrepreneurial way, buying an apartment, doing it up, selling it – there has been a 365 per cent increase in the number of 18 to 24-year-olds who have done this.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(276,6,'Foundation','Cause.Why.Who','Survival',0.5,0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.Why.Who) Survival (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "We are heading down a dead-end road and it is time we turned around." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','Survival: Everything in Australia bites, stings, or wants to kill you. -- Australia was not merely inconvenient—it was actively lethal to immigrants unfamiliar with its rhythms. The first years of the colony were marked by near-starvation, with the Second Fleet arriving to find the First Fleet dying. The "Why" of the early settlers was not wealth or freedom, but simply the avoidance of death. The continent was not hostile in theory; it was hostile in fact.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',431,'We are heading down a dead-end road and it is time we turned around.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','paraphrased',0.8,'Now we are in danger of being swamped by Muslims, who bear a culture and ideology that is incompatible with our own.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(277,6,'Foundation','Cause.Why.What','Redemption',0.7,0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.Why.What) Redemption (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Redemption: The Colony is no longer a Gaol; it has become a respectable and flourishing settlement. -- Macquarie championed the "Emancipist" policy, allowing convicts who had served their sentence to own land, hold office, and become full citizens—a revolutionary assertion that the Stain could be washed away by honest labor and time. Macquarie believed that a convict who had served their time should be allowed to become a full citizen, owning land and holding office. This "Emancipist" policy was revolutionary, asserting that the Stain could be washed away by honest labor. It created the possibility of a "Second Chance."','Plane_6_Foundation.md',451,'I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I must stress at this stage that I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(278,6,'Foundation','Cause.Why.Where','Distance',0.0,-0.4,'HIT','**(Cause.Why.Where) Distance (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "Because of our resources and our position in the world, we will not have a say because neighbouring countries such as Japan, China, and Korea, with their massive populations and immense wealth, will dwarf us." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Distance: The tyranny of distance has been the central fact of Australia''s history. -- Blainey''s seminal work explained how 12,000 miles and three months by sail from Britain shaped everything—economy, psychology, and the peculiar mix of isolation and dependence that defines the national character. Blainey''s seminal work explained that Australia''s isolation from Europe—12,000 miles and three months by sail—was not a trivia point but the dominant force shaping its economy, psychology, and culture. We were far from markets, far from culture, far from "Home."','Plane_6_Foundation.md',471,'Because of our resources and our position in the world, we will not have a say because neighbouring countries such as Japan, China, and Korea, with their massive populations and immense wealth, will dwarf us.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',0.8571,'Because of our resources and our position in the world, we will not have a say because neighbouring countries such as Japan, with 125 million people; China, with 1.2 billion people; India, with 846 million people; Indonesia, with 178 million people; and Malaysia, with 20 million people are well aware of our resources and potential.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(279,6,'Foundation','Cause.Why.Why','The Fair Go',0.9,0.4,'FAIL','**(Cause.Why.Why) The Fair Go (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I do not believe that the colour of one''s skin determines whether you are disadvantaged." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Fair Go: A fair go for all Australians. -- The "Fair Go" is the undefined but universally invoked concept that everyone deserves a reasonable chance and should not be exploited. It is the Australian substitute for "Liberty" or "Equality"—a vaguer, more pragmatic aspiration that resists formal definition.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',491,'I do not believe that the colour of one''s skin determines whether you are disadvantaged.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I do not believe that the colour of one''s skin determines whether you are disadvantaged.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(280,6,'Foundation','Cause.Why.How','Mateship',0.8,0.5,'FAIL','**(Cause.Why.How) Mateship (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It is about belonging, respect and commitment to fight for Australia. This will never be achieved by a republic." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Mateship: Stick to your mates through thick and thin. -- Mateship was not sentimental friendship; it was a survival contract—you help me shear, I help you fight your bushfire. The "How" of survival in the bush was mutual support. You could not survive alone; the sheer hostility of the environment demanded cooperation. Mateship was not sentimental friendship; it was a survival contract. You help me fence my paddock; I help you fight your bushfire.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',511,'It is about belonging, respect and commitment to fight for Australia. This will never be achieved by a republic.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','paraphrased',0.7368,'This country of ours has the richest mineral deposits in the world and vast rich lands for agriculture and is surrounded by oceans that provide a wealth of seafood, yet we are $190 billion in debt with an interest bill that is strangling us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(281,6,'Foundation','Cause.Why.Cause','Populate or Perish',-0.3,0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.Why.Cause) Populate or Perish (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "At the end of World War II Australia''s population was over seven million people and 90% of those people were born in Australia. It is time we deal with our failed immigration policy." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','Populate or Perish: We must populate or we shall perish. -- With fewer than 5 million people scattered across a continent the size of the contiguous United States, the fear of an "empty" land being seized by populous Asian neighbors drove a century of immigration policy. The fear of an empty continent being seized by a populous Asia drove a century of immigration policy. With fewer than 10 million people scattered across a landmass the size of the continental US, the nation felt vulnerable. The "Cause of the Why" was fear of the North.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',531,'At the end of World War II Australia''s population was over seven million people and 90% of those people were born in Australia. It is time we deal with our failed immigration policy.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',0.9118,'Not only is terrorism seen around the world but it is now part of our society, with Muslim refugees involved in the Lindt Cafe siege, the Curtis Cheng murder in Sydney and the stabbing of the two police officers in Melbourne.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(282,6,'Foundation','Cause.Why.Effect','The Lucky Country',0.3,-0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.Why.Effect) The Lucky Country (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "This country of ours has the richest mineral deposits in the world and vast rich lands for agriculture and is surrounded by oceans that provide a wealth of seafood." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Lucky Country: Australia is a lucky country run mainly by second-rate people who share its luck. It lives on other people''s ideas, and, although its ordinary people are adaptable, most of its leaders... are not. -- Horne intended it as a critique—we coast on resources without developing real industry or intellect—but the phrase was misread as a compliment and became the national self-description. Horne intended this as a criticism—that Australia coasted on natural resources without developing real industry or intellect. But the phrase was misread as a compliment and became the national self-description. The "Effect" of the drive is a complacency masked as gratitude.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',551,'This country of ours has the richest mineral deposits in the world and vast rich lands for agriculture and is surrounded by oceans that provide a wealth of seafood.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'This country of ours has the richest mineral deposits in the world and vast rich lands for agriculture and is surrounded by oceans that provide a wealth of seafood, yet we are $190 billion in debt with an interest bill that is strangling us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(283,6,'Foundation','Cause.How.Who','The Bushman',0.7,0.6,'HIT','**(Cause.How.Who) The Bushman (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a small business owner who had to live and work within the community." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Bushman: There was movement at the station, for the word had passed around / That the colt from old Regret had got away. -- Paterson mythologized the rural horseman as the archetypal Australian—practical, laconic, and able to ride where others would not dare. Paterson''s poem mythologized the rural horseman as the archetypal Australian, the man who could ride "where the wild scrub horses are." The Bushman was the practical, laconic, self-sufficient figure who could survive anything the land threw at him. He was the "How" of the early population—the method of surviving the interior.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',573,'My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a small business owner who had to live and work within the community.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',0.8889,'My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(284,6,'Foundation','Cause.How.What','The Shearers'' Strike',0.8,0.7,'FAIL','**(Cause.How.What) The Shearers'' Strike (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Where has the spirit of the fair go gone? People used to leave their doors unlocked. Communities used to look after each other. That Australia still exists in the bush, but it is being destroyed in the cities." -National Press Club Address (2026)[^npc26]','The Shearers'' Strike: Unionism came to the Australian bushman as a religion... it had in it that feeling of mateship which counted for so much in the old days. -- Spence, founder of the Australian Workers'' Union, organized the Great Shearers'' Strike of 1891—the largest industrial action in Australian history—which, though crushed, gave birth to the Labor Party. The Great Shearers'' Strike of 1891 was the largest industrial action in Australian history, where pastoral workers across three colonies downed tools and demanded collective bargaining. It was crushed by troops and strikebreakers, but from its ashes rose the Labor Party.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',581,'Where has the spirit of the fair go gone? People used to leave their doors unlocked. Communities used to look after each other. That Australia still exists in the bush, but it is being destroyed in the cities.',1,'National Press Club Address (2026)','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','paraphrased',0.7895,'The Albanese Governments response to the coming of AI is largely to leave it in the hands of corporations with little regulation to ensure that the industry operates in the public interest.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(285,6,'Foundation','Cause.How.Where','The Bush (as Method)',0.7,0.5,'HIT','**(Cause.How.Where) The Bush (as Method) (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "I may be only a fish and chip shop lady, but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Bush (as Method): With stringybark and greenhide, our fathers conquered all. -- The song celebrates bush improvisation—stringybark (eucalyptus bark) and greenhide (raw cattle hide) could be fashioned into roofs, rope, saddles, and almost anything else when no shops or specialists existed within a hundred miles. The method of survival in the bush was improvisation—making tools, buildings, and solutions out of whatever was at hand. Stringybark (the bark of the eucalyptus) and greenhide (raw cattle hide) could be fashioned into almost anything, from roofs to rope.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',601,'I may be only a fish and chip shop lady, but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I may be only ''a fish and chip shop lady'', but some of these economists need to get their heads out of the textbooks and get a job in the real world.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(286,6,'Foundation','Cause.How.Why','The Secret Ballot',0.9,0.6,'HIT','**(Cause.How.Why) The Secret Ballot (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism. When have we been asked or consulted about our population?" -Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','The Secret Ballot: The ballot shall be prepared in a room to which no scrutineer shall have access, and... the elector shall alone enter the compartment. -- The "Victorian Ballot" (later known as the "Australian Ballot") was exported to Britain, the United States, and most democracies, ending the era when landlords could see how their tenants voted. Victoria was the first place in the world to implement the secret ballot for elections, ending the era of open voting where landlords could see how their tenants voted. It was quietly revolutionary, protecting the "Why" (the private vote) from the "Who" (the powerful).','Plane_6_Foundation.md',621,'Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism. When have we been asked or consulted about our population?',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'Australians have never been permitted to vote on immigration and multiculturalism.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(287,6,'Foundation','Cause.How.How','Compulsory Arbitration',0.8,0.5,'FAIL','**(Cause.How.How) Compulsory Arbitration (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake. They are waiting longer for their life-saving operation. The unemployment queues grow longer, and even longer when government jobs are given priority to migrants." -Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)[^ms16]','Compulsory Arbitration: We aim at establishing the rule of law in a new province, where it was not previously recognised—the province of industrial relations. -- Australia pioneered the system where labor disputes were settled not by strikes and lockouts, but by independent tribunals that set wages and conditions—the Arbitration Court as umpire between Capital and Labor. Australia pioneered the system where labor disputes were settled not by strikes and lockouts, but by independent tribunals that set wages and conditions. The Arbitration Court was the umpire between Capital and Labor.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',641,'High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake. They are waiting longer for their life-saving operation. The unemployment queues grow longer, and even longer when government jobs are given priority to migrants.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate, Hansard (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(288,6,'Foundation','Cause.How.Cause','The Colonial Secretary''s Office',-0.4,-0.4,'HIT','**(Cause.How.Cause) The Colonial Secretary''s Office (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Colonial Secretary''s Office: From the Right Honourable the Secretary of State for the Colonies, Downing Street, London. -- For 113 years, every significant decision required approval from London via multi-month sailing voyages, creating a culture of waiting for permission and managing upwards to the distant power. For 113 years, Australia was governed by instructions sent from London. Every significant decision had to be approved by the Colonial Office, creating a culture of waiting for permission, deferring to authority, and managing upwards to the distant power.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',661,'They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(289,6,'Foundation','Cause.How.Effect','Peaceful Federation',0.8,0.4,'FAIL','**(Cause.How.Effect) Peaceful Federation (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "A truly multicultural country can never be strong or united." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','Peaceful Federation: A continent for a nation and a nation for a continent. -- Unlike the American Union (born in revolution) or the German Union (born in conquest), Australian Federation was negotiated peacefully over a decade of conventions and ratified by democratic referendums in each colony between 1898-1900. No one died to create the nation. Unlike the American Union (born in war) or the German Union (born in conquest), the Australian Federation was negotiated peacefully over a decade of conferences and ratified by democratic referendums. No one died to create the nation.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',681,'A truly multicultural country can never be strong or united.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','paraphrased',0.8,'As a strong, united team I guarantee we will make a difference.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(290,6,'Foundation','Cause.Cause.Who','The Dreaming',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Cause.Cause.Who) The Dreaming (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Present governments are encouraging separatism in Australia by providing opportunities, land, moneys and facilities available only to Aboriginals." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Dreaming: The Rainbow Serpent came from beneath the ground and as it moved, it created the rivers, the valleys, and the mountains. -- The Indigenous cosmology posits that the landscape was shaped by ancestral beings during the Dreaming, and that these beings are still present in the land. The "Who" of the Deep Time is not human; it is Spirit. The Songlines are the maps of creator-being journeys, sung into existence.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',691,'Present governments are encouraging separatism in Australia by providing opportunities, land, moneys and facilities available only to Aboriginals.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Present governments are encouraging separatism in Australia by providing opportunities, land, moneys and facilities available only to Aboriginals.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(291,6,'Foundation','Cause.Cause.What','Gondwana',0.0,0.0,'FAIL','**(Cause.Cause.What) Gondwana (υ: 0.0, ψ: 0.0): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country." -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','Gondwana: Australia was once attached to Antarctica, and drifted north carrying a cargo of unique life that evolved in splendid isolation. -- Australia was once part of the supercontinent Gondwana, attached to Antarctica, Africa, and South America. When it broke off and drifted north, it carried a unique cargo of life that evolved in isolation—the marsupials, the eucalyptus, the venomous snakes.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',711,'Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country.',1,'Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country; hydro power like the Tully-Millstream project—why aren’t we doing these projects?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(292,6,'Foundation','Cause.Cause.Where','The Great Barrier Reef',0.8,0.4,'FAIL','**(Cause.Cause.Where) The Great Barrier Reef (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The government must be imaginative enough to become involved, in the short term at least, in job creating projects that will help establish the foundation for a resurgence of manufacturing." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Great Barrier Reef: A structure built entirely by living things, stretching 2,300 kilometers along the Queensland coast—the largest living structure on Earth, visible from space. -- The Reef is over 2,000 kilometers long and visible from space, a monument to 10,000 years of coral growth. It is the most complex ecosystem in the Australian realm, and its health is the indicator of the planet''s health.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',731,'The government must be imaginative enough to become involved, in the short term at least, in job creating projects that will help establish the foundation for a resurgence of manufacturing.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',0.9667,'The government must be imaginative enough to become involved, in the short term at least, in job creating projects that will help establish the foundation for a resurgence of national development and enterprise.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(293,6,'Foundation','Cause.Cause.Why','The Megafauna Extinction',-0.3,0.4,'FAIL','**(Cause.Cause.Why) The Megafauna Extinction (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals and Torres Strait Islanders are the most disadvantaged people in Australia." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Megafauna Extinction: Diprotodon, the giant wombat; Thylacoleo, the marsupial lion; the giant short-faced kangaroo—all gone within a few thousand years of human arrival. -- When humans first arrived, Australia was home to giant versions of familiar animals. Within a few thousand years, they were gone—likely victims of hunting and fire-stick farming. The "Why" of the deep past includes the First Extinction, the pruning of the ecosystem by the first Australians.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',751,'I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals and Torres Strait Islanders are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(294,6,'Foundation','Cause.Cause.How','Fire-Stick Farming',0.8,0.6,'FAIL','**(Cause.Cause.How) Fire-Stick Farming (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Reduced tariffs on foreign goods that compete with local products seem only to cost Australians their jobs. We must look after our own before lining the pockets of overseas countries and investors at the expense of our living standards and future." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96] -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)[^senate18tax]','Fire-Stick Farming: The Aboriginal people managed this continent with fire for tens of thousands of years, creating the park-like landscape the Europeans mistook for wilderness. -- Gammage''s research, using explorer journals, paintings, and ecological analysis, demonstrated that the "untouched" land the settlers saw was actually a garden. Gammage''s research showed that the Indigenous people actively managed the entire continent through controlled burns, creating the parkland landscape that the first Europeans mistook for "wilderness." The land was not wild; it was farmed.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',771,'Reduced tariffs on foreign goods that compete with local products seem only to cost Australians their jobs. We must look after our own before lining the pockets of overseas countries and investors at the expense of our living standards and future.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96] -Senate Speech: Corporate Tax Cuts (2018)','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','paraphrased',0.6585,'People ask me, ‘Why do we send billions overseas in the form of foreign aid?’ It’s a good question, isn’t it, especially when every single one of you drives past at least six homeless people sleeping near Outback Jacks on Northbourne Avenue here in Canberra.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(295,6,'Foundation','Cause.Cause.Cause','Plate Tectonics',0.0,0.0,'HIT','**(Cause.Cause.Cause) Plate Tectonics (υ: 0.0, ψ: 0.0): HIT.** **Quote:** "We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Plate Tectonics: The Indo-Australian Plate is pushing northward into Asia at approximately 7 centimeters per year, carrying the continent towards eventual collision with Indonesia. -- The entire continent sits on a tectonic plate that is pushing northward into Asia at 7cm per year. The geology—the ancient, eroded mountains, the flat plains, the mineral wealth—is the product of billions of years of planetary mechanics.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',791,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(296,6,'Foundation','Cause.Cause.Effect','The Arid Core',0.0,-0.3,'HIT','**(Cause.Cause.Effect) The Arid Core (υ: 0.0, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "The modernised Bradfield Scheme could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world." -Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)[^senate20jm]','The Arid Core: The Dead Heart—a place of red rock and silence, receiving less than 250mm of rain annually. -- The center of Australia is one of the driest places on Earth, receiving less than 250mm of rain per year. This aridity shaped everything: the population hugging the coast, the pastoral economy, the myth of the "Outback." The "Effect" of the geology is the desert.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',799,'The modernised Bradfield Scheme could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world.',1,'Senate Speech: Flawed JobMaker (2020)','senate20jm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate20jm.txt','verified',1.0,'It could irrigate such large parts of Central Queensland that it could become a food bowl not only for Australia but for the rest of the world.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(297,6,'Foundation','Cause.Effect.Who','The Digger (Myth)',0.6,0.4,'HIT','**(Cause.Effect.Who) The Digger (Myth) (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American salaries for the few and not much achieved for the many." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Digger (Myth): The Australian soldier is different from all others... the independent, self-reliant man who had to use his initiative. -- Bean, the official war correspondent and historian, almost single-handedly created the ANZAC Legend, elevating the men of Gallipoli from enlisted soldiers to secular saints. The immediate elevation of the Anzac soldier from "Enlisted Man" to "National Saint" created a secular pantheon to replace the kings we rejected. We needed a human face for the abstract Cause, so we turned the men of Gallipoli into marble statues.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',821,'Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American salaries for the few and not much achieved for the many.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',0.9189,'Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(298,6,'Foundation','Cause.Effect.What','Warrior \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.8,0.7,'FAIL','**(Cause.Effect.What) Warrior \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded industries that flourish in our society." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Warrior [First Nations Perspective]:  -- The Anzac legend celebrates the Australian soldier fighting for Empire in Turkey and France. It ignores the thousands of First Nations warriors—Pemulwuy, Yagan, Jandamarra—who fought a 140-year guerilla war against the British invasion on their own soil. Pemulwuy, the Bidjigal leader, led a resistance campaign for 12 years, famously surviving multiple severe wounds, leading to the belief he was bulletproof.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',841,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded industries that flourish in our society.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(299,6,'Foundation','Cause.Effect.Where','The Suburban House',0.5,-0.3,'HIT','**(Cause.Effect.Where) The Suburban House (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake." -Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)[^ms16]','The Suburban House: The Great Australian Dream is to own your own home. -- The result of the Fair Go and the Living Wage was a population of homeowners. The freestanding house on a quarter-acre block became the standard unit of Australian settlement, spreading across the coastal plains in a vast low-density sprawl.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',861,'High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake.',1,'Maiden Speech, Senate (2016)','ms16','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms16.txt','verified',1.0,'High immigration is only beneficial to multinationals, banks and big business, seeking a larger market while everyday Australians suffer from this massive intake.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(300,6,'Foundation','Cause.Effect.Why','The Welfare State',0.8,0.4,'HIT','**(Cause.Effect.Why) The Welfare State (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "There is a handout mentality in the third and fourth generations of this nation." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Welfare State: The Safety Net—no Australian should fall into poverty through circumstances beyond their control. -- Australia built a comprehensive welfare state guaranteeing a baseline of survival: pension, unemployment benefit, disability support, public healthcare. From the Age Pension (1909) to Medicare (1984), Australia built a comprehensive welfare state that guaranteed a baseline of survival. The Effect of the Fair Go is the safety net that catches the fallen, ensuring that no one starves in the Lucky Country.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',881,'There is a handout mentality in the third and fourth generations of this nation.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','paraphrased',0.7143,'This country of ours has the richest mineral deposits in the world and vast rich lands for agriculture and is surrounded by oceans that provide a wealth of seafood, yet we are $190 billion in debt with an interest bill that is strangling us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(301,6,'Foundation','Cause.Effect.How','Consensus',0.6,-0.2,'FAIL','**(Cause.Effect.How) Consensus (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \-0.2): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It is refreshing to be able to express my views without having to toe a party line. It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I would not have it any other way." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Consensus: The Australian Settlement was a set of interlocking policies—White Australia, Protection, Arbitration, State Paternalism—that governed Australia for most of the twentieth century. -- Kelly described how this "settlement" was a grand bargain that kept capital, labor, and government roughly satisfied for 90 years until the Hawke-Keating reforms. Paul Kelly described the interlocking policies of White Australia, Protectionism, Arbitration, and State Paternalism as a "Settlement" that governed Australia for most of the 20th century. It was a grand bargain that kept everyone roughly happy.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',889,'It is refreshing to be able to express my views without having to toe a party line. It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I would not have it any other way.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'It is refreshing to be able to express my views without having to toe a party line.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(302,6,'Foundation','Cause.Effect.Cause','The Unfinished Business',0.8,0.7,'FAIL','**(Cause.Effect.Cause) The Unfinished Business (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','The Unfinished Business: We seek constitutional reforms to empower our people and take a rightful place in our own country. When we have power over our destiny our children will flourish. -- The Statement calls for Voice, Treaty, Truth—the unfinished work of Reconciliation, the acknowledgment that the foundation is still cracked. The Statement calls for a constitutionally enshrined Voice to Parliament, a Makarrata Commission, and a truth-telling process. It represents the unfinished work of Reconciliation, the acknowledgment that the Cause has not yet been fully repaired.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',909,'Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Reconciliation is everyone recognising and treating each other as equals, and everyone must be responsible for their own actions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(303,6,'Foundation','Cause.Effect.Effect','Continuity',0.7,0.4,'HIT','**(Cause.Effect.Effect) Continuity (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent, and my greatest desire is to see all Australians benefit from living in this wonderful country." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)[^ms96]','Continuity: Australia has maintained continuous democratic government since Federation in 1901—no coups, no civil wars, no constitutional collapses. -- Despite world wars, depressions, and cultural revolutions, the system has kept running. The Constitution has been amended only 8 times in 123 years, and every transfer of power has been peaceful. Despite world wars, depressions, and cultural revolutions, Australia has maintained continuous democratic government since 1901. We have never had a coup, a civil war (since Eureka), or a constitutional crisis that broke the machine. The system has kept running.','Plane_6_Foundation.md',929,'I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent, and my greatest desire is to see all Australians benefit from living in this wonderful country.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',0.9394,'I consider myself just an ordinary Australian who wants to keep this great country strong and independent, and my greatest desire is to see all Australians treat each other as equals as we travel together towards the new century.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(304,7,'Result','Effect.Who.Who','The Quiet Australian',0.3,-0.4,'HIT','**(Effect.Who.Who) The Quiet Australian (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "For far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Quiet Australian: The Quiet Australians who have worked hard, who have paid their taxes, who have invested for their future. It is for them that we have done this. -- After a surprise election win that defied all polls, Morrison invoked the "Quiet Australian" as the forgotten voter—suburban, mortgage-paying, skeptical of elite activism—who decided the result in silence. Morrison''s invocation of the "Quiet Australian" defined the central agent of modern politics: the suburban homeowner who pays their mortgage, minds their own business, and resents being lectured by elites. This figure replaced the "Working Class" as the political subject, shifting the locus of identity from the factory to the cul-de-sac.','Plane_7_Result.md',5,'For far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Immigration and multiculturalism are issues that this government is trying to address, but for far too long ordinary Australians have been kept out of any debate by the major parties.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(305,7,'Result','Effect.Who.What','The Multicultural Citizen',0.8,0.5,'FAIL','**(Effect.Who.What) The Multicultural Citizen (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "A truly multicultural country can never be strong or united." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Multicultural Citizen: We are one, but we are many / And from all the lands on earth we come. -- The song became the unofficial second anthem, sung at citizenship ceremonies and school assemblies, celebrating the mosaic of cultures that now define the nation after the dismantling of White Australia in 1973. The song became the unofficial second anthem, celebrating the mosaic of cultures that now define the nation. From Greek to Vietnamese to Lebanese, the "Who" of Australia is no longer monochrome. The dismantling of White Australia in 1973 produced a new "What"—a diverse population that retains ethnic identity within a civic framework.','Plane_7_Result.md',25,'A truly multicultural country can never be strong or united.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'A truly multicultural country can never be strong or united.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(306,7,'Result','Effect.Who.Where','The Coastal Dweller',0.2,-0.3,'HIT','**(Effect.Who.Where) The Coastal Dweller (υ: \+0.2, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "There is a housing crisis. But the not so smart thinkers in the Albanese Government make changes to negative gearing. If you make changes to negative gearing, investment will move away from housing... Unsustainable demand is being driven by several factors, but the biggest is high immigration." -National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026[^npc26]','The Coastal Dweller: The sea change phenomenon: Australians abandoning the cities for coastal towns in search of lifestyle. -- The phrase captured the post-industrial migration trend, though it obscures the larger truth: 85% of Australians live within 50km of the coast, making Australia one of the most urbanized and coastal nations on Earth, clinging to the edge of an empty continent. Over 85% of Australians live within 50km of the coast, and the population continues to concentrate in the capital cities. The "Where" of the Result is the narrow fringe, the "Sandgroper" and the "Sydney-sider" clinging to the edge of the continent. The interior remains empty.','Plane_7_Result.md',45,'There is a housing crisis. But the not so smart thinkers in the Albanese Government make changes to negative gearing. If you make changes to negative gearing, investment will move away from housing... Unsustainable demand is being driven by several factors, but the biggest is high immigration.',1,'National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'But the not so smart thinkers in the Albanese Government make changes to negative gearing.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(307,7,'Result','Effect.Who.Why','The Aspirational',-0.4,0.7,'HIT','**(Effect.Who.Why) The Aspirational (υ: \-0.4, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','The Aspirational: The Aspirational Voter—they want to get ahead, not just get by. -- Coined to describe working-class Australians who shifted from Labor to Liberal, prioritizing personal wealth creation (second investment property, private school fees) over traditional union solidarity. "Howard''s Battlers" became the pivotal electoral demographic. John Howard''s political genius was to identify a new "Why" for the Australian working class: not solidarity but aspiration, not redistribution but wealth creation. The "Aspie" wanted to move up, to own a second property, to send their kids to private school. They were "Howard''s Battlers"—Labor voters who switched to Liberal.','Plane_7_Result.md',65,'My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'My view on issues is based on commonsense, and my experience as a mother of four children, as a sole parent, and as a businesswoman running a fish and chip shop.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(308,7,'Result','Effect.Who.How','The Sports Fanatic',0.3,0.6,'HIT','**(Effect.Who.How) The Sports Fanatic (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "I will fight hard to keep my seat in this place, but that will depend on the people who sent me here." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Sports Fanatic: C''mon Aussie, C''mon, C''mon / C''mon Aussie, C''mon! -- Kerry Packer''s breakaway cricket competition used this earworm to brand Australian sporting identity, and it became the template for turning sport into secular religion—the primary ritual calendar (AFL Grand Final, Melbourne Cup, State of Origin) and mythology (Bradman, Cathy Freeman, the Ashes). Sport is the secular religion of Australia, providing the primary ritual calendar (AFL Grand Final, Melbourne Cup, State of Origin) and the primary mythology (the Ashes, Bradman, Cathy Freeman). The "How" of Australian identity is enacted on the oval, the court, and the track.','Plane_7_Result.md',85,'I will fight hard to keep my seat in this place, but that will depend on the people who sent me here.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I will fight hard to keep my seat in this place, but that will depend on the people who sent me here.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(309,7,'Result','Effect.Who.Cause','The Digger''s Heir',0.5,-0.2,'FAIL','**(Effect.Who.Cause) The Digger''s Heir (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.2): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We oppose entirely people coming into this country and bringing with them the troubles they have left behind; coming to this country and ignoring our values, our language, our traditions, our dress and the fact that we are predominately a Judeo-Christian society." -National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026[^npc26]','The Digger''s Heir: They shall grow not old, as we that are left grow old: Age shall not weary them, nor the years condemn. -- Adopted as the sacred verse of the ANZAC tradition, recited at every Dawn Service on April 25th. The "Digger''s Heir" is the grandchild wearing the medals of the dead, inheriting glory without paying the price. The descendant of the original ANZAC carries the ghost of sacrifice. The "ANZAC Day March" is paraded by grandchildren and great-grandchildren wearing the medals of the dead. The Cause of the national identity is remembered through the Heir, who inherits the glory without paying the price.','Plane_7_Result.md',105,'We oppose entirely people coming into this country and bringing with them the troubles they have left behind; coming to this country and ignoring our values, our language, our traditions, our dress and the fact that we are predominately a Judeo-Christian society.',1,'National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'We oppose entirely people coming into this country and bringing with them the troubles they have left behind; coming to this country and ignoring our values, our language, our traditions, our dress and the fact that we are predominately a Judeo-Christian society.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(310,7,'Result','Effect.Who.Effect','The Citizen',0.9,0.4,'FAIL','**(Effect.Who.Effect) The Citizen (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Citizen: I pledge my loyalty to Australia and its people, whose democratic beliefs I share, whose rights and liberties I respect, and whose laws I will uphold and obey. -- The Citizenship Ceremony, held at town halls and Australia Day events, is the formal ritual of conversion from "Immigrant" to "Australian"—the moment when the outsider becomes legally and symbolically an insider. The final product of the Australian system is the Citizen—the legal bearer of rights and duties, bound by law and entitled to vote. The Citizenship Ceremony, with its oath to "share Australian democratic beliefs," is the formal ritual of conversion, turning the "Immigrant" into the "Australian."','Plane_7_Result.md',125,'I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I must stress at this stage that I do not consider those people from ethnic backgrounds currently living in Australia anything but first-class citizens, provided of course that they give this country their full, undivided loyalty.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(311,7,'Result','Effect.Where.Who','The Australian Diaspora',0.4,0.5,'FAIL','**(Effect.Where.Who) The Australian Diaspora (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Australian Diaspora: To live in Australia permanently is rather like going to a party and dancing all night with one''s mother. -- The comic genius who created Dame Edna became the most famous expatriate of his generation, spending decades in London while remaining quintessentially Australian. His wry observation captures why over a million Australians live abroad—the suffocating familiarity of home. Over a million Australians live abroad, forming influential networks in London, New York, Hong Kong, and Singapore. Barry Humphries, Clive James, Germaine Greer—the great expatriates fled for London, not to abandon Australia but to escape its comforting provincialism. They carry Australian values into global institutions, acting as soft power ambassadors who need distance to see home clearly.','Plane_7_Result.md',147,'Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Australia must review its membership and funding of the UN, as it is a little like ATSIC on a grander scale, with huge tax-free American dollar salaries, duty-free luxury cars and diplomatic status.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(312,7,'Result','Effect.Where.What','The Commodity',-0.3,0.6,'HIT','**(Effect.Where.What) The Commodity (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "We want more gas, more oil, and more energy to drive our economy forward, pay down our debts, and secure our energy future... This will be the first time that Australians have a genuine ownership stake in the nation''s natural resources." -One Nation Gas Policy launch, onenation.org.au, unveiled at the Australian Energy Producers Conference, Adelaide, 21 May 2026[^onenation_anwic][^energy26]','The Commodity: The fine wool of New South Wales will prove more valuable than all its gold. -- The "Father of Australian Wool" prophetically valued the sustainable fleece over the extractive rush. He proved right: wool funded the colony long after the gold faded. From wool to iron ore, Australia''s primary impact on the global economy has always been through raw materials—we dig it up and ship it out. Australia''s primary impact on the global economy is through raw materials—we dig them up and ship them out. The nation "rode on the sheep''s back" for a century before transitioning to iron ore, coal, and LNG. The "What" of Australia''s global footprint is the physical stuff that fuels China''s construction boom and Japan''s power grid. We remain the Quarry of the World.','Plane_7_Result.md',167,'We want more gas, more oil, and more energy to drive our economy forward, pay down our debts, and secure our energy future... This will be the first time that Australians have a genuine ownership stake in the nation''s natural resources.',1,'One Nation Gas Policy launch, onenation.org.au, unveiled at the Australian Energy Producers Conference, Adelaide, 21 May 2026[^onenation_anwic]','energy26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/energy26.txt','paraphrased',0.7619,'“We want more gas, more oil and more energy to drive our economy forward,” she said.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(313,7,'Result','Effect.Where.Where','The Alliance',-0.2,-0.5,'HIT','**(Effect.Where.Where) The Alliance (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \-0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** Hanson''s Senate voting record and public statements show consistent opposition to Chinese government-linked investment in Australian ports, agricultural land, and critical infrastructure, framed as incompatible with Australia''s Five Eyes and ANZUS alliance obligations. -Senate speeches and voting record, 2016-2026[^wiki][^tvfy]','The Alliance: The ANZUS Treaty: a security alliance between Australia, New Zealand, and the United States. -- Article IV states: "Each Party recognizes that an armed attack in the Pacific Area on any of the Parties would be dangerous to its own peace and safety." Since 1951, Australia has fought in every American war—Korea, Vietnam, Afghanistan, Iraq—as the price of the security guarantee, tethering Canberra to Washington. Australia''s "Where" in the geopolitical map is defined by its alliance with the United States. Since 1951, Australian security policy has been tethered to Washington. We have fought in every American war since WWII—Korea, Vietnam, Afghanistan, Iraq—as the price of the security guarantee.','Plane_7_Result.md',187,'Hanson''s Senate voting record and public statements show consistent opposition to Chinese government-linked investment in Australian ports, agricultural land, and critical infrastructure, framed as incompatible with Australia''s Five Eyes and ANZUS alliance obligations.',0,'Senate speeches and voting record, 2016-2026[^wiki]','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','paraphrased',0.1389,'TITLE: Pauline Hanson - Voting Record Overview',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(314,7,'Result','Effect.Where.Why','The Middle Power',0.7,0.5,'FAIL','**(Effect.Where.Why) The Middle Power (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I am going to find out how many treaties we have signed with the UN, have them exposed and then call for their repudiation." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Middle Power: Australia as a creative middle power—punching above our weight through diplomacy, not military force. -- Evans championed the Cairns Group (agricultural trade), APEC (regional cooperation), and the Cambodia peace settlement. The "Good International Citizen" finds purpose by solving problems the Great Powers ignore—brokerage, mediation, coalition-building. Gareth Evans articulated a role for Australia as a "Good International Citizen," punching above its weight in international forums. We cannot dominate, but we can mediate. We cannot lead, but we can build coalitions. The Cairns Group, APEC, and the Cambodia peace settlement were examples of this diplomacy.','Plane_7_Result.md',207,'I am going to find out how many treaties we have signed with the UN, have them exposed and then call for their repudiation.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I am going to find out how many treaties we have signed with the UN, have them exposed and then call for their repudiation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(315,7,'Result','Effect.Where.How','Soft Power',0.6,0.3,'FAIL','**(Effect.Where.How) Soft Power (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** Hanson has argued that free trade agreements have facilitated the importation of cheap foreign labour at the expense of Australian workers, treating trade policy as a vector for wage suppression rather than economic growth. -Senate speeches and voting record, 2016-2026[^wiki][^tvfy]','Soft Power: Where the bloody hell are you? -- The slogan (delivered by model Lara Bingle) encapsulated the laid-back, provocative, slightly irreverent Australian brand. Australia''s global image is beaches, wildlife, and relaxed fun—the opposite of threat or intimidation. We attract tourists, students, and migrants through seduction, not coercion. Australia''s global image is beaches, wildlife, and laid-back fun—the opposite of threat or intimidation. The "How" of our influence is through attraction, not coercion. We are liked because we are non-threatening—the friendly neighbor, not the bullying hegemon.','Plane_7_Result.md',227,'Hanson has argued that free trade agreements have facilitated the importation of cheap foreign labour at the expense of Australian workers, treating trade policy as a vector for wage suppression rather than economic growth.',0,'Senate speeches and voting record, 2016-2026[^wiki]','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','paraphrased',0.0882,'They Vote For You Senator Pauline Hanson voting record overview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(316,7,'Result','Effect.Where.Cause','The Pacific',-0.3,0.4,'FAIL','**(Effect.Where.Cause) The Pacific (υ: \-0.3, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** Hanson has consistently framed Australia''s resource wealth as a strategic vulnerability, arguing that without sovereignty over its own assets, neighbouring powers will exercise economic and geopolitical control over the nation. -Senate speeches, 2016-2026[^wiki][^onenation]','The Pacific: The Pacific Step-Up: Australia''s renewed commitment to our Pacific family. -- Increased aid, diplomatic posts, and infrastructure loans to Papua New Guinea, Fiji, Tonga, Vanuatu, and Solomon Islands. The "Cause" is strategic: these islands sit between Australia and the world. We compete with China for influence on our doorstep, treating the region as our natural sphere. Australia''s immediate neighborhood—Papua New Guinea, Fiji, Tonga, Vanuatu—is the closest expression of our foreign policy responsibility. The "Cause" of our interest is geography: they are the "Where" between us and the world. We compete with China for influence in these small island nations.','Plane_7_Result.md',247,'Hanson has consistently framed Australia''s resource wealth as a strategic vulnerability, arguing that without sovereignty over its own assets, neighbouring powers will exercise economic and geopolitical control over the nation.',0,'Senate speeches, 2016-2026[^wiki]','onenation','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation.txt','paraphrased',0.3871,'Visible content: "LOWERING PRICES FOR HOUSEHOLDS, BUSINESSES AND INDUSTRIES / READ MORE" (a single policy tile headline, likely the first of several tiles that load individually via JS as the user scrolls; the accessibility/text-extraction pass only captured this one visible tile).',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(317,7,'Result','Effect.Where.Effect','The Asian Century',0.5,0.4,'FAIL','**(Effect.Where.Effect) The Asian Century (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** Hanson has said her 1996 warning about being "swamped by Asians" was not disrespect but a warning about the pace of demographic change, and that her later statements about Muslim immigration applied the same logic to a different community. -Public statements defending her Maiden Speech, cited widely[^wiki]','The Asian Century: Australia in the Asian Century. -- The document declared: "The Asian century is an Australian opportunity... by 2025, four of the world''s five largest economies will be in Asia." It recognized that Australia''s future is inextricably linked to China, India, and Indonesia—we cannot pretend to be European in an Asian sea. The recognition that Australia''s future is inextricably linked to the rise of Asia. The "Effect" of the geography is that we cannot pretend to be European. The 21st century will be Asian, and Australia must find its place in a region it has historically feared.','Plane_7_Result.md',267,'Hanson has said her 1996 warning about being "swamped by Asians" was not disrespect but a warning about the pace of demographic change, and that her later statements about Muslim immigration applied the same logic to a different community.',0,'Public statements defending her Maiden Speech, cited widely','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','paraphrased',0.8462,'However, the prime minister at the time, John Howard, refused to censure Hanson or speak critically about her, acknowledging that her views were shared by many Australians, [[ 19 ]]() commenting that he saw the expression of such views as evidence that the "pall of political correctness" had been lifted in Australia, and that Australians could now "speak a little more freely and a little more openly about what they feel".',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(318,7,'Result','Effect.What.Who','The Home Owner',-0.2,0.5,'HIT','**(Effect.What.Who) The Home Owner (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "For the majority of Australians however, high immigration means poorly paid jobs, high electricity and water prices, unaffordable housing, long wait times for access to health services, insufficient money for schools and congestion on public transport and our roads." -Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", senatorhanson.com.au (22 Aug 2018)[^senate18imm]','The Home Owner: The Great Australian Dream: to own your own home on your own block of land. -- Home ownership rates peaked at 71% in 1966, remained above 65% into the 2020s. The freestanding house on a quarter-acre block—the suburban ideal—is the tangible proof of the Fair Go, the mortgage the sacred contract, the title deed the holy scroll. The "What" that defines Australian success is property ownership—the freestanding house on the quarter-acre block. The Home Owner is the completed Agent, having achieved the tangible proof of the Fair Go. The mortgage is the sacred contract, the title deed is the holy scroll.','Plane_7_Result.md',289,'For the majority of Australians however, high immigration means poorly paid jobs, high electricity and water prices, unaffordable housing, long wait times for access to health services, insufficient money for schools and congestion on public transport and our roads.',1,'Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", senatorhanson.com.au (22 Aug 2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',1.0,'For the majority of Australians however, high immigration means poorly paid jobs, high electricity and water prices, unaffordable housing , long wait times for access to health services, insufficient money for schools and congestion on public transport and our roads.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:39');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(319,7,'Result','Effect.What.What','The Superannuation Balance',0.7,0.6,'FAIL','**(Effect.What.What) The Superannuation Balance (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.6): FAIL.** **Quote:** Hanson supported the 2020 COVID-19 early superannuation release scheme allowing members to withdraw up to $20,000 from retirement savings, and has periodically proposed allowing first-home buyers to access superannuation for housing deposits. -Senate voting record and public statements, 2020-2026[^tvfy][^wiki]','The Superannuation Balance: The Superannuation Guarantee: employers must contribute a percentage of wages to employees'' retirement savings. -- Initially at 3%, rising to 12% by 2025, compulsory super created one of the world''s largest pools of investment capital (~$3.5 trillion by 2024), the deferred Fair Go guaranteeing that old age will not mean poverty. Compulsory superannuation is the "What" that Australia exports as a policy model. By forcing employers to contribute to retirement savings, the nation created one of the largest pools of investment capital in the world (~$3.5 trillion). The "What" is now a financial behemoth.','Plane_7_Result.md',309,'Hanson supported the 2020 COVID-19 early superannuation release scheme allowing members to withdraw up to $20,000 from retirement savings, and has periodically proposed allowing first-home buyers to access superannuation for housing deposits.',0,'Senate voting record and public statements, 2020-2026[^tvfy]','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','paraphrased',0.7714,'[[ 167 ]]() She is also said to have "used the crisis to call for Australia to withdraw from its free trade agreement with China, has urged Australians to boycott products made in China, called for the immediate suspension of all Chinese foreign investment into Australia and suggested that backpackers and foreign workers should be denied welfare assistance and called for Australia to cease all foreign aid".',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(320,7,'Result','Effect.What.Where','The University Sector',0.3,0.5,'HIT','**(Effect.What.Where) The University Sector (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** Hanson has criticised Australian universities for prioritising foreign student revenue over domestic students and national security, calling for stronger controls on Chinese government influence in Australian academic institutions. -Senate committee contributions, 2019-2021[^wiki]','The University Sector: Education is Australia''s third-largest export industry, worth $40 billion annually at peak. -- Australian degrees are the "What" we sell to the world—Group of Eight universities, pathway visas, the promise of migration. The university campus is a factory for exporting credentials. International education is a massive industry, with over 700,000 international students pre-pandemic. Australian degrees are the "What" we sell to the world. The "Where" of the university campus is a factory for exporting credentials.','Plane_7_Result.md',329,'Hanson has criticised Australian universities for prioritising foreign student revenue over domestic students and national security, calling for stronger controls on Chinese government influence in Australian academic institutions.',0,'Senate committee contributions, 2019-2021','wiki','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/wiki.txt','paraphrased',0.7143,'In June 2021, following media reports that the proposed national curriculum was "preoccupied with the oppression, discrimination and struggles of Indigenous Australians ", the Australian Senate approved a motion tabled by Hanson calling on the federal government to reject critical race theory , despite it not being included in the curriculum.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(321,7,'Result','Effect.What.Why','The Medicare Card',0.9,0.5,'FAIL','**(Effect.What.Why) The Medicare Card (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** Hanson has argued that welfare and health services should be prioritised for Australian citizens and long-term residents, expressing concern about recent arrivals accessing Medicare-funded services before establishing sufficient contribution history. -Senate speeches and voting record, 2016-2026[^wiki][^tvfy]','The Medicare Card: Medicare: universal healthcare for all Australians. -- The green card guarantees access to healthcare regardless of wealth—bulk-billed GP visits, free public hospitals—the material embodiment of the Fair Go in hospitals and clinics. Medicare is the "What" of the Australian welfare state—the card that guarantees access to healthcare regardless of wealth. The "Why" of the system is not profit but health. It is the material embodiment of the Fair Go in hospitals and clinics.','Plane_7_Result.md',349,'Hanson has argued that welfare and health services should be prioritised for Australian citizens and long-term residents, expressing concern about recent arrivals accessing Medicare-funded services before establishing sufficient contribution history.',0,'Senate speeches and voting record, 2016-2026[^wiki]','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','paraphrased',0.0938,'They Vote For You Senator Pauline Hanson voting record overview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(322,7,'Result','Effect.What.How','The Renewable Transition',0.8,0.7,'FAIL','**(Effect.What.How) The Renewable Transition (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.7): FAIL.** **Quote:** "One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery, grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even government underwriting anything that sponsors the net zero hoax." -National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026[^npc26]','The Renewable Transition: Australia has the highest per-capita rate of rooftop solar installation in the world. -- Over 3 million households had rooftop solar by 2023, generating a distributed energy revolution. The "What" being produced is increasingly kilowatt-hours from the sun, creating tension between the old extractive economy (coal exports) and the new domestic reality (renewable uptake). Australia has the highest per-capita rate of rooftop solar installation in the world. The "How" of the everyday Australian is now increasingly decarbonized. The "What" being produced is kilowatt-hours from the sun.','Plane_7_Result.md',369,'One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery, grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even government underwriting anything that sponsors the net zero hoax.',1,'National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'One Nation will end this renewable energy bribery – grants, tax incentives, concessional finance, even the government underwriting anything that sponsors the whole net zero hoax.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(323,7,'Result','Effect.What.Cause','Biodiversity',0.7,-0.2,'FAIL','**(Effect.What.Cause) Biodiversity (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \-0.2): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Why aren''t we duplicating the Bruce Highway from Brisbane to Cairns for tourism and freight? Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country; hydro power like the Tully-Millstream project, why aren''t we doing these projects?" -Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018[^senate18tax]','Biodiversity: The koala, the platypus, the kangaroo, the echidna—species that exist nowhere else on Earth. -- This biodiversity is both national symbol and ecological responsibility; 83% of mammals, 89% of reptiles, and 93% of frogs are endemic. We are custodians of an evolutionary miracle. Australia''s unique flora and fauna are the "What" that we inherited, not created. The isolation of Gondwana produced a living laboratory of evolution. This biodiversity is both a national symbol and an ecological responsibility.','Plane_7_Result.md',389,'Why aren''t we duplicating the Bruce Highway from Brisbane to Cairns for tourism and freight? Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country; hydro power like the Tully-Millstream project, why aren''t we doing these projects?',1,'Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'Coal-fired power stations to produce the dispatchable energy that we need to reduce the power prices in this country; hydro power like the Tully-Millstream project—why aren’t we doing these projects?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(324,7,'Result','Effect.What.Effect','Stability',0.6,0.4,'FAIL','**(Effect.What.Effect) Stability (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I do not feel we can go on living in a dream world forever and a day believing that war will never touch our lives again." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Stability: Australia: 32 years without a recession (1991-2020)—the longest unbroken economic expansion in the developed world. -- Only COVID-19 finally broke the streak. The "What" of the Effect was simply: it worked. The economy grew, living standards rose, and the machine kept running. This created national complacency but also a genuine achievement—we kept the machine running longer than anyone else. Until COVID, Australia had the longest unbroken economic expansion in the developed world. The "What" of the Effect was simply: it worked. The economy grew, living standards rose, and the machine kept running.','Plane_7_Result.md',409,'I do not feel we can go on living in a dream world forever and a day believing that war will never touch our lives again.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'This could be a civil service with a touch of military training, because I do not feel we can go on living in a dream world forever and a day believing that war will never touch our lives again.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(325,7,'Result','Effect.Why.Who','Egalitarianism vs. Aspiration',0.0,0.0,'FAIL','**(Effect.Why.Who) Egalitarianism vs. Aspiration (υ: 0.0, ψ: 0.0): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','Egalitarianism vs. Aspiration: Tall Poppy Syndrome: the Australian tendency to cut down those who rise too high versus the Battler''s right to aspire. -- The central tension of the Australian character is between the leveling impulse (resent success) and the aspirational impulse (celebrate success), creating a narrow band of acceptable achievement. The central tension of the Australian character is between the leveling impulse (cut down the tall poppy) and the aspirational impulse (rise up from battler to success). These two forces pull against each other, creating a narrow band of acceptable achievement.','Plane_7_Result.md',431,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'We now have a situation where a type of reverse racism is applied to mainstream Australians by those who promote political correctness and those who control the various taxpayer funded ''industries'' that flourish in our society servicing Aboriginals, multiculturalists and a host of other minority groups.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(326,7,'Result','Effect.Why.What','Sustainability vs. Extraction',0.5,-0.2,'FAIL','**(Effect.Why.What) Sustainability vs. Extraction (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \-0.2): FAIL.** **Quote:** "America has half-price energy. There''s your problem. Reduce the cost of energy in Australia, so industries and manufacturing can compete, instead of escalating prices." -Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018[^senate18tax]','Sustainability vs. Extraction: The Climate Wars: Australia''s decade-long political paralysis over climate and energy policy. -- The conflict between the coal economy (Australia''s biggest export) and the climate crisis (existential threat) defines the central evaluation of the Australian "What." The judgment is unresolved; the climate wars continue. The conflict between the coal economy and the climate crisis defines the central evaluation of the Australian "What." We judge our effect by whether we are destroying the planet for short-term profit or building a sustainable future.','Plane_7_Result.md',451,'America has half-price energy. There''s your problem. Reduce the cost of energy in Australia, so industries and manufacturing can compete, instead of escalating prices.',1,'Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'Reduce the cost of energy in Australia, so industries and manufacturing can compete, instead of escalating prices.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(327,7,'Result','Effect.Why.Where','Urban vs. Regional',0.0,0.0,'HIT','**(Effect.Why.Where) Urban vs. Regional (υ: 0.0, ψ: 0.0): HIT.** **Quote:** Documented position, Hanson has argued that the immigration intake imports workers into cities rather than addressing genuine regional labour shortages, treating population growth as a substitute for redeploying Australia''s own unemployed. -Senate contributions on immigration and regional labour, 2016-2026[^wiki][^tvfy]','Urban vs. Regional: The Bush vs. The City: two Australias that vote differently, think differently, and resent each other. -- 90% of Australians live in urban areas, but political mythology remains heavily rural (the Drover, the Stockman, the Man from Snowy River). The Nationals represent rural interests; the Greens represent inner-city interests. The nation is judged by how well it reconciles these two Australias. Australia''s population is heavily urban, but its political mythology is heavily rural. This creates a permanent tension between the needs of the cities (infrastructure, density) and the mythology of the bush (independence, resource extraction).','Plane_7_Result.md',471,'Documented position, Hanson has argued that the immigration intake imports workers into cities rather than addressing genuine regional labour shortages, treating population growth as a substitute for redeploying Australia''s own unemployed.',0,'Senate contributions on immigration and regional labour, 2016-2026[^wiki]','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','paraphrased',0.0938,'They Vote For You Senator Pauline Hanson voting record overview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(328,7,'Result','Effect.Why.Why','Fair Go vs. Market',0.0,0.0,'HIT','**(Effect.Why.Why) Fair Go vs. Market (υ: 0.0, ψ: 0.0): HIT.** **Quote:** "Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Fair Go vs. Market: Social Democracy vs. Neoliberalism: the debate over whether government ensures equity or the market ensures efficiency. -- The Hawke-Keating reforms (1983-1996) moved Australia towards the market (tariff reduction, privatization, floating the dollar); the welfare state (Medicare, NDIS) pulled back towards equity. The nation oscillates, never fully committing to either pole. The evaluation of the Australian economy oscillates between two poles: the Fair Go (government ensures equity) and the Market (competition ensures efficiency). The judgment is whether policies serve the collective or the individual, the weak or the strong.','Plane_7_Result.md',491,'Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Along with millions of Australians, I am fed up to the back teeth with the inequalities that are being promoted by the government and paid for by the taxpayer under the assumption that Aboriginals are the most disadvantaged people in Australia.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(329,7,'Result','Effect.Why.How','Reconciliation vs. Denial',0.7,-0.4,'FAIL','**(Effect.Why.How) Reconciliation vs. Denial (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \-0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Reconciliation vs. Denial: The History Wars: the battle over how Australia should remember its treatment of Indigenous people. -- The debate divides those who demand truth-telling, apology, and reparation (Reconciliation) from those who insist the country should "move on" and not be "lectured" about the past (Denial). The judgment is the temperature of the national soul. The evaluation of Australia''s treatment of Indigenous people is the deepest wound in the national conscience. We judge ourselves by whether we are moving towards Reconciliation (truth-telling, reparation) or remaining in Denial (forgetting, minimizing).','Plane_7_Result.md',511,'This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'This nation is being divided into black and white, and the present system encourages this.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(330,7,'Result','Effect.Why.Cause','Luck vs. Effort',0.4,-0.3,'FAIL','**(Effect.Why.Cause) Luck vs. Effort (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Put bluntly, these figures derive because of one policy above all others: the hoax of global warming which is now climate change. It has produced an increase in energy costs which has taken Australia into energy poverty." -National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026[^npc26]','Luck vs. Effort: Australia is a lucky country run mainly by second-rate people who share its luck. -- Horne intended this as a critique—we coast on resources without developing real industry or intellect. The central causal question: is Australian prosperity *earned* (policy, work ethic, innovation) or merely *inherited* (resources, geography, timing)? The answer determines whether we can claim virtue or merely gratitude. Horne''s critique asked whether Australia''s prosperity was *earned* or merely *lucked into*. If it was luck (resources, geography, timing), then we have no right to complacency. If it was effort (policy, work ethic, innovation), then we can take credit.','Plane_7_Result.md',531,'Put bluntly, these figures derive because of one policy above all others: the hoax of global warming which is now climate change. It has produced an increase in energy costs which has taken Australia into energy poverty.',1,'National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'Put bluntly, these figures derive because of one policy, above all others, the hoax of global warming which is now climate change.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(331,7,'Result','Effect.Why.Effect','Unity vs. Division',0.0,0.0,'HIT','**(Effect.Why.Effect) Unity vs. Division (υ: 0.0, ψ: 0.0): HIT.** **Quote:** "At the centre of this crisis is the utterly flawed policy of multiculturalism. We cannot be a multicultural society. We are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural. Australians must live under the one cultural umbrella." -National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026[^npc26]','Unity vs. Division: E Pluribus Unum (Australian version): are we ''One and Free'' as the anthem claims, or fragmenting along lines of class, race, geography, and ideology? -- The question of whether the nation holds together or splinters remains unanswered. The ultimate judgment is whether the nation holds together or splinters. Are we "One and Free" as the anthem claims, or are we fragmenting along lines of class, race, geography, and ideology? The Effect is judged by its cohesion.','Plane_7_Result.md',551,'At the centre of this crisis is the utterly flawed policy of multiculturalism. We cannot be a multicultural society. We are a multiracial society, but we must be monocultural. Australians must live under the one cultural umbrella.',1,'National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'At the centre of this crisis is the utterly flawed policy of multiculturalism.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(332,7,'Result','Effect.How.Who','The Vote',0.8,0.6,'HIT','**(Effect.How.Who) The Vote (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.6): HIT.** **Quote:** "I won the seat of Oxley largely on an issue that has resulted in me being called a racist. That issue related to my comment that Aboriginals received more benefits than non-Aboriginals." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Vote: The Preferential Ballot: voters rank candidates in order of preference, with eliminations and redistributions until a majority is reached. -- Unlike first-past-the-post systems, preferential voting forces coalition-building and excludes extremists. The "How" of Australian democracy produces centrist governments that must appeal to the median voter—we judge our leaders by a complex **calculus** of preference. Australia''s voting system allows for preference distribution, meaning the voter can rank candidates rather than pick just one. This produces centrist outcomes, as extremists are excluded by preference flows to moderates. The "How" of judgment is the sophisticated ballot.','Plane_7_Result.md',573,'I won the seat of Oxley largely on an issue that has resulted in me being called a racist. That issue related to my comment that Aboriginals received more benefits than non-Aboriginals.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'I won the seat of Oxley largely on an issue that has resulted in me being called a racist.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(333,7,'Result','Effect.How.What','The Royal Commission',0.7,0.7,'HIT','**(Effect.How.What) The Royal Commission (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "I am calling for ATSIC to be abolished. It is a failed, hypocritical and discriminatory organisation that has failed dismally the people it was meant to serve." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Royal Commission: Let''s have a Royal Commission—the reflexive Australian response when something goes badly wrong. -- From the HIH Insurance collapse to Banking misconduct to Aboriginal Deaths in Custody, the Royal Commission is the "How" of serious investigation, the State acknowledging that something is rotten and demanding the truth. When something goes badly wrong, Australia convenes a Royal Commission—an inquiry with coercive powers to summon witnesses and documents. It is the "How" of serious investigation, the method by which scandals are unpacked and blame is assigned.','Plane_7_Result.md',593,'I am calling for ATSIC to be abolished. It is a failed, hypocritical and discriminatory organisation that has failed dismally the people it was meant to serve.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'It is a failed, hypocritical and discriminatory organisation that has failed dismally the people it was meant to serve.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(334,7,'Result','Effect.How.Where','The High Court',0.8,0.5,'FAIL','**(Effect.How.Where) The High Court (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Enough is enough. And we must -- and I stress ''must'' -- have a sunset clause on native title and land right claims, which already cover more than half the Australian continent. We must have a comprehensive audit on these land councils, Aboriginal corporations..." -Statements by Senators: Native Title, Senate Hansard (26 March 2024)[^tvfy]','The High Court: The High Court of Australia: the final court of appeal and the guardian of the Constitution. -- The High Court is the "Where" where the Constitution is defended, determining whether laws comply with the national compact. From *Mabo* (native title) to *Work Choices* (industrial relations), the High Court is the umpire enforcing the rules of the game. The High Court is the "Where" where the Constitution is defended. It judges whether laws comply with the national compact. The "How" of constitutional evaluation is the ruling from the bench.','Plane_7_Result.md',613,'Enough is enough. And we must',1,'- and I stress ''must'' -- have a sunset clause on native title and land right claims, which already cover more than half the Australian continent. We must have a comprehensive audit on these land councils, Aboriginal corporations..." -Statements by Senators: Native Title, Senate Hansard (26 March 2024)','tvfy','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/tvfy.txt','fabricated',0.1667,'- Against carbon pricing and net-zero policies.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(335,7,'Result','Effect.How.Why','The Media',-0.2,0.4,'HIT','**(Effect.How.Why) The Media (υ: \-0.2, ψ: \+0.4): HIT.** **Quote:** "It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Media: The Fourth Estate: the press as the informal check on government power. -- The media provides the framing through which the nation sees itself—headlines, talkback, and the nightly news filter reality, amplifying some judgments and silencing others. The Australian media—from the ABC to Murdoch''s News Corp—provides the framing through which the nation sees itself. The "How" of public evaluation is through headlines, talk-back radio, and the nightly news.','Plane_7_Result.md',633,'It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'It has got me into trouble on the odd occasion, but I am not going to stop saying what I think.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(336,7,'Result','Effect.How.How','The ABS',0.8,0.4,'FAIL','**(Effect.How.How) The ABS (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Statistics, by cooking the books, say that Australia''s unemployment is at 8.6 per cent... If we disregard that one hour''s work a week classifies a person as employed, then the figure is really between 1.5 million and 1.9 million unemployed." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The ABS: The Australian Bureau of Statistics: the nation''s official statistician. -- The ABS provides the baseline data—unemployment, GDP, inflation, population, the Census—that underpins all policy evaluation. The "How" of measurement is the official statistic, the agreed-upon baseline for argument. We judge by the stats. The ABS provides the baseline data—unemployment, GDP, inflation, population—that underpins all policy evaluation. The "How" of measurement is the official statistic.','Plane_7_Result.md',653,'Statistics, by cooking the books, say that Australia''s unemployment is at 8.6 per cent... If we disregard that one hour''s work a week classifies a person as employed, then the figure is really between 1.5 million and 1.9 million unemployed.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'If we disregard that one hour''s work a week classifies a person as employed, then the figure is really between 1.5 million and 1.9 million unemployed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(337,7,'Result','Effect.How.Cause','The Pub Test',0.4,-0.3,'HIT','**(Effect.How.Cause) The Pub Test (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "When I go shopping, people ask, ''Why can''t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?'' They''re right." -Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018[^senate18tax]','The Pub Test: Would it pass the pub test?—the imagined judgment of ordinary Australians drinking at the local. -- The "Pub Test" asks whether a policy or action would be seen as fair and reasonable by the common person—the anti-intellectual check on complexity, demanding that ideas be defensible in simple terms. We judge by the vibe. The informal judgment of ordinary Australians, imagined as a conversation at the local pub. The "Pub Test" asks whether a policy or action would be seen as fair and reasonable by the common person.','Plane_7_Result.md',673,'When I go shopping, people ask, ''Why can''t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?'' They''re right.',1,'Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'When I go shopping, people ask, ‘Why can’t the government help the farmers instead of these big companies?’ They’re right.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(338,7,'Result','Effect.How.Effect','The Treasury',0.6,0.5,'HIT','**(Effect.How.Effect) The Treasury (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "If immigration at the current levels is such a great idea, why have we gone steadily into debt so that every worker in Australia pays over $1300 a year to service our debt mountain?" -Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", senatorhanson.com.au (22 Aug 2018)[^senate18imm]','The Treasury: The Budget: the annual fiscal reckoning where the government justifies its priorities and the Treasurer delivers their speech. -- It is the formal evaluation of the nation''s finances—income, expenditure, surplus, or deficit. The Treasury is the accountant of the state, ensuring that promises are funded by real money. We judge by the numbers. The annual Budget is the formal evaluation of the nation''s finances, where the government presents its income and expenditure and justifies its priorities. The "How" of fiscal judgment is the Treasurer''s speech.','Plane_7_Result.md',693,'If immigration at the current levels is such a great idea, why have we gone steadily into debt so that every worker in Australia pays over $1300 a year to service our debt mountain?',1,'Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", senatorhanson.com.au (22 Aug 2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',1.0,'If immigration at the current levels is such a great idea, why have we gone steadily into debt so that every worker in Australia pays over $1300 a year to service our debt mountain?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(339,7,'Result','Effect.Cause.Who','The Next Generation',0.7,0.8,'FAIL','**(Effect.Cause.Who) The Next Generation (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.8): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I''m worried about the future generations and the debt we are going to leave them." -Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018[^senate18tax]','The Next Generation: Gen Z and the School Strike for Climate: ''You are stealing our future!'' -- Inspired by Greta Thunberg, Australian students staged mass walkouts from schools demanding climate action. The emerging generation defines itself by the crisis it inherits—they are the future voters who will deliver the verdict on our century, inheriting our debts (financial, ecological, social) and our unfinished projects. The emerging generation defines itself by the crisis it inherits. The Climate Strike movement placed young Australians at the forefront of global activism, demanding action from adults who have failed them.','Plane_7_Result.md',715,'I''m worried about the future generations and the debt we are going to leave them.',1,'Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'I’m worried about the future generations and the debt we are going to leave them.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(340,7,'Result','Effect.Cause.What','The Energy Transition',0.9,0.8,'FAIL','**(Effect.Cause.What) The Energy Transition (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.8): FAIL.** **Quote:** "We will never be able to do without coal and gas." -National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026[^npc26]','The Energy Transition: 100% Renewables by 2050 (or 2030, or 2040)—the target varies but the direction is clear. -- The shift from coal and gas to solar, wind, and storage is the defining economic transformation of the coming decades. Australia could become a "clean energy superpower" (exporting hydrogen, green metals) or fail the transition and become a stranded asset economy. The "What" of the future is written in kilowatts. The shift from coal and gas to solar and wind is the defining economic transformation of the coming decades. The "What" of the future will be clean energy or climate catastrophe.','Plane_7_Result.md',735,'We will never be able to do without coal and gas.',1,'National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'We will never be able to do without coal and gas.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(341,7,'Result','Effect.Cause.Where','Northern Australia',0.3,0.5,'HIT','**(Effect.Cause.Where) Northern Australia (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "What I''ve been pushing for is the Bradfield Scheme that comes from North Queensland, the Herbert, Tully, and the Burdekin Rivers, to actually direct it inland... Bring it from the Ord, water inland, Australia from the Ord Scheme as well, and bring water inland and flush out our river systems." -Sky News "Paul Murray Live" interview, 29 January 2019[^onenation_bradfield19]','Northern Australia: Developing the North: the recurring Australian ambition to populate and industrialize the tropical zone. -- Darwin, Cairns, the Pilbara remain underdeveloped despite decades of rhetoric. If southern cities become unlivable (heat, water stress), the north may finally be colonized. The geography is waiting to be rewritten. The tropical north (Darwin, Cairns, the Pilbara) remains underdeveloped despite decades of policy ambitions. The "Where" of the future may shift from the temperate south to the tropical north.','Plane_7_Result.md',755,'What I''ve been pushing for is the Bradfield Scheme that comes from North Queensland, the Herbert, Tully, and the Burdekin Rivers, to actually direct it inland... Bring it from the Ord, water inland, Australia from the Ord Scheme as well, and bring water inland and flush out our river systems.',1,'Sky News "Paul Murray Live" interview, 29 January 2019','onenation_bradfield19','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/onenation_bradfield19.txt','fabricated',0.2745,'PRIMARY URL: https://www.onenation.org.au/pauline-hanson-calls-for-construction-of-bradfield-and-ord-schemes-to-drought-proof-inland-australia/',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(342,7,'Result','Effect.Cause.Why','The Republic',0.6,0.4,'FAIL','**(Effect.Cause.Why) The Republic (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "It doesn''t matter whether you think Australia should be a republic or that Australia only belongs to Indigenous people, Australia is a constitutional monarchy that belongs to every Australian, Indigenous or not." -Senate Hansard, Censure Motion, 27 September 2022[^hansard22crown]','The Republic: Should Australia become a republic? -- The issue has never gone away. When Elizabeth II died (8 September 2022), the debate returned. The "Why" of continued monarchy is increasingly hard to articulate (tradition, stability); the "Why" of a republic is autonomy and identity. The question has been deferred, not denied. The 1999 referendum failed, but the question persists. When the Queen died (2022), the issue returned. The "Why" of continued monarchy is increasingly hard to articulate; the "Why" of a republic is autonomy and identity.','Plane_7_Result.md',775,'It doesn''t matter whether you think Australia should be a republic or that Australia only belongs to Indigenous people, Australia is a constitutional monarchy that belongs to every Australian, Indigenous or not.',1,'Senate Hansard, Censure Motion, 27 September 2022','hansard22crown','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/hansard22crown.txt','verified',1.0,'I remind them that it doesn''t matter whether you think Australia should be a republic or that Australia only belongs to Indigenous people, Australia is a constitutional monarchy that belongs to every Australian, Indigenous or not.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(343,7,'Result','Effect.Cause.How','Treaty \[First Nations Perspective\]',0.9,0.8,'FAIL','**(Effect.Cause.How) Treaty \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.8): FAIL.** **Quote:** "If we recognise prior indigenous ownership in the Constitution and then, one day, become a republic, the High Court could be forced to rule the Crown''s former sovereignty over Australia only belongs to indigenous people as native title holders rather than every Australian." -Senate speech opposing the Voice to Parliament, senatorhanson.com.au (2021)[^senate21voice]','Treaty [First Nations Perspective]: We seek a Makarrata Commission to supervise a process of agreement-making between governments and First Nations and truth-telling about our history. -- The Republican debate obsessively focuses on cutting ties with the British Monarchy to achieve "maturity." For First Nations people, the issue is not the Crown, but the lack of a **Treaty**—Australia is the only Commonwealth nation without one. Innovative sovereignty requires acknowledging that the land was occupied by sovereign nations who never surrendered their rights, only their lives. The path to Reconciliation laid out by the First Nations leaders includes a constitutionally enshrined Voice, a Treaty process, and a truth-telling commission.','Plane_7_Result.md',795,'If we recognise prior indigenous ownership in the Constitution and then, one day, become a republic, the High Court could be forced to rule the Crown''s former sovereignty over Australia only belongs to indigenous people as native title holders rather than every Australian.',1,'Senate speech opposing the Voice to Parliament, senatorhanson.com.au (2021)','senate21voice','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate21voice.txt','verified',1.0,'Finally, a note of warning: if we recognise prior indigenous ownership in the Constitution and then, one day, become a republic, the High Court could be forced to rule the Crown’s former sovereignty over Australia only belongs to indigenous people as native title holders rather than every Australian.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(344,7,'Result','Effect.Cause.Cause','Asia',0.5,0.3,'FAIL','**(Effect.Cause.Cause) Asia (υ: \+0.5, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I believe we are in danger of being swamped by Asians. Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin. They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996[^ms96]','Asia: We are part of the Asian region.—Geographic Fact, Geopolitical Destiny. -- Australia''s future is inextricably tied to China (largest trading partner), India (fastest-growing neighbor), and Indonesia (closest large nation). The gravity of Asia pulls us into its orbit; we cannot remain a European outpost in an Asian sea. The map is claiming us. Australia''s future is inextricably tied to the rise of China, India, and Indonesia. The "Cause" of the future is the gravity of Asia, pulling us into its orbit. We cannot remain a European outpost in an Asian sea.','Plane_7_Result.md',815,'I believe we are in danger of being swamped by Asians. Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin. They have their own culture and religion, form ghettos and do not assimilate.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard, 10 September 1996','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Between 1984 and 1995, 40 per cent of all migrants coming into this country were of Asian origin.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(345,7,'Result','Effect.Cause.Effect','The Good Life',0.7,0.5,'HIT','**(Effect.Cause.Effect) The Good Life (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \+0.5): HIT.** **Quote:** "The people are over it. They''re tired of every single one of you urinating their money up against a brick wall." -Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018[^senate18tax]','The Good Life: Australia consistently ranks in the top 10 on the Human Development Index, World Happiness Report, and Quality of Life indices. -- The "Effect" of the future is whether this can be maintained. Can someone born in 2050 enjoy the same fairness, safety, and prosperity as someone born in 1980? The goal is preservation of the Good Life for those who come after us. Australia consistently ranks among the top nations for quality of life—health, education, safety, environment. The "Effect" of the future is whether this can be maintained.','Plane_7_Result.md',835,'The people are over it. They''re tired of every single one of you urinating their money up against a brick wall.',1,'Senate speech, Corporate Tax Cuts and Government Failure, 22 August 2018','senate18tax','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18tax.txt','verified',1.0,'They’re tired of every single one of you urinating their money up against a brick wall.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(346,7,'Result','Effect.Effect.Who','The Fair Go',0.9,0.3,'FAIL','**(Effect.Effect.Who) The Fair Go (υ: \+0.9, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "The right to express cultural identity comes with the responsibility to accept Australia''s liberal democracy and to read, write and speak English." -Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", senatorhanson.com.au (22 Aug 2018)[^senate18imm]','The Fair Go: A Fair Go for all Australians.—The undefined but universally invoked principle at the heart of Australian identity. -- The Fair Go is the answer to "Who are we?"—everyone deserves a reasonable chance, no one should be exploited or left behind. It is vaguer than "Liberty," more practical than "Justice," but deeply felt. We are the people who believe in Fairness. The Fair Go is the answer to "Who are we?" It is the undefined but universally invoked principle that everyone deserves a reasonable chance. It is the closest Australia has to a founding creed—vaguer than "Liberty," more practical than "Justice," but deeply felt.','Plane_7_Result.md',857,'The right to express cultural identity comes with the responsibility to accept Australia''s liberal democracy and to read, write and speak English.',1,'Senate speech "Immigration Debate Cannot Be Silenced", senatorhanson.com.au (22 Aug 2018)','senate18imm','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate18imm.txt','verified',1.0,'Most Australians believe multiculturalism has been good for Australia, but the right to express cultural identity comes with the responsibility to accept Australia’s liberal democracy and to read, write and speak English.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(347,7,'Result','Effect.Effect.What','The Lifestyle',0.6,0.3,'FAIL','**(Effect.Effect.What) The Lifestyle (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.3): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Time is running out. We may have only 10 to 15 years left to turn things around." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','The Lifestyle: The best country in the world—if you''re middle-class, love beaches, and can tolerate the heat. -- The tangible result of the Australian experiment is a standard of living that is the envy of much of the world: beaches, weather, space, safety, healthcare. We have achieved comfort. The dream was achieved: the house, the car, the holiday, the pension. The tangible result of the Australian experiment is a standard of living that is the envy of the world. The beaches, the weather, the space, the safety, the healthcare—these are the "What" of the outcome. We have achieved comfort.','Plane_7_Result.md',877,'Time is running out. We may have only 10 to 15 years left to turn things around.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'We may have only 10 to 15 years left to turn things around.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(348,7,'Result','Effect.Effect.Where','Girt By Sea',0.4,-0.3,'HIT','**(Effect.Effect.Where) Girt By Sea (υ: \+0.4, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "If I can invite whom I want into my home, then I should have the right to have a say in who comes into my country." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Girt By Sea: Our land is girt by sea.—*Advance Australia Fair*, National Anthem. -- The nation is defined by its encirclement by water—the ocean is the moat that protected us from invasion and enabled our immigration policy. We are fundamentally an island continent, isolated by sea, looking out from the edge of the land. The nation is defined by its encirclement by water. The ocean is the moat that protected us from invasion and enabled our immigration policy. The "Where" of Australia is fundamentally defined by its island status.','Plane_7_Result.md',897,'If I can invite whom I want into my home, then I should have the right to have a say in who comes into my country.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Of course, I will be called racist but, if I can invite whom I want into my home, then I should have the right to have a say in who comes into my country.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(349,7,'Result','Effect.Effect.Why','The Second Chance',0.8,0.5,'FAIL','**(Effect.Effect.Why) The Second Chance (υ: \+0.8, ψ: \+0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Governments must give to all those who have hit life''s hurdles the chance to rebuild and have a future." -Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)[^ms96]','Dispossession [First Nations Perspective]: For some, this land was not a second chance but a first home. -- The "Second Chance" myth frames Australia as a place of redemption for convicts and migrants. This narrative erases the experience of Indigenous people, for whom colonization was not a fresh start but a catastrophic interruption.','Plane_7_Result.md',917,'Governments must give to all those who have hit life''s hurdles the chance to rebuild and have a future.',1,'Maiden Speech, House of Representatives, Hansard (1996)','ms96','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/ms96.txt','verified',1.0,'Governments must give to all those who have hit life''s hurdles the chance to rebuild and have a future.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(350,7,'Result','Effect.Effect.Why','Dispossession \[First Nations Perspective\]',-0.8,-0.7,'HIT','**(Effect.Effect.Why) Dispossession \[First Nations Perspective\] (υ: \-0.8, ψ: \-0.7): HIT.** **Quote:** "I do not believe we need a Voice. I believe all Australians, no matter what their background, should be treated the same." -Senate speech opposing the Voice to Parliament, senatorhanson.com.au (2021)[^senate21voice]','Dispossession [First Nations Perspective]: For some, this land was not a second chance but a first home. -- The "Second Chance" myth frames Australia as a place of redemption for convicts and migrants. This narrative erases the experience of Indigenous people, for whom colonization was not a fresh start but a catastrophic interruption.','Plane_7_Result.md',937,'I do not believe we need a Voice. I believe all Australians, no matter what their background, should be treated the same.',1,'Senate speech opposing the Voice to Parliament, senatorhanson.com.au (2021)','senate21voice','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/senate21voice.txt','verified',0.8636,'It’s no wonder the unaccountable aboriginal industry is campaigning for it, but some feedback from the consultation process suggests many are sceptical that recognition or a ‘voice to Parliament’ will do anything to make a practical difference in their lives.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(351,7,'Result','Effect.Effect.How','She''ll Be Right',0.3,-0.5,'FAIL','**(Effect.Effect.How) She''ll Be Right (υ: \+0.3, ψ: \-0.5): FAIL.** **Quote:** "Why are we not putting in as much money into this country? ... We need to look after our own, first and foremost." -Senate statement, Ministerial Statements: Australian Bushfires, 25 November 2019[^oa_bushfirevolunteers]','She''ll Be Right: She''ll be right, mate.—The relaxed optimism that assumes things will work out. -- The "How" of the Australian approach is casual confidence—steady effort beats frantic worry, extremes are unnecessary, there''s always tomorrow. "She''ll be right" is the psychological byproduct of success: things have worked out before, so they''ll work out again. We endure by refusing to worry. The "How" of the Australian approach is casual confidence—the assumption that things will work out, that extremes are unnecessary, that steady effort beats frantic worry. "She''ll be right, mate" is the method of the national soul.','Plane_7_Result.md',957,'Why are we not putting in as much money into this country? ... We need to look after our own, first and foremost.',1,'Senate statement, Ministerial Statements: Australian Bushfires, 25 November 2019','oa_bushfirevolunteers','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/oa_bushfirevolunteers.txt','verified',1.0,'If Di Natale is saying that it''s because of climate change, why are we not putting in as much money into this country?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(352,7,'Result','Effect.Effect.Cause','The Land',0.7,-0.3,'HIT','**(Effect.Effect.Cause) The Land (υ: \+0.7, ψ: \-0.3): HIT.** **Quote:** "We want more gas, more oil and more energy to drive our economy forward." -Australian Energy Producers conference address, Adelaide, 21 May 2026[^energy26]','The Land: Australia Felix—the Happy South Land.—Thomas Mitchell''s name for the rich pastures of western Victoria, 1836. -- The geology that gave us minerals, the climate that gave us beaches, the distance that gave us peace. We inherit the gift of the continent. We owe our existence to the accident of geography, the luck of the draw—the land gave us the raw materials; we just showed up and dug. The ultimate "Cause" of the Australian result is the Land itself. The geology that gave us minerals, the climate that gave us beaches, the distance that gave us peace. We inherit the gift of the continent.','Plane_7_Result.md',977,'We want more gas, more oil and more energy to drive our economy forward.',1,'Australian Energy Producers conference address, Adelaide, 21 May 2026','energy26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/energy26.txt','verified',1.0,'“We want more gas, more oil and more energy to drive our economy forward,” she said.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
INSERT INTO "nodes" VALUES(353,7,'Result','Effect.Effect.Effect','Australia',0.6,0.4,'FAIL','**(Effect.Effect.Effect) Australia (υ: \+0.6, ψ: \+0.4): FAIL.** **Quote:** "I love this country. I''m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first." -National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026[^npc26]','Australia: Australians all let us rejoice, for we are one and free.—*Advance Australia Fair*, National Anthem, lyrics updated 2021. -- The Effect of the Effect is the fact of our existence, the sum of all the vectors. We exist. We endure. We continue. The experiment is still running. The question is always: "What next?" The final result is the nation itself—the integrated, sovereign, prosperous, flawed, hopeful entity named "Australia." The Effect of the Effect is the fact of our existence, the sum of all the vectors.','Plane_7_Result.md',997,'I love this country. I''m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist. I will always put Australia and Australians first.',1,'National Press Club Address, 17 June 2026','npc26','/sessions/sharp-jolly-carson/mnt/Aus_Kanon/Audits/Hanson_Audit/Sources_Archive/npc26.txt','verified',1.0,'I’m a patriot, and an unashamed nationalist.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-09T18:43:40');
